resent action", "ex_ko": "온라인에서 물건을 살 때는 정확한 정보를 확인하는 것이 중요해요.", "ex_en": "When buying things online, it''s important to check accurate information."}, {"name": "~인 (that is N)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "noun-modifying form of 이다. 인기이다 → 인기인 제품 = \"a product that is popular\".", "ex_ko": "소셜미디어(SNS)에서 인기인 제품을 살 때는 더욱 조심해야 합니다.", "ex_en": "When buying products that are popular on social media, you need to be even more careful."}, {"name": "~아/어야 하다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "must, have to", "ex_ko": "소셜미디어(SNS)에서 인기인 제품을 살 때는 더욱 조심해야 합니다.", "ex_en": "When buying products that are popular on social media, you need to be even more careful."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mniwzglxp014' and md5(translation) = '649fc4da1a7bf7d2e0ff02995e7c8d92';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"sentences": [{"text": "지금 로봇이 대단하다고 생각하세요?", "idx": 0, "translation": "Do you think robots are amazing right now?", "vocab": [{"ko": "로봇", "en": "robot", "note": ""}, {"ko": "대단하다", "en": "to be amazing/impressive", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~다고 생각하다", "exp": "To think or believe that something is a certain way", "example_in_sentence": "로봇이 대단하다고 생각하세요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "6G(6세대 이동통신) 기술이 나오면 로봇이 훨씬 더 놀라워질 거예요.", "idx": 1, "translation": "When 6G (sixth-generation mobile communication) technology comes out, robots will become much more amazing.", "vocab": [{"ko": "기술", "en": "technology", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나오다", "en": "to come out/appear", "note": ""}, {"ko": "놀라워지다", "en": "to become amazing/surprising", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~(으)면", "exp": "Conditional: ''if/when'' something happens", "example_in_sentence": "기술이 나오면"}, {"pattern": "~어질 거예요", "exp": "Future change or state using ~어지다 and ~ㄹ 거예요", "example_in_sentence": "놀라워질 거예요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "6G는 핸드폰을 더 빠르게 만드는 것뿐만 아니라 로봇에게 새로운 능력을 줄 거예요.", "idx": 2, "translation": "6G will not only make phones faster but also give robots new abilities.", "vocab": [{"ko": "빠르다", "en": "to be fast", "note": ""}, {"ko": "능력", "en": "ability/capacity", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~을/를 뿐만 아니라", "exp": "Not only X but also Y", "example_in_sentence": "핸드폰을 더 빠르게 만드는 것뿐만 아니라"}, {"pattern": "~ㄹ 거예요", "exp": "Future tense polite: ''will/shall''", "example_in_sentence": "줄 거예요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "로봇들이 모든 것을 느끼고 항상 배울 수 있게 될 거예요.", "idx": 3, "translation": "Robots will be able to feel everything and always learn.", "vocab": [{"ko": "느끼다", "en": "to feel/sense", "note": ""}, {"ko": "배우다", "en": "to learn", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~을/를 수 있다", "exp": "To be able to; possibility", "example_in_sentence": "모든 것을 느끼고 항상 배울 수 있게"}, {"pattern": "~ㄹ 거예요", "exp": "Future tense polite", "example_in_sentence": "될 거예요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "앞으로 로봇들은 6G를 통해서 서로 정보를 나눌 수 있어요.", "idx": 4, "translation": "From now on, robots will be able to share information with each other through 6G.", "vocab": [{"ko": "앞으로", "en": "from now on/in the future", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정보", "en": "information", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나누다", "en": "to share/divide", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~을/를 통해서", "exp": "Through; by means of", "example_in_sentence": "6G를 통해서"}, {"pattern": "~을/를 수 있어요", "exp": "Can/able to do (present polite capability)", "example_in_sentence": "정보를 나눌 수 있어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "마치 똑똑한 로봇 팀처럼 함께 일할 수 있게 돼요.", "idx": 5, "translation": "They will be able to work together like a smart robot team.", "vocab": [{"ko": "마치", "en": "as if/just like", "note": ""}, {"ko": "똑똑하다", "en": "to be smart/clever", "note": ""}, {"ko": "팀", "en": "team", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~처럼", "exp": "Like; similar to", "example_in_sentence": "똑똑한 로봇 팀처럼"}, {"pattern": "~게 되다", "exp": "To come to (be able to); to end up doing", "example_in_sentence": "함께 일할 수 있게 돼요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "한국도 6G 기술 개발에 열심히 참여하고 있어요.", "idx": 6, "translation": "Korea is also actively participating in 6G technology development.", "vocab": [{"ko": "한국", "en": "Korea", "note": ""}, {"ko": "개발", "en": "development", "note": ""}, {"ko": "참여하다", "en": "to participate", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~고 있어요", "exp": "Progressive/continuous action in present", "example_in_sentence": "참여하고 있어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "우리 생활이 더 편리해질 것 같아요.", "idx": 7, "translation": "It seems our lives will become more convenient.", "vocab": [{"ko": "생활", "en": "life/livelihood", "note": ""}, {"ko": "편리하다", "en": "to be convenient", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~어질 것 같아요", "exp": "It seems like something will change/become a certain way", "example_in_sentence": "더 편리해질 것 같아요"}], "analysis": []}], "version": "p2"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "로봇", "en": "robot", "note": ""}, {"ko": "대단하다", "en": "to be amazing/impressive", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기술", "en": "technology", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나오다", "en": "to come out/appear", "note": ""}, {"ko": "놀라워지다", "en": "to become amazing/surprising", "note": ""}, {"ko": "빠르다", "en": "to be fast", "note": ""}, {"ko": "능력", "en": "ability/capacity", "note": ""}, {"ko": "느끼다", "en": "to feel/sense", "note": ""}, {"ko": "배우다", "en": "to learn", "note": ""}, {"ko": "앞으로", "en": "from now on/in the future", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정보", "en": "information", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나누다", "en": "to share/divide", "note": ""}, {"ko": "마치", "en": "as if/just like", "note": ""}, {"ko": "똑똑하다", "en": "to be smart/clever", "note": ""}, {"ko": "팀", "en": "team", "note": ""}, {"ko": "한국", "en": "Korea", "note": ""}, {"ko": "개발", "en": "development", "note": ""}, {"ko": "참여하다", "en": "to participate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "생활", "en": "life/livelihood", "note": ""}, {"ko": "편리하다", "en": "to be convenient", "note": ""}, {"word": "6G", "reading": "yukji", "meaning": "6th generation mobile communication"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": []}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mnix0c5b1d97' and md5(translation) = 'c6835c555af33f23333f5db2a82f9d5e';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"sentences": [{"text": "인도의 한 소년이 표범을 피해 도망치는 급박한 상황에서도 휴대폰을 챙겨 화제가 되고 있어요.", "idx": 0, "translation": "A boy in India is becoming a hot topic for grabbing his phone even in an urgent situation while fleeing from a leopard.", "vocab": [{"ko": "표범", "en": "leopard", "note": ""}, {"ko": "피하다", "en": "to avoid; to escape from", "note": "피하다 conjugated"}, {"ko": "도망치다", "en": "to run away; to flee", "note": ""}, {"ko": "급박하다", "en": "urgent; pressing", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ/은 상황에서도", "exp": "Even in a situation where X happens, the action still occurs.", "example_in_sentence": "표범을 피해 도망치는 급박한 상황에서도"}, {"pattern": "~어/아 화제가 되다", "exp": "To become a topic of discussion; to become trending.", "example_in_sentence": "화제가 되고 있어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 영상은 온라인에서 빠르게 퍼지며 많은 사람들의 관심을 받았습니다.", "idx": 1, "translation": "This video spread rapidly online and received attention from many people.", "vocab": [{"ko": "영상", "en": "video; footage", "note": ""}, {"ko": "퍼지다", "en": "to spread; to disperse", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~으며", "exp": "While doing X, simultaneously Y happens.", "example_in_sentence": "온라인에서 빠르게 퍼지며"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "표범이 나타나자 소년은 즉시 도망치기 시작했어요.", "idx": 2, "translation": "When the leopard appeared, the boy immediately started to run away.", "vocab": [{"ko": "나타나다", "en": "to appear; to show up", "note": ""}, {"ko": "즉시", "en": "immediately; at once", "note": "adverb"}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~자 (temporal clause)", "exp": "As soon as X happens, Y follows.", "example_in_sentence": "표범이 나타나자"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "하지만 놀랍게도 그는 도망치면서도 자신의 휴대폰을 잊지 않고 가져갔습니다.", "idx": 3, "translation": "But surprisingly, even while running away, he did not forget his phone and took it with him.", "vocab": [{"ko": "놀랍게도", "en": "surprisingly; astonishingly", "note": "adverb from 놀랍다"}, {"ko": "잊다", "en": "to forget", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~으면서도", "exp": "Even while doing X, the person does Y (contradictory actions).", "example_in_sentence": "도망치면서도"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "이 모습을 본 네티즌들은 \"위험한 상황에서도 휴대폰을 챙기다니\"라며 놀라워했어요.", "idx": 4, "translation": "Netizens who saw this scene were amazed, saying ''He grabbed his phone even in a dangerous situation.''", "vocab": [{"ko": "모습", "en": "appearance; sight; scene", "note": ""}, {"ko": "네티즌", "en": "netizen; internet user", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~며 놀라워하다", "exp": "To be amazed while expressing/saying something.", "example_in_sentence": "\"위험한 상황에서도 휴대폰을 챙기다니\"라며 놀라워했어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "일부는 \"요즘 젊은이들에게 휴대폰이 얼마나 중요한지 보여주는 사례\"라고 평가했습니다.", "idx": 5, "translation": "Some evaluated it as ''a case showing how important phones are to young people these days.''", "vocab": [{"ko": "일부", "en": "some; a part", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ다고 평가하다", "exp": "To evaluate/judge that X is the case.", "example_in_sentence": "\"요즘 젊은이들에게 휴대폰이 얼마나 중요한지 보여주는 사례\"라고 평가했습니다"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "전문가들은 위험한 상황에서는 생명이 가장 중요하다고 강조했어요.", "idx": 6, "translation": "Experts emphasized that in dangerous situations, life is most important.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert; specialist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "생명", "en": "life", "note": ""}, {"ko": "강조하다", "en": "to emphasize; to stress", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ다고 강조하다", "exp": "To stress/emphasize that X is true.", "example_in_sentence": "생명이 가장 중요하다고 강조했어요"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "하지만 이 소년의 침착한 모습은 많은 사람들에게 인상 깊게 남았습니다.", "idx": 7, "translation": "However, the composure shown by this boy left a deep impression on many people.", "vocab": [{"ko": "침착하다", "en": "calm; composed; cool-headed", "note": ""}, {"ko": "인상 깊다", "en": "impressive; striking", "note": ""}], "grammar": [{"pattern": "~ㄴ 모습", "exp": "The appearance/scene of X (descriptive modifier).", "example_in_sentence": "이 소년의 침착한 모습"}, {"pattern": "~에게 ~이/가 남다", "exp": "X leaves/remains with person Y.", "example_in_sentence": "많은 사람들에게 인상 깊게 남았습니다"}], "analysis": []}], "version": "p2"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "표범", "en": "leopard", "note": ""}, {"ko": "피하다", "en": "to avoid; to escape from", "note": "피하다 conjugated"}, {"ko": "도망치다", "en": "to run away; to flee", "note": ""}, {"ko": "급박하다", "en": "urgent; pressing", "note": ""}, {"ko": "영상", "en": "video; footage", "note": ""}, {"ko": "퍼지다", "en": "to spread; to disperse", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나타나다", "en": "to appear; to show up", "note": ""}, {"ko": "즉시", "en": "immediately; at once", "note": "adverb"}, {"ko": "놀랍게도", "en": "surprisingly; astonishingly", "note": "adverb from 놀랍다"}, {"ko": "잊다", "en": "to forget", "note": ""}, {"ko": "모습", "en": "appearance; sight; scene", "note": ""}, {"ko": "네티즌", "en": "netizen; internet user", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일부", "en": "some; a part", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert; specialist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "생명", "en": "life", "note": ""}, {"ko": "강조하다", "en": "to emphasize; to stress", "note": ""}, {"ko": "침착하다", "en": "calm; composed; cool-headed", "note": ""}, {"ko": "인상 깊다", "en": "impressive; striking", "note": ""}, {"word": "휴대폰", "reading": "hyudaepon", "meaning": "mobile phone/smartphone"}, {"word": "챙기다", "reading": "chaenggida", "meaning": "to take/bring along"}, {"word": "화제", "reading": "hwaje", "meaning": "topic/issue of interest"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": []}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mnwpdnl0n58y' and md5(translation) = 'e41f9a329f5bc27858225b8801324f78';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["A new wellness trend called ''Nothing Maxxing'' is gaining popularity among young people in the United States. It means intentionally doing nothing. This trend is spreading rapidly through social media. The key is taking complete rest away from a busy daily life. It''s about having time to just sit still without even looking at your smartphone. Experts analyze that this phenomenon is due to burnout among modern people. It''s a trend worth paying attention to even in competitive societies like Korea. Awareness is growing that intentional rest is necessary for mental health. However, rather than unconditionally doing nothing, the balance between appropriate rest and activity is important. Experts advise that it''s good to find a rest method that suits you.", "South Korea''s Teacher Shortage Crisis Serious, School Classes Disrupted", "What is an ''Anxiety Bag''? A Popular Trend", "\"Talking Pig\" SNS Star", "United States and China Resume Talks over Trade Issues", "From Salmon Sperm to Bird Droppings, Strange Beauty Trends"], "sentences": [{"text": "미국에서 ''낫싱 맥싱(Nothing Maxxing)''이라는 새로운 웰니스 트렌드가 젊은층 사이에서 인기를 얻고 있어요.", "translation": "A new wellness trend called ''Nothing Maxxing'' is gaining popularity among young people in the United States.", "vocab": [{"ko": "웰니스", "en": "wellness"}, {"ko": "트렌드", "en": "trend"}, {"ko": "젊은층", "en": "young generation/demographic"}, {"ko": "인기를 얻다", "en": "to gain popularity"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~이라는", "exp": "Quotative marker meaning ''called/named.'' Links a name or description to the noun it modifies.", "example_in_sentence": "''낫싱 맥싱(Nothing Maxxing)''이라는 새로운 웰니스 트렌드"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다 (be V-ing)", "exp": "ongoing action. 얻다 → 얻고 있어요 = \"is gaining\".", "example_in_sentence": "인기를 얻고 있어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ 사이에서 (among)", "exp": "among a group. 사이 (between, among) + 에서: 젊은층 사이에서 = \"among young people\".", "example_in_sentence": "젊은층 사이에서"}]}, {"text": "이는 의도적으로 아무것도 하지 않는 것을 뜻해요.", "translation": "This means intentionally doing nothing at all.", "vocab": [{"ko": "의도적으로", "en": "intentionally"}, {"ko": "아무것도", "en": "nothing at all; anything (in negative context)"}, {"ko": "뜻하다", "en": "to mean; to signify"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않다", "exp": "Negation marker. Creates negative form of action verbs. From 하다 → 하지 않다.", "example_in_sentence": "하지 않는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것을", "exp": "Nominalization. ~는 것 converts verb phrase into noun; 을 marks object. From 하다 → 하는 것.", "example_in_sentence": "하지 않는 것을"}]}, {"text": "이 트렌드는 소셜미디어를 통해 빠르게 퍼지고 있어요.", "translation": "This trend is spreading rapidly through social media.", "vocab": [{"ko": "소셜미디어", "en": "social media"}, {"ko": "퍼지다", "en": "to spread"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 통해 (through)", "exp": "the channel or means of something. 소셜미디어 → 소셜미디어를 통해 = \"through social media\".", "example_in_sentence": "소셜미디어를 통해"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있어요", "exp": "Progressive aspect marking ongoing action. From 퍼지다 → 퍼지고 있다.", "example_in_sentence": "퍼지고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "바쁜 일상에서 벗어나 완전한 휴식을 취하는 것이 핵심이에요.", "translation": "The key is to get away from busy daily life and take a complete rest.", "vocab": [{"ko": "일상", "en": "daily life; everyday routine"}, {"ko": "벗어나다", "en": "to escape; to get out of"}, {"ko": "완전하다", "en": "to be complete"}, {"ko": "휴식", "en": "rest; break"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 벗어나다", "exp": "Means ''to escape from/get out of.'' 에서 marks starting point; 벗어나다 is the action verb.", "example_in_sentence": "일상에서 벗어나"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것이 핵심이다 (the key is V-ing)", "exp": "~는 것 turns a verb into a noun. 취하다 → 취하는 것이 핵심이에요 = \"the key is taking (a rest)\".", "example_in_sentence": "취하는 것이 핵심이에요"}]}, {"text": "스마트폰도 보지 않고 그냥 가만히 있는 시간을 갖는 거예요.", "translation": "It is having time to just stay still without even looking at a smartphone.", "vocab": [{"ko": "스마트폰", "en": "smartphone"}, {"ko": "가만히", "en": "still; quietly; without moving"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~도 ~지 않다", "exp": "Emphatic negation: 도 (even, also) + ~지 않다 (not). Emphasizes what is excluded. From 보다 → 보지 않다.", "example_in_sentence": "스마트폰도 보지 않고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 시간을 갖다 (have time to V)", "exp": "~는 describes 시간 (time). 있다 → 가만히 있는 시간을 갖다 = \"to have time to just stay still\".", "example_in_sentence": "있는 시간을 갖는"}]}, {"text": "전문가들은 이런 현상이 현대인의 번아웃 때문이라고 분석해요.", "translation": "Experts analyze that this phenomenon is due to burnout of modern people.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert; specialist"}, {"ko": "현상", "en": "phenomenon"}, {"ko": "현대인", "en": "modern person; contemporary person"}, {"ko": "번아웃", "en": "burnout"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~때문이다", "exp": "Causal marker meaning ''because of; due to.'' 때문 (reason) + 이다. Indicates the cause or reason.", "example_in_sentence": "번아웃 때문이라고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~라고 분석하다", "exp": "Reported speech marker. 라고 + verb of communication/cognition (분석하다). From 이다 → 이라고.", "example_in_sentence": "때문이라고 분석해요"}]}, {"text": "특히 한국처럼 경쟁이 치열한 사회에서도 주목받을 만한 트렌드예요.", "translation": "It is a trend worth paying attention to, even in a highly competitive society like Korea.", "vocab": [{"ko": "경쟁", "en": "competition"}, {"ko": "치열하다", "en": "to be fierce; to be intense"}, {"ko": "사회", "en": "society"}, {"ko": "주목받다", "en": "to receive attention; to be noticed"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~처럼", "exp": "Comparison marker meaning ''like; as; similar to.'' Attached to noun. Indicates similarity or example.", "example_in_sentence": "한국처럼"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서도 (even in)", "exp": "에서 (in) + 도 (even). 사회 → 사회에서도 = \"even in a society\".", "example_in_sentence": "사회에서도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 만하다", "exp": "Expression meaning ''worthy of; worth.'' ~(으)ㄹ (future/potential) + 만하다 (sufficient/worthy). From 받다 → 받을.", "example_in_sentence": "받을 만한"}]}, {"text": "정신 건강을 위해 의도적인 휴식이 필요하다는 인식이 커지고 있어요.", "translation": "Awareness that intentional rest is necessary for mental health is growing.", "vocab": [{"ko": "정신 건강", "en": "mental health"}, {"ko": "의도적", "en": "intentional; deliberate"}, {"ko": "인식", "en": "awareness; recognition"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 위해", "exp": "Purpose/beneficiary marker meaning ''for the sake of; for.'' Attached to object noun with 을/를.", "example_in_sentence": "정신 건강을 위해"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다는 + N (the idea that)", "exp": "links a statement to a noun. 필요하다 → 필요하다는 인식 = \"the awareness that (it) is necessary\".", "example_in_sentence": "필요하다는 인식"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있어요", "exp": "Progressive aspect. From 커지다 → 커지고 있다. Shows ongoing growth/change.", "example_in_sentence": "커지고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 무조건 아무것도 안 하는 것보다는 적절한 휴식과 활동의 균형이 중요해요.", "translation": "However, balance between appropriate rest and activity is more important than doing absolutely nothing.", "vocab": [{"ko": "무조건", "en": "unconditionally; absolutely; no matter what"}, {"ko": "적절하다", "en": "to be appropriate; suitable"}, {"ko": "균형", "en": "balance"}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것보다(는) (rather than V-ing)", "exp": "comparison. 하다 → 하는 것보다는 = \"rather than doing\".", "example_in_sentence": "하는 것보다는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~과/와 (and)", "exp": "joins two nouns. 휴식과 활동의 균형 = \"a balance of rest and activity\".", "example_in_sentence": "휴식과 활동"}]}, {"text": "전문가들은 자신에게 맞는 휴식 방법을 찾는 것이 좋다고 조언해요.", "translation": "Experts advise that it is good to find a way of resting that suits you.", "vocab": [{"ko": "맞다", "en": "to suit; to fit; to match"}, {"ko": "방법", "en": "method; way"}, {"ko": "찾다", "en": "to find; to look for"}, {"ko": "조언하다", "en": "to advise; to counsel"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (verb modi