ech marker. 라고 + verb of communication/cognition (분석하다). From 이다 → 이라고.", "ex_ko": "전문가들은 이런 현상이 현대인의 번아웃 때문이라고 분석해요.", "ex_en": "Experts analyze that this phenomenon is due to burnout of modern people."}, {"name": "~처럼", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Comparison marker meaning ''like; as; similar to.'' Attached to noun. Indicates similarity or example.", "ex_ko": "특히 한국처럼 경쟁이 치열한 사회에서도 주목받을 만한 트렌드예요.", "ex_en": "It is a trend worth paying attention to, even in a highly competitive society like Korea."}, {"name": "~에서도 (even in)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "에서 (in) + 도 (even). 사회 → 사회에서도 = \"even in a society\".", "ex_ko": "특히 한국처럼 경쟁이 치열한 사회에서도 주목받을 만한 트렌드예요.", "ex_en": "It is a trend worth paying attention to, even in a highly competitive society like Korea."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moa04nmuwb0v' and md5(translation) = 'ef06be4397100358a0185d7db1279275';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"sentences": [{"text": "스포츠에서 가장 중요한 것은 무엇일까요?", "idx": 0, "translation": "What is the most important thing in sports?", "vocab": [{"ko": "스포츠", "en": "sports", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가장", "en": "most", "note": "superlative marker"}, {"ko": "중요하다", "en": "to be important", "note": ""}, {"ko": "것", "en": "thing", "note": "nominalizer"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서 (location/source)", "exp": "at/in (location of action) or from (source)", "example_in_sentence": "스포츠에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은 (past verb / present adj modifier)", "exp": "verb past OR adjective present modifying a noun", "example_in_sentence": "중요한"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic marker)", "exp": "topic particle", "example_in_sentence": "것은"}]}, {"text": "많은 사람들이 팀워크(teamwork)라고 말해요.", "idx": 1, "translation": "Many people say it''s teamwork.", "vocab": [{"ko": "많다", "en": "to be many/much", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person", "note": ""}, {"ko": "팀워크", "en": "teamwork", "note": ""}, {"ko": "말하다", "en": "to say", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은 (past verb / present adj modifier)", "exp": "verb past OR adjective present modifying a noun", "example_in_sentence": "많은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "exp": "subject particle", "example_in_sentence": "사람들이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(이)라고 말하다 (say that it is)", "exp": "quotes what people say. 팀워크 → 팀워크라고 말해요 = \"say (it is) teamwork\".", "example_in_sentence": "팀워크(teamwork)라고 말해요"}]}, {"text": "혼자서는 할 수 없는 일도 함께하면 가능해져요.", "idx": 2, "translation": "Things that cannot be done alone become possible when done together.", "vocab": [{"ko": "혼자", "en": "alone", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일", "en": "work, matter", "note": ""}, {"ko": "함께", "en": "together", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가능하다", "en": "to be possible", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다/없다 (ability/possibility)", "exp": "ability or possibility", "example_in_sentence": "할 수 없는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 (topic / contrast)", "exp": "contrast. 혼자서 → 혼자서는 = \"(when) alone\", in contrast to together.", "example_in_sentence": "혼자서는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~도 (also)", "exp": "inclusive particle", "example_in_sentence": "일도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면 (if/when)", "exp": "conditional", "example_in_sentence": "함께하면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어지다 (become)", "exp": "change of state. 가능하다 → 가능해지다 → 가능해져요 = \"becomes possible\".", "example_in_sentence": "가능해져요"}]}, {"text": "성공하는 팀들을 보면 공통점이 있어요.", "idx": 3, "translation": "If you look at successful teams, they have something in common.", "vocab": [{"ko": "성공하다", "en": "to succeed", "note": ""}, {"ko": "팀", "en": "team", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보다", "en": "to see, look", "note": ""}, {"ko": "공통점", "en": "common point", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present verb modifier)", "exp": "verb modifying a noun (present)", "example_in_sentence": "성공하는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "direct object particle", "example_in_sentence": "팀들을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면 (if/when)", "exp": "conditional", "example_in_sentence": "보면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 (subject marker)", "exp": "subject particle", "example_in_sentence": "공통점이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어/여요 (present polite)", "exp": "present polite informal ending", "example_in_sentence": "있어요"}]}, {"text": "서로를 믿고 도와주는 마음이 강해요.", "idx": 4, "translation": "Their spirit of trusting and helping each other is strong.", "vocab": [{"ko": "서로", "en": "each other", "note": ""}, {"ko": "믿다", "en": "to believe, trust", "note": ""}, {"ko": "돕다", "en": "to help", "note": "ㅂ-irregular verb"}, {"ko": "마음", "en": "heart, mind", "note": ""}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object marker)", "exp": "direct object particle", "example_in_sentence": "서로를"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "