 "ex_ko": "혼자서는 할 수 없는 일도 함께하면 가능해져요.", "ex_en": "Things that cannot be done alone become possible when done together."}, {"name": "~도 (also)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "inclusive particle", "ex_ko": "혼자서는 할 수 없는 일도 함께하면 가능해져요.", "ex_en": "Things that cannot be done alone become possible when done together."}, {"name": "~(으)면 (if/when)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "conditional", "ex_ko": "혼자서는 할 수 없는 일도 함께하면 가능해져요.", "ex_en": "Things that cannot be done alone become possible when done together."}, {"name": "~아/어지다 (become)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "change of state. 가능하다 → 가능해지다 → 가능해져요 = \"becomes possible\".", "ex_ko": "혼자서는 할 수 없는 일도 함께하면 가능해져요.", "ex_en": "Things that cannot be done alone become possible when done together."}, {"name": "~는 (present verb modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "verb modifying a noun (present)", "ex_ko": "성공하는 팀들을 보면 공통점이 있어요.", "ex_en": "If you look at successful teams, they have something in common."}, {"name": "~을/를 (object marker)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "direct object particle", "ex_ko": "성공하는 팀들을 보면 공통점이 있어요.", "ex_en": "If you look at successful teams, they have something in common."}, {"name": "~아/어/여요 (present polite)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "present polite informal ending", "ex_ko": "성공하는 팀들을 보면 공통점이 있어요.", "ex_en": "If you look at successful teams, they have something in common."}, {"name": "~아/어 주다 (do for)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "do as a favor for someone", "ex_ko": "서로를 믿고 도와주는 마음이 강해요.", "ex_en": "Their spirit of trusting and helping each other is strong."}, {"name": "ㅂ 불규칙 (ㅂ → 우/오)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "ㅂ-irregular. 돕다 → 도와 (ㅂ becomes 오 before 아) → 도와주는.", "ex_ko": "서로를 믿고 도와주는 마음이 강해요.", "ex_en": "Their spirit of trusting and helping each other is strong."}, {"name": "~지 않다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "negation", "ex_ko": "어려운 상황에서도 포기하지 않고 함께 노력해요.", "ex_en": "Even in difficult situations, they don''t give up and make efforts together."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'moeg39286sbz' and md5(translation) = '17fe34c449c9ac7d77dfff7542e3426e';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Turkey declared war on Germany and Japan in February 1945. This was a time when it became clear that Germany would lose in World War II.", "Turkey''s declaration of war was very special. It began with \"Friends, during the last few years of human history, certain people have appeared.\" It added, \"They decorated their flags with absurd things like superior races and living space.\"", "This was Turkey''s declaration to stand on the side of the Allied Powers after the outcome of the war was decided. Many neutral countries at that time made similar choices.", "This decision by Turkey was a strategy to secure its position in international society after the war. Although it barely participated in actual combat, it officially became a victorious nation."], "sentences": [{"text": "터키는 1945년 2월에 독일과 일본에 선전포고를 했어요.", "translation": "Turkey declared war on Germany and Japan in February 1945.", "vocab": [{"ko": "선전포고", "en": "declaration of war"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~과/와", "exp": "Coordinating particle linking two nouns (독일 ''Germany'' and 일본 ''Japan''). Shows parallel listing of objects.", "example_in_sentence": "독일과 일본에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에", "exp": "Locative particle indicating target/direction of action. Marks the recipients of the declaration.", "example_in_sentence": "일본에 선전포고를"}]}, {"text": "이때는 2차 세계대전에서 독일이 질 것이 분명해진 시기였어요.", "translation": "This was a time when it had become clear that Germany would lose in World War II.", "vocab": [{"ko": "세계대전", "en": "world war"}, {"ko": "분명하다", "en": "to be clear; evident"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 것 (that ~ will)", "exp": "future-tense noun clause. 지다 (to lose) → 질 것 = \"that (Germany) would lose\".", "example_in_sentence": "질 것이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어지다 (become)", "exp": "change of state, used here as a past modifier. 분명하다 → 분명해지다 → 분명해진 시기 = \"a time when it had become clear\".", "example_in_sentence": "분명해진 시기"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~였어요", "exp": "Past tense of 이다 (copula). Links subject 이때 to predicate 시기 in past.", "example_in_sentence": "시기였어요"}]}, {"text": "터키의 선전포고문은 매우 특별했어요.", "translation": "Turkey''s declaration of war was very special.", "vocab": [{"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special; exceptional"}], "analysis": []}, {"text": "\"친구들, 인류 역사의 마지막 몇 년 동안 어떤 사람들이 나타났습니다\"라고 시작했어요.", "translation": "It began by saying, \"Friends, in the last few years of human history, certain people appeared.\"", "vocab": [{"ko": "인류", "en": "mankind; humanity"}, {"ko": "나타나다", "en": "to appear; emerge"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ 동안 (during, for)", "exp": "duration. 몇 년 → 몇 년 동안 = \"for a few years\".", "example_in_sentence": "몇 년 동안"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~라고", "exp": "Quotative particle introducing reported/quoted speech. Marks the content of direct quotation.", "example_in_sentence": "습니다\"라고"}]}, {"text": "\"그들은 우월한 민족과 생존 공간 같은 말도 안 되는 것들로 자신들의 깃발을 장식했습니다\"라고 덧붙였어요.", "translation": "It added, \"They decorated their flags with absurd ideas like a superior race and living space.\"", "vocab": [{"ko": "우월하다", "en": "to be superior"}, {"ko": "생존", "en": "survival; existence"}, {"ko": "장식하다", "en": "to decorate; adorn"}, {"ko": "덧붙이다", "en": "to add (to); append"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "present-tense form of an adjective before a noun. 우월하다 → 우월한 민족 = \"a superior race\".", "example_in_sentence": "우월한 민족"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~ 같은 (such as, like)", "exp": "N 같은 + noun = \"noun(s) such as N\". 생존 공간 같은 말도 안 되는 것들 = \"absurd things such as living space\".", "example_in_sentence": "생존 공간 같은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~로", "exp": "Instrumental particle marking means/material. 것들로 장식했다 = decorated with things.", "example_in_sentence": "것들로 자신들의"}]}, {"text": "이는 터키가 전쟁의 승부가 결정된 후에 연합국(Allied Powers) 편에 서겠다고 선언한 것이에요.", "translation": "This means Turkey declared it would side with the Allied Powers after the outcome of the war had already been decided.", "vocab": [{"ko": "승부", "en": "outcome; decision; match"}, {"ko": "결정되다", "en": "to be decided; determined"}, {"ko": "연합국", "en": "allied powers; allies"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 후에 (after)", "exp": "after an action is finished. 결정되다 → 결정된 후에 = \"after (it) was decided\".", "example_in_sentence": "결정된 후에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~겠다고", "exp": "Prospective intention marker + quotative. 서다(to stand) → 서겠다(will/shall stand) → 서겠다고 = ''will stand'', quoted speech.", "example_in_sentence": "편에 서겠다고"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~ 편에 서다", "exp": "Expression meaning ''to take a side; to stand with''. 연합국 편에 서다 = to take the side of the Allies.", "example_in_sentence": "연합국(Allied Powers) 편에 서겠다고"}]}, {"text": "당시 많은 중립국들이 비슷한 선택을 했어요.", "translation": "Many neutral nations made similar choices at that time.", "vocab": [{"ko": "당시", "en": "at that time; then"}, {"ko": "중립국", "en": "neutral country"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "present-tense form of an adjective before a noun. 비슷하다 → 비슷한 선택 = \"a similar choice\".", "example_in_sentence": "비슷한 선택"}]}, {"text": "터키의 이런 결정은 전쟁 후 국제 사회에서 자신의 위치를 확보하려는 전략이었어요.", "translation": "This decision by Turkey was a strategy to secure its position in the international community after the war.", "vocab": [{"ko": "위치", "en": "position; location"}, {"ko": "확보하다", "en": "to secure; ensure; obtain"}, {"ko": "전략", "en": "strategy; tactic"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)려는 (intended to)", "exp": "intention, used before a noun. 확보하다 → 확보하려는 전략 = \"a strategy intended to secure\".", "example_in_sentence": "확보하려는 전략"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서", "exp": "Locative particle marking location/domain of action. 국제 사회에서 = in international society.", "example_in_sentence": "국제 사회에서 자신의"}]}, {"text": "실제 전투에는 거의 참여하지 않았지만 공식적으로는 승전국이 되었어요.", "translation": "Although it hardly participated in actual combat, it officially became a victor nation.", "vocab": [{"ko": "실제", "en": "actual; real"}, {"ko": "참여하다", "en": "to participate; take part"}, {"ko": "승전국", "en": "victor nation; winning nation"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않다", "exp": "Negation form. 참여하다 → 참여하지 않다 = did not participate.", "example_in_sentence": "참여하지 않았지만"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지만", "exp": "Connective ending expressing contrast/concession. Joins two clauses with opposite meanings.", "example_in_sentence": "않았지만 공식적으로는"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "선전포고", "en": "declaration of war", "note": ""}, {"ko": "세계대전", "en": "world war", "note": ""}, {"ko": "분명하다", "en": "to be clear; evident", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special; exceptional", "note": ""}, {"ko": "인류", "en": "mankind; humanity", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나타나다", "en": "to appear; emerge", "note": ""}, {"ko": "우월하다", "en": "to be superior", "note": ""}, {"ko": "생존", "en": "survival; existence", "note": ""}, {"ko": "장식하다", "en": "to decorate; adorn", "note": ""}, {"ko": "덧붙이다", "en": "to add (to); append", "note": ""}, {"ko": "승부", "en": "outcome; decision; match", "note": ""}, {"ko": "결정되다", "en": "to be decided; determined", "note": ""}, {"ko": "연합국", "en": "allied powers; allies", "note": ""}, {"ko": "당시", "en": "at that time; then", "note": ""}, {"ko": "중립국", "en": "neutral country", "note": ""}, {"ko": "위치", "en": "position; location", "note": ""}, {"ko": "확보하다", "en": "to secure; ensure; obtain", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전략", "en": "strategy; tactic", "note": ""}, {"ko": "실제", "en": "actual; real", "note": ""}, {"ko": "참여하다", "en": "to participate; take part", "note": ""}, {"ko": "승전국", "en": "victor nation; winning nation", "note": ""}, {"word": "생존 공간", "reading": "saengjae gonggian", "meaning": "living space", "context": "우월한 민족과 생존 공간 같은 말도 안 되는 것들로"}, {"word": "깃발", "reading": "gitbal", "meaning": "flag", "context": "자신들의 깃발을 장식했습니다"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~과/와", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Coordinating particle linking two nouns (독일 ''Germany'' and 일본 ''Japan''). Shows parallel listing of objects.", "ex_ko": "터키는 1945년 2월에 독일과 일본에 선전포고를 했어요.", "ex_en": "Turkey declared war on Germany and Japan in February 1945."}, {"name": "~에서", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Locative particle indicating target/direction of action. Marks the recipients of the declaration.", "ex_ko": "터키는 1945년 2월에 독일과 일본에 선전포고를 했어요.", "ex_en": "Turkey declared war on Germany and Japan in February 1945."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 것 (that ~ will)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "future-tense noun clause. 지다 (to lose) → 질 것 = \"that (Germany) would lose\".", "ex_ko": "이때는 2차 세계대전에서 독일이 질 것이 분명해진 시기였어요.", "ex_en": "This was a time when it had become clear that Germany would lose in World War II."}, {"name": "~아/어지다 (become)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "change of state, used here as a past modifier. 분명하다 → 분명해지다 → 분명해진 시기 = \"a time when it had become clear\".", "ex_ko": "이때는 2차 세계대전에서 독일이 질 것이 분명해진 시기였어요.", "ex_en": "This was a time when it had become clear that Germany would lose in World War II."}, {"name": "~였어요", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past tense of 이다 (copula). Links subject 이때 to predicate 시기 in past.", "ex_ko": "이때는 2차 세계대전에서 독일이 질 것이 분명해진 시기였어요.", "ex_en": "This was a time when it had become clear that Germany would lose in World War II."}, {"name": "~ 동안 (during, for)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "duration. 몇 년 → 몇 년 동안 = \"for a few years\".", "ex_ko": "\"친구들, 인류 역사의 마지막 몇 년 동안 어떤 사람들이 나타났습니다\"라고 시작했어요.", "ex_en": "It began by saying, \"Friends, in the last few years of human history, certain people appeared.\""}, {"name": "~라고", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Quotative particle introducing reported/quoted speech. Marks the content of direct quotation.", "ex_ko": "\"친구들, 인류 역사의 마지막 몇 년 동안 어떤 사람들이 나타났습니다\"라고 시작했어요.", "ex_en": "It began by saying, \"Friends, in the last few years of human history, certain people appeared.\""}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "present-tense form of an adjective before a noun. 비슷하다 → 비슷한 선택 = \"a similar choice\".", "ex_ko": "\"그들은 우월한 민족과 생존 공간 같은 말도 안 되는 것들로 자신들의 깃발을 장식했습니다\"라고 덧붙였어요.", "ex_en": "It added, \"They decorated their flags with absurd ideas like a superior race and living space.\""}, {"name": "~로", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Instrumental particle marking means/material. 것들로 장식했다 = decorated with things.", "ex_ko": "\"그들은 우월한 민족과 생존 공간 같은 말도 안 되는 것들로 자신들의 깃발을 장식했습니다\"라고 덧붙였어요.", "ex_en": "It added, \"They decorated their flags with absurd ideas like a superior race and living space.\""}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ 후에 (after)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "after an action is finished. 결정되다 → 결정된 후에 = \"after (it) was decided\".", "ex_ko": "이는 터키가 전쟁의 승부가 결정된 후에 연합국(Allied Powers) 편에 서겠다고 선언한 것이에요.", "ex_en": "This means Turkey declared it would side with the Allied Powers after the outcome of the war had already been decided."}, {"name": "~겠다고", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Prospective intention marker + quotative. 서다(to stand) → 서겠다(will/shall stand) → 서겠다고 = ''will stand'', quoted speech.", "ex_ko": "이는 터키가 전쟁의 승부가 결정된 후에 연합국(Allied Powers) 편에 서겠다고 선언한 것이에요.", "ex_en": "This means Turkey declared it would side with the Allied Powers after the outcome of the war had already been decided."}, {"name": "~(으)려는 (intended to)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "intention, used before a noun. 확보하다 → 확보하려는 전략 = \"a strategy intended to secure\".", "ex_ko": "터키의 이런 결정은 전쟁 후 국제 사회에서 자신의 위치를 확보하려는 전략이었어요.", "ex_en": "This decision by Turkey was a strategy to secure its position in the international community after the war."}, {"name": "~지 않다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Negation form. 참여하다 → 참여하지 않다 = did not participate.", "ex_ko": "실제 전투에는 거의 참여하지 않았지만 공식적으로는 승전국이 되었어요.", "ex_en": "Although it hardly participated in actual combat, it officially became a victor nation."}, {"name": "~지만", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Connective ending expressing contrast/concession. Joins two clauses with opposite meanings.", "ex_ko": "실제 전투에는 거의 참여하지 않았지만 공식적으로는 승전국이 되었어요.", "ex_en": "Although it hardly participated in actual combat, it officially became a victor nation."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mofayfaq6xhp' and md5(translation) = 'ab1136b440f00cd114b4f5b737256617';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["A special fact has been discovered in the United States. There are more households that keep pets than households with children.", "These days, American people are getting married later or having fewer children. However, they continue to keep animals like dogs and cats.", "Korea is in a similar situation. The birth rate is decreasing. Instead, the number of people who think of pets as family members is increasing.", "This change seems like it will have a big impact on society. Pet-related businesses will also grow larger."], "sentences": [{"text": "미국에서 특별한 사실이 발견되었어요.", "translation": "A special fact has been discovered in the United States.", "vocab": [{"ko": "특별하다", "en": "special; particular"}, {"ko": "사실", "en": "fact"}, {"ko": "발견되다", "en": "to be discovered"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past)", "exp": "past polite. 발견되다 → 발견되었어요 = \"was discovered\".", "example_in_sentence": "발견되었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이 (subject particle)", "exp": "Marks the subject of the sentence; used after noun ending in consonant.", "example_in_sentence": "사실이"}]}, {"text": "아이가 있는 가정보다 애완동물을 키우는 가정이 더 많다고 해요.", "translation": "It is said that there are more households raising pets than households with children.", "vocab": [{"ko": "아이", "en": "child"}, {"ko": "가정", "en": "household; family"}, {"ko": "애완동물", "en": "pet"}, {"ko": "키우다", "en": "to raise; to keep (an animal)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (verb modifier)", "exp": "present-tense modifier before a noun. 키우다 → 키우는 가정 = \"households that raise (pets)\".", "example_in_sentence": "키우는 가정"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~보다 (comparison particle)", "exp": "Marks the standard of comparison; means ''than'' or ''more than''.", "example_in_sentence": "가정보다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다고 하다", "exp": "Reported speech pattern. Converts direct statement to indirect report; 많다 + 고 + 하다 = ''it is said that''.", "example_in_sentence": "많다고 해요"}]}, {"text": "요즘 미국 사람들은 결혼을 늦게 하거나 아이를 적게 낳아요.", "translation": "These days, Americans marry late or have few children.", "vocab": [{"ko": "요즘", "en": "these days; nowadays"}, {"ko": "결혼", "en": "marriage"}, {"ko": "늦다", "en": "to be late"}, {"ko": "낳다", "en": "to give birth; to have (a child)"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~거나 (alternative connective)", "exp": "Connects two alternative clauses; 하 + 거나 = ''or'' (one option or another).", "example_in_sentence": "하거나"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요", "exp": "Present tense polite ending. 낳 + 아 + 요 = have (present habitual).", "example_in_sentence": "낳아요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 강아지나 고양이 같은 동물은 계속 키우고 있어요.", "translation": "However, they continue to raise animals like dogs and cats.", "vocab": [{"ko": "하지만", "en": "however; but"}, {"ko": "강아지", "en": "dog"}, {"ko": "고양이", "en": "cat"}, {"ko": "계속", "en": "continuously; continually"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~나 (alternative particle with nouns)", "exp": "Joins items as alternatives; 강아지 + 나 = ''dogs or/and [such things]''.", "example_in_sentence": "강아지나"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~같은 (similarity marker)", "exp": "Means ''like; such as''; attaches to noun to modify following noun.", "example_in_sentence": "같은 동물은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다 (be V-ing)", "exp": "ongoing action. 키우다 → 키우고 있어요 = \"are raising\".", "example_in_sentence": "키우고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "한국도 비슷한 상황이에요.", "translation": "Korea is in a similar situation.", "vocab": [{"ko": "비슷하다", "en": "similar; alike"}, {"ko": "상황", "en": "situation; circumstance"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "이다 (copula)", "exp": "Links subject to predicate noun. 상황 + 이 + 어요 = ''is a situation''.", "example_in_sentence": "상황이에요"}]}, {"text": "출산율이 낮아지고 있어요.", "translation": "The birth rate is decreasing.", "vocab": [{"ko": "출산율", "en": "birth rate"}, {"ko": "낮아지다", "en": "to become low; to decrease"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어지다 (change of state)", "exp": "becoming. 낮다 → 낮아지다 = \"to become low\".", "example_in_sentence": "낮아지고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect showing ongoing action or state. Indicates the process is currently happening.", "example_in_sentence": "낮아지고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "대신 반려동물(pet)을 가족처럼 생각하는 사람들이 늘어나고 있어요.", "translation": "Instead, people who think of pets as family are increasing.", "vocab": [{"ko": "대신", "en": "instead; in place of"}, {"ko": "반려동물", "en": "companion animal; pet"}, {"ko": "가족", "en": "family"}, {"ko": "늘어나다", "en": "to increase; to grow"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~처럼 (similarity/manner)", "exp": "Means ''like; as if''; indicates manner or comparison. 가족 + 처럼 = ''like family''.", "example_in_sentence": "가족처럼"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (verb modifier)", "exp": "present-tense modifier before a noun. 생각하다 → 생각하는 사람들 = \"people who think\".", "example_in_sentence": "생각하는 사람들이"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다 (be V-ing)", "exp": "ongoing action. 늘어나다 → 늘어나고 있어요 = \"are increasing\".", "example_in_sentence": "늘어나고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "이런 변화는 사회에 큰 영향을 줄 것 같아요.", "translation": "Changes like this seem to have a big impact on society.", "vocab": [{"ko": "변화", "en": "change"}, {"ko": "사회", "en": "society"}, {"ko": "영향", "en": "influence; impact"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "영향을 주다 (have an impact)", "exp": "to influence or affect something. 사회에 큰 영향을 주다 = \"to have a big impact on society\".", "example_in_sentence": "영향을 줄"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 것 같다 (I think it will)", "exp": "a guess about the future. 주다 → 줄 것 같아요 = \"it seems (it) will give\".", "example_in_sentence": "줄 것 같아요"}]}, {"text": "애완동물 관련 사업도 더 커질 거예요.", "translation": "Pet-related businesses will also grow larger.", "vocab": [{"ko": "관련", "en": "relation; connection"}, {"ko": "사업", "en": "business"}, {"ko": "커지다", "en": "to grow bigger"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 거예요 (will)", "exp": "future. 커지다 (to grow bigger) → 커질 거예요 = \"will grow bigger\".", "example_in_sentence": "커질 거예요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~도 (inclusive particle, ''also'')", "exp": "Adds the current item to a series; 사업 + 도 = ''business also''.", "example_in_sentence": "사업도"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "특별하다", "en": "special; particular", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사실", "en": "fact", "note": ""}, {"ko": "발견되다", "en": "to be discovered", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아이", "en": "child", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가정", "en": "household; family", "note": ""}, {"ko": "애완동물", "en": "pet", "note": ""}, {"ko": "키우다", "en": "to raise; to keep (an animal)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "요즘", "en": "these days; nowadays", "note": ""}, {"ko": "결혼", "en": "marriage", "note": ""}, {"ko": "늦다", "en": "to be late", "note": ""}, {"ko": "낳다", "en": "to give birth; to have (a child)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하지만", "en": "however; but", "note": ""}, {"ko": "강아지", "en": "dog", "note": ""}, {"ko": "고양이", "en": "cat", "note": ""}, {"ko": "계속", "en": "continuously; continually", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비슷하다", "en": "similar; alike", "note": ""}, {"ko": "상황", "en": "situation; circumstance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "출산율", "en": "birth rate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "낮아지다", "en": "to become low; to decrease", "note": ""}, {"ko": "대신", "en": "instead; in place of", "note": ""}, {"ko": "반려동물", "en": "companion animal; pet", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가족", "en": "family", "note": ""}, {"ko": "늘어나다", "en": "to increase; to grow", "note": ""}, {"ko": "변화", "en": "change", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사회", "en": "society", "note": ""}, {"ko": "영향", "en": "influence; impact", "note": ""}, {"ko": "관련", "en": "relation; connection", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사업", "en": "business", "note": ""}, {"ko": "커지다", "en": "to grow bigger", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~았/었어요 (past)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "past polite. 발견되다 → 발견되었어요 = \"was discovered\".", "ex_ko": "미국에서 특별한 사실이 발견되었어요.", "ex_en": "A special fact has been discovered in the United States."}, {"name": "~이 (subject particle)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks the subject of the sentence; used after noun ending in consonant.", "ex_ko": "미국에서 특별한 사실이 발견되었어요.", "ex_en": "A special fact has been discovered in the United States."}, {"name": "~는 (verb modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "present-tense modifier before a noun. 키우다 → 키우는 가정 = \"households that raise (pets)\".", "ex_ko": "아이가 있는 가정보다 애완동물을 키우는 가정이 더 많다고 해요.", "ex_en": "It is said that there are more households raising pets than households with children."}, {"name": "~보다 (comparison particle)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Marks the standard of comparison; means ''than'' or ''more than''.", "ex_ko": "아이가 있는 가정보다 애완동물을 키우는 가정이 더 많다고 해요.", "ex_en": "It is said that there are more households raising pets than households with children."}, {"name": "~다고 하다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Reported speech pattern. Converts direct statement to indirect report; 많다 + 고 + 하다 = ''it is said that''.", "ex_ko": "아이가 있는 가정보다 애완동물을 키우는 가정이 더 많다고 해요.", "ex_en": "It is said that there are more households raising pets than households with children."}, {"name": "~거나 (alternative connective)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Connects two alternative clauses; 하 + 거나 = ''or'' (one option or another).", "ex_ko": "요즘 미국 사람들은 결혼을 늦게 하거나 아이를 적게 낳아요.", "ex_en": "These days, Americans marry late or have few children."}, {"name": "~아/어요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Present tense polite ending. 낳 + 아 + 요 = have (present habitual).", "ex_ko": "요즘 미국 사람들은 결혼을 늦게 하거나 아이를 적게 낳아요.", "ex_en": "These days, Americans marry late or have few children."}, {"name": "~나 (alternative particle with nouns)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Joins items as alternatives; 강아지 + 나 = ''dogs or/and [such things]''.", "ex_ko": "하지만 강아지나 고양이 같은 동물은 계속 키우고 있어요.", "ex_en": "However, they continue to raise animals like dogs and cats."}, {"name": "~같은 (similarity marker)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''like; such as''; attaches to noun to modify following noun.", "ex_ko": "하지만 강아지나 고양이 같은 동물은 계속 키우고 있어요.", "ex_en": "However, they continue to raise animals like dogs and cats."}, {"name": "~고 있다 (be V-ing)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Progressive aspect showing ongoing action or state. Indicates the process is currently happening.", "ex_ko": "하지만 강아지나 고양이 같은 동물은 계속 키우고 있어요.", "ex_en": "However, they continue to raise animals like dogs and cats."}, {"name": "이다 (copula)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Links subject to predicate noun. 상황 + 이 + 어요 = ''is a situation''.", "ex_ko": "한국도 비슷한 상황이에요.", "ex_en": "Korea is in a similar situation."}, {"name": "~아/어지다 (change of state)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "becoming. 낮다 → 낮아지다 = \"to become low\".", "ex_ko": "출산율이 낮아지고 있어요.", "ex_en": "The birth rate is decreasing."}, {"name": "~처럼 (similarity/manner)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Means ''like; as if''; indicates manner or comparison. 가족 + 처럼 = ''like family''.", "ex_ko": "대신 반려동물(pet)을 가족처럼 생각하는 사람들이 늘어나고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Instead, people who think of pets as family are increasing."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 것 같다 (I think it will)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "a guess about the future. 주다 → 줄 것 같아요 = \"it seems (it) will give\".", "ex_ko": "이런 변화는 사회에 큰 영향을 줄 것 같아요.", "ex_en": "Changes like this seem to have a big impact on society."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 거예요 (will)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "future. 커지다 (to grow bigger) → 커질 거예요 = \"will grow bigger\".", "ex_ko": "애완동물 관련 사업도 더 커질 거예요.", "ex_en": "Pet-related businesses will also grow larger."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mofayuusefil' and md5(translation) = '8306d178479199ac0e53762fd9f364bf';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["The Black Rhino lives in Africa. This animal fights much more than other animals. The results of scientists'' research are surprising. 50% of male black rhinos die from fighting. 30% of females die for the same reason. These animals fight with members of their own species. They don''t fight with other animals. They get injured and die fighting with black rhinos like themselves. Among all mammals (animals that nurse their young), the black rhino is the most dangerous. There is no animal that fights this much.", "Korean Teacher Shortage Becomes Serious, School Classes Disrupted", "What is an \"anxiety bag\"? A Popular Trend", "The United States and China Resume Talks Over Trade Issues", "\"Talking Pig\" Becomes SNS Star", "Apple Greatly Improves iPhone Speed with New AI Chip"], "sentences": [{"text": "검은 코뿔소(Black Rhino)는 아프리카에 살아요.", "translation": "The black rhino lives in Africa.", "vocab": [{"ko": "검다", "en": "to be black"}, {"ko": "코뿔소", "en": "rhino"}, {"ko": "아프리카", "en": "Africa"}, {"ko": "살다", "en": "to live"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어요", "exp": "Present tense declarative ending for beginners. Stems ending in ㅏ/ㅗ take ~아요; others take ~어요.", "example_in_sentence": "살아요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 (in, at)", "exp": "marks where someone lives or is. 아프리카 → 아프리카에 살아요 = \"live in Africa\".", "example_in_sentence": "아프리카에"}]}, {"text": "이 동물은 다른 동물보다 싸움을 많이 해요.", "translation": "This animal fights much more than other animals.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이", "en": "this"}, {"ko": "동물", "en": "animal"}, {"ko": "다른", "en": "different/other"}, {"ko": "싸움", "en": "fight"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~보다", "exp": "Comparison particle meaning ''than'' or ''compared to''.", "example_in_sentence": "다른 동물보다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를", "exp": "Object marker particle. Stems ending in consonants take ~을; vowels take ~를.", "example_in_sentence": "싸움을"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "싸움을 하다", "exp": "Verb phrase meaning ''to fight/engage in combat''. The noun 싸움 (fight) + 하다 (to do).", "example_in_sentence": "싸움을 많이 해요"}]}, {"text": "과학자들이 연구한 결과가 놀라워요.", "translation": "The result of scientists'' research is surprising.", "vocab": [{"ko": "과학자", "en": "scientist"}, {"ko": "연구하다", "en": "to research"}, {"ko": "결과", "en": "result"}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be surprising"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/은 (past participle)", "exp": "Modifying form used to describe nouns with past events. Stems ending in consonants take ~은; vowels take ~ㄴ.", "example_in_sentence": "연구한"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가", "exp": "Subject marker particle. Stems ending in consonants take ~이; vowels take ~가.", "example_in_sentence": "결과가"}]}, {"text": "수컷 검은 코뿔소 중 50%가 싸우다가 죽어요.", "translation": "50% of male black rhinos die while fighting.", "vocab": [{"ko": "수컷", "en": "male"}, {"ko": "싸우다", "en": "to fight"}, {"ko": "죽다", "en": "to die"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~ 중", "exp": "Among; used to specify a subset from a whole group.", "example_in_sentence": "수컷 검은 코뿔소 중"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다가", "exp": "Connective ending indicating a change of state or interruption during an action. Links two sequential events where the second interrupts or follows the first.", "example_in_sentence": "싸우다가"}]}, {"text": "암컷도 30%가 같은 이유로 죽어요.", "translation": "30% of females also die for the same reason.", "vocab": [{"ko": "암컷", "en": "female"}, {"ko": "이유", "en": "reason"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~도", "exp": "Particle meaning ''also'' or ''too'', indicating inclusion or addition.", "example_in_sentence": "암컷도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 (for, by)", "exp": "marks a reason or means; use 로 after a vowel. 같은 이유 → 같은 이유로 = \"for the same reason\".", "example_in_sentence": "같은 이유로"}]}, {"text": "이 동물들은 같은 종끼리 싸워요.", "translation": "These animals fight among their own species.", "vocab": [{"ko": "종", "en": "species"}, {"ko": "싸우다", "en": "to fight"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~끼리", "exp": "Particle meaning ''with each other'' or ''among themselves'', indicating mutual action within a group.", "example_in_sentence": "같은 종끼리"}]}, {"text": "다른 동물과 싸우는 게 아니에요.", "translation": "It''s not that they fight with other animals.", "vocab": [{"ko": "다른", "en": "different/other"}, {"ko": "싸우다", "en": "to fight"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것 (V-ing)", "exp": "turns a verb into a noun; 게 is the spoken form of 것이. 싸우다 → 싸우는 게 = \"fighting\".", "example_in_sentence": "싸우는 게"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 아니에요", "exp": "Negative copula in present tense. Negates nouns and nominalized phrases.", "example_in_sentence": "게 아니에요"}]}, {"text": "자기와 같은 검은 코뿔소와 싸우다가 다쳐서 죽어요.", "translation": "They get injured and die while fighting with other black rhinos like themselves.", "vocab": [{"ko": "자기", "en": "itself/oneself"}, {"ko": "같다", "en": "to be the same"}, {"ko": "싸우다", "en": "to fight"}, {"ko": "다치다", "en": "to be injured"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~과/와", "exp": "Conjunction particle meaning ''with'' or ''and''. Stems ending in consonants take ~과; vowels take ~와.", "example_in_sentence": "자기와"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다가", "exp": "Connective ending indicating a change of state or interruption during an action.", "example_in_sentence": "싸우다가"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어서/아서", "exp": "Connective ending indicating sequential actions or cause-effect relationship. Stems ending in ㅏ/ㅗ take ~아서; others take ~어서.", "example_in_sentence": "다쳐서"}]}, {"text": "모든 포유동물(젖을 먹여 기르는 동물) 중에서 검은 코뿔소가 가장 위험해요.", "translation": "Among all mammals (animals that feed their young with milk), the black rhino is the most dangerous.", "vocab": [{"ko": "모든", "en": "all"}, {"ko": "포유동물", "en": "mammal"}, {"ko": "젖", "en": "milk"}, {"ko": "먹이다", "en": "to feed"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~ 중에서", "exp": "Among; used to specify a subset from a larger whole group.", "example_in_sentence": "모든 포유동물 중에서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (verb modifier)", "exp": "present-tense modifier before a noun. 기르다 → 기르는 동물 = \"animals that raise (their young)\".", "example_in_sentence": "기르는 동물"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "가장 (the most)", "exp": "superlative. 위험하다 → 가장 위험해요 = \"is the most dangerous\".", "example_in_sentence": "가장 위험해요"}]}, {"text": "이렇게 많이 싸우는 동물은 없어요.", "translation": "There is no animal that fights this much.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이렇게", "en": "like this/this much"}, {"ko": "많이", "en": "much/a lot"}, {"ko": "싸우다", "en": "to fight"}, {"ko": "없다", "en": "to not exist"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (verb modifier)", "exp": "present-tense modifier before a noun. 싸우다 → 싸우는 동물 = \"an animal that fights\".", "example_in_sentence": "싸우는 동물"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~은/는 없어요", "exp": "Negative existential construction. Indicates non-existence or absence of something. Stems ending in consonants take ~은; vowels take ~는.", "example_in_sentence": "동물은 없어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "검다", "en": "to be black", "note": ""}, {"ko": "코뿔소", "en": "rhino", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아프리카", "en": "Africa", "note": ""}, {"ko": "살다", "en": "to live", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이", "en": "this", "note": ""}, {"ko": "동물", "en": "animal", "note": ""}, {"ko": "다른", "en": "different/other", "note": ""}, {"ko": "싸움", "en": "fight", "note": ""}, {"ko": "과학자", "en": "scientist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "연구하다", "en": "to research", "note": ""}, {"ko": "결과", "en": "result", "note": ""}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be surprising", "note": ""}, {"ko": "수컷", "en": "male", "note": ""}, {"ko": "싸우다", "en": "to fight", "note": ""}, {"ko": "죽다", "en": "to die", "note": ""}, {"ko": "암컷", "en": "female", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이유", "en": "reason", "note": ""}, {"ko": "종", "en": "species", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자기", "en": "itself/oneself", "note": ""}, {"ko": "같다", "en": "to be the same", "note": ""}, {"ko": "다치다", "en": "to be injured", "note": ""}, {"ko": "모든", "en": "all", "note": ""}, {"ko": "포유동물", "en": "mammal", "note": ""}, {"ko": "젖", "en": "milk", "note": ""}, {"ko": "먹이다", "en": "to feed", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이렇게", "en": "like this/this much", "note": ""}, {"ko": "많이", "en": "much/a lot", "note": ""}, {"ko": "없다", "en": "to not exist", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~아/어요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Present tense declarative ending for beginners. Stems ending in ㅏ/ㅗ take ~아요; others take ~어요.", "ex_ko": "검은 코뿔소(Black Rhino)는 아프리카에 살아요.", "ex_en": "The black rhino lives in Africa."}, {"name": "~에 (in, at)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "marks where someone lives or is. 아프리카 → 아프리카에 살아요 = \"live in Africa\".", "ex_ko": "검은 코뿔소(Black Rhino)는 아프리카에 살아요.", "ex_en": "The black rhino lives in Africa."}, {"name": "~보다", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Comparison particle meaning ''than'' or ''compared to''.", "ex_ko": "이 동물은 다른 동물보다 싸움을 많이 해요.", "ex_en": "This animal fights much more than other animals."}, {"name": "~을/를", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Object marker particle. Stems ending in consonants take ~을; vowels take ~를.", "ex_ko": "이 동물은 다른 동물보다 싸움을 많이 해요.", "ex_en": "This animal fights much more than other animals."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/은 (past participle)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Modifying form used to describe nouns with past events. Stems ending in consonants take ~은; vowels take ~ㄴ.", "ex_ko": "과학자들이 연구한 결과가 놀라워요.", "ex_en": "The result of scientists'' research is surprising."}, {"name": "~이/가", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Subject marker particle. Stems ending in consonants take ~이; vowels take ~가.", "ex_ko": "과학자들이 연구한 결과가 놀라워요.", "ex_en": "The result of scientists'' research is surprising."}, {"name": "~다가", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Connective ending indicating a change of state or interruption during an action. Links two sequential events where the second interrupts or follows the first.", "ex_ko": "수컷 검은 코뿔소 중 50%가 싸우다가 죽어요.", "ex_en": "50% of male black rhinos die while fighting."}, {"name": "~도", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Particle meaning ''also'' or ''too'', indicating inclusion or addition.", "ex_ko": "암컷도 30%가 같은 이유로 죽어요.", "ex_en": "30% of females also die for the same reason."}, {"name": "~(으)로 (for, by)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "marks a reason or means; use 로 after a vowel. 같은 이유 → 같은 이유로 = \"for the same reason\".", "ex_ko": "암컷도 30%가 같은 이유로 죽어요.", "ex_en": "30% of females also die for the same reason."}, {"name": "~끼리", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Particle meaning ''with each other'' or ''among themselves'', indicating mutual action within a group.", "ex_ko": "이 동물들은 같은 종끼리 싸워요.", "ex_en": "These animals fight among their own species."}, {"name": "~는 것 (V-ing)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "turns a verb into a noun; 게 is the spoken form of 것이. 싸우다 → 싸우는 게 = \"fighting\".", "ex_ko": "다른 동물과 싸우는 게 아니에요.", "ex_en": "It''s not that they fight with other animals."}, {"name": "~이/가 아니에요", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Negative copula in present tense. Negates nouns and nominalized phrases.", "ex_ko": "다른 동물과 싸우는 게 아니에요.", "ex_en": "It''s not that they fight with other animals."}, {"name": "~과/와", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Conjunction particle meaning ''with'' or ''and''. Stems ending in consonants take ~과; vowels take ~와.", "ex_ko": "자기와 같은 검은 코뿔소와 싸우다가 다쳐서 죽어요.", "ex_en": "They get injured and die while fighting with other black rhinos like themselves."}, {"name": "~어서/아서", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "Connective ending indicating sequential actions or cause-effect relationship. Stems ending in ㅏ/ㅗ take ~아서; others take ~어서.", "ex_ko": "자기와 같은 검은 코뿔소와 싸우다가 다쳐서 죽어요.", "ex_en": "They get injured and die while fighting with other black rhinos like themselves."}, {"name": "~는 (verb modifier)", "level": "Beginner", "exp": "present-tense modifier before a noun. 기르다 → 기르는 동물 = \"animals that raise (their young)\".", "ex_ko": "모든 포유동물(젖을 먹여 기르는 동물) 중에서 검은 코뿔소가 가장 위험해요.", "ex_en": "Among all mammals (animals that feed their young with milk), the black rhino is the most dangerous."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mofazpyrvz4t' and md5(translation) = '24ac3e07dfe2e4d75505241280a0e3f3';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["This is a story that happened in America long ago. In 1930, 600 beavers were released in Oregon. It was to prevent soil from being washed away by water.", "One beaver cost 5 dollars. But what the beaver did was worth 300 dollars. This is because the beaver built a dam and protected the soil.", "Beavers build dams with wood. The dam blocks the water so the soil doesn''t get washed away. If people do it, it costs a lot of money.", "Animals can also help us greatly. The power of nature is truly amazing."], "sentences": [{"text": "옛날 미국에서 일어난 일이에요.", "translation": "It''s something that happened in the United States long ago.", "vocab": [{"ko": "옛날", "en": "long ago; the old days"}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to happen; to occur"}, {"ko": "일", "en": "thing; matter; event"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "describes a noun with a past action. 일어나다 → 일어난 일 = \"something that happened\".", "example_in_sentence": "일어난 일"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "이에요 (copula)", "exp": "Combines 이다 (to be) + ~어요 (polite present ending). Connects subject to descriptive predicate.", "example_in_sentence": "일이에요"}]}, {"text": "1930년에 오리건 주에서 비버 600마리를 풀어놨어요.", "translation": "In 1930, they released 600 beavers in Oregon.", "vocab": [{"ko": "풀어놓다", "en": "to release; to let loose"}, {"ko": "마리", "en": "counter for animals"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "exp": "past polite. 풀어놓다 → 풀어놓았어요, shortened to 풀어놨어요 = \"released\".", "example_in_sentence": "풀어놨어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "을/를 (object particle)", "exp": "Marks 비버 600마리 as the direct object of the action 풀어놓다.", "example_in_sentence": "비버 600마리를"}]}, {"text": "흙이 물에 쓸려가는 것을 막기 위해서였어요.", "translation": "It was in order to prevent soil from being washed away by water.", "vocab": [{"ko": "흙", "en": "soil; earth"}, {"ko": "쓸려가다", "en": "to be washed away; to be swept away"}, {"ko": "막다", "en": "to prevent; to block"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것 (V-ing)", "exp": "turns a verb into a noun. 쓸려가다 → 쓸려가는 것 = \"(soil) being washed away\".", "example_in_sentence": "쓸려가는 것"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 위해서 (in order to)", "exp": "purpose. 막다 → 막기 위해서 = \"in order to prevent\".", "example_in_sentence": "막기 위해서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "였어요 (past copula)", "exp": "이다 + 었어요 forms past tense of copula. Describes a past state or reason.", "example_in_sentence": "였어요"}]}, {"text": "비버 한 마리는 5달러였어요.", "translation": "One beaver was 5 dollars.", "vocab": [{"ko": "달러", "en": "dollar"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "는 (contrastive particle)", "exp": "Marks 비버 한 마리 as the topic, suggesting contrast or focus on this specific item.", "example_in_sentence": "비버 한 마리는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "였어요 (past copula)", "exp": "이다 + 었어요 forms past tense of copula. Connects subject to its value/price.", "example_in_sentence": "였어요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 비버가 한 일은 300달러 값어치였어요.", "translation": "However, the work that beavers did was worth 300 dollars.", "vocab": [{"ko": "하지만", "en": "however; but"}, {"ko": "값어치", "en": "value; worth"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "describes a noun with a past action. 하다 → 한 일 = \"the work (they) did\".", "example_in_sentence": "한 일"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "은 (contrastive particle)", "exp": "Marks 비버가 한 일 as the topic, contrasting with the previous statement about individual beaver cost.", "example_in_sentence": "일은"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "였어요 (past copula)", "exp": "이다 + 었어요 forms past tense of copula. Indicates the worth in a past context.", "example_in_sentence": "였어요"}]}, {"text": "비버가 댐을 만들어서 흙을 지켜줬거든요.", "translation": "Because beavers built a dam and protected the soil for us.", "vocab": [{"ko": "댐", "en": "dam"}, {"ko": "만들다", "en": "to make; to build"}, {"ko": "지키다", "en": "to protect; to keep"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~어서 (sequential connective)", "exp": "만들다 (build) + 어서 connects two actions in sequence. Shows that building the dam led to protecting soil.", "example_in_sentence": "만들어서"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~아/어 주다 (do for someone)", "exp": "doing something that helps someone else. 지키다 → 지켜 주다 = \"to protect (for us)\".", "example_in_sentence": "지켜줬"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었거든요 (reason/explanation in past)", "exp": "Combines past tense 았/었 + 거든요 to give a reason or explanation. Emphasizes the reason for the previous statement.", "example_in_sentence": "지켜줬거든요"}]}, {"text": "비버는 나무로 댐을 만들어요.", "translation": "Beavers make dams with wood.", "vocab": [{"ko": "나무", "en": "wood; tree"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 (instrumental particle)", "exp": "나무 (wood) + 로 marks the material or means used to make the dam. Shows what something is made from.", "example_in_sentence": "나무로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어요 (polite present tense)", "exp": "만들다 (make) + 어요 forms polite present tense. Describes a habitual or general action.", "example_in_sentence": "만들어요"}]}, {"text": "댐이 물을 막아줘서 흙이 안 쓸려가요.", "translation": "Because the dam blocks water for us, soil doesn''t get washed away.", "vocab": [{"ko": "막다", "en": "to block; to prevent"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~아/어주다 (benefactive auxiliary verb)", "exp": "막다 (block) + 아/어주다 expresses doing an action as a benefit. The dam blocks water in a way that helps.", "example_in_sentence": "막아줘서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어서 (sequential connective)", "exp": "막아주다 + 어서 connects the blocking action as the reason for the following result.", "example_in_sentence": "막아줘서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "안 (negation adverb)", "exp": "안 (not) negates the following verb 쓸려가다. Indicates that soil does not get washed away.", "example_in_sentence": "안 쓸려가요"}]}, {"text": "사람이 하면 돈이 많이 들어요.", "translation": "If people do it, it costs a lot of money.", "vocab": [{"ko": "들다", "en": "to cost; to take (time/money)"}, {"ko": "많이", "en": "much; a lot"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면 (if)", "exp": "condition. 하다 → 하면 = \"if (people) do it\".", "example_in_sentence": "하면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어요 (polite present tense)", "exp": "들다 (cost) + 어요 forms polite present tense. Describes a general fact or habitual situation.", "example_in_sentence": "들어요"}]}, {"text": "동물도 우리에게 큰 도움을 줄 수 있어요.", "translation": "Animals can also give great help to us.", "vocab": [{"ko": "도움", "en": "help; assistance"}, {"ko": "주다", "en": "to give"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~도 (also particle)", "exp": "동물 (animals) + 도 means ''also'' or ''too'', suggesting animals in addition to other subjects can help.", "example_in_sentence": "동물도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~을/를 (object particle)", "exp": "도움 (help) + 을 marks the direct object of 주다 (give). Indicates what is being given.", "example_in_sentence": "도움을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄹ 수 있다 (possibility/ability)", "exp": "주다 (give) + ㄹ + 수 + 있어요 expresses possibility or ability. Indicates that something can happen.", "example_in_sentence": "줄 수 있어요"}]}, {"text": "자연의 힘은 정말 대단해요.", "translation": "The power of nature is really amazing.", "vocab": [{"ko": "자연", "en": "nature"}, {"ko": "힘", "en": "power; strength"}, {"ko": "대단하다", "en": "to be amazing; to be great"}, {"ko": "정말", "en": "really; truly"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "의 (possessive particle)", "exp": "자연 (nature) + 의 marks possession or attribution. Shows that 힘 (power) belongs to or comes from nature.", "example_in_sentence": "자연의"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어요 (polite present tense)", "exp": "대단하다 (be amazing) + 어요 forms polite present tense. Expresses a state or quality in present time.", "example_in_sentence": "대단해요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "옛날", "en": "long ago; the old days", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to happen; to occur", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일", "en": "thing; matter; event", "note": ""}, {"ko": "풀어놓다", "en": "to release; to let loose", "note": ""}, {"ko": "마리", "en": "counter for animals", "note": ""}, {"ko": "흙", "en": "soil; earth", "note": ""}, {"ko": "쓸려가다", "en": "to be washed away; to be swept away", "note": ""}, {"ko": "막다", "en": "to prevent; to block", "note": ""}, {"ko": "달러", "en": "dollar", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하지만", "en": "however; but", "note": ""}, {"ko": "값어치", "en": "value; worth", "note": ""}, {"ko": "댐", "en": "dam", "note": ""}, {"ko": "만들다", "en": "to make; to build", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지키다", "en": "to protect; to keep", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나무", "en": "wood; tree", "note": ""}, {"ko": "들다", "en": "to cost; to take (time/money)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "많이", "en": "much; a lot", "note": ""}, {"ko": "도움", "en": "help; assistance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "주다", "en": "to give", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자연", "en": "nature", "note": ""}, {"ko": "힘", "en": "power; strength", "note": ""}, {"ko": "대단하다", "en": "to be amazing; to be great", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정말", "en": "really; truly", "note": ""}, {"word": "비버", "reading": "bibeo", "meaning": "beaver", "context": "1930년에 오리건 주에서 비버 600마리를 풀어놨어요"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "describes a noun with a past action. 일어나다 → 일어난 일 = \"something that happened\".", "ex_ko": "옛날 미국에서 일어난 일이에요.", "ex_en": "It''s something that happened in the United States long ago."}, {"name": "이에요 (copula)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Combines 이다 (to be) + ~어요 (polite present ending). Connects subject to descriptive predicate.", "ex_ko": "옛날 미국에서 일어난 일이에요.", "ex_en": "It''s something that happened in the United States long ago."}, {"name": "~았/었어요 (past tense)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "past polite. 풀어놓다 → 풀어놓았어요, shortened to 풀어놨어요 = \"released\".", "ex_ko": "1930년에 오리건 주에서 비버 600마리를 풀어놨어요.", "ex_en": "In 1930, they released 600 beavers in Oregon."}, {"name": "을/를 (object particle)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Marks 비버 600마리 as the direct object of the action 풀어놓다.", "ex_ko": "1930년에 오리건 주에서 비버 600마리를 풀어놨어요.", "ex_en": "In 1930, they released 600 beavers in Oregon."}, {"name": "~는 것 (V-ing)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "turns a verb into a noun. 쓸려가다 → 쓸려가는 것 = \"(soil) being washed away\".", "ex_ko": "흙이 물에 쓸려가는 것을 막기 위해서였어요.", "ex_en": "It was in order to prevent soil from being washed away by water."}, {"name": "~기 위해서 (in order to)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "purpose. 막다 → 막기 위해서 = \"in order to prevent\".", "ex_ko": "흙이 물에 쓸려가는 것을 막기 위해서였어요.", "ex_en": "It was in order to prevent soil from being washed away by water."}, {"name": "였어요 (past copula)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "이다 + 었어요 forms past tense of copula. Indicates the worth in a past context.", "ex_ko": "흙이 물에 쓸려가는 것을 막기 위해서였어요.", "ex_en": "It was in order to prevent soil from being washed away by water."}, {"name": "는 (contrastive particle)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Marks 비버 한 마리 as the topic, suggesting contrast or focus on this specific item.", "ex_ko": "비버 한 마리는 5달러였어요.", "ex_en": "One beaver was 5 dollars."}, {"name": "은 (contrastive particle)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Marks 비버가 한 일 as the topic, contrasting with the previous statement about individual beaver cost.", "ex_ko": "하지만 비버가 한 일은 300달러 값어치였어요.", "ex_en": "However, the work that beavers did was worth 300 dollars."}, {"name": "~어서 (sequential connective)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "만들다 (build) + 어서 connects two actions in sequence. Shows that building the dam led to protecting soil.", "ex_ko": "비버가 댐을 만들어서 흙을 지켜줬거든요.", "ex_en": "Because beavers built a dam and protected the soil for us."}, {"name": "~았/었거든요 (reason/explanation in past)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Combines past tense 았/었 + 거든요 to give a reason or explanation. Emphasizes the reason for the previous statement.", "ex_ko": "비버가 댐을 만들어서 흙을 지켜줬거든요.", "ex_en": "Because beavers built a dam and protected the soil for us."}, {"name": "~(으)로 (instrumental particle)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "나무 (wood) + 로 marks the material or means used to make the dam. Shows what something is made from.", "ex_ko": "비버는 나무로 댐을 만들어요.", "ex_en": "Beavers make dams with wood."}, {"name": "~어요 (polite present tense)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "대단하다 (be amazing) + 어요 forms polite present tense. Expresses a state or quality in present time.", "ex_ko": "비버는 나무로 댐을 만들어요.", "ex_en": "Beavers make dams with wood."}, {"name": "~아/어서 (sequential connective)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "막아주다 + 어서 connects the blocking action as the reason for the following result.", "ex_ko": "댐이 물을 막아줘서 흙이 안 쓸려가요.", "ex_en": "Because the dam blocks water for us, soil doesn''t get washed away."}, {"name": "안 (negation adverb)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "안 (not) negates the following verb 쓸려가다. Indicates that soil does not get washed away.", "ex_ko": "댐이 물을 막아줘서 흙이 안 쓸려가요.", "ex_en": "Because the dam blocks water for us, soil doesn''t get washed away."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mofb0jl5y7ag' and md5(translation) = '98581d2783706a74c0dc598fffe5d890';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["In 2015, something extraordinary happened in Texas, USA. A man''s wife hired a killer to murder her husband. After the police learned about this fact, they made a surprising decision. The police staged a fake death together with this man. They even took photos of a grave to make it completely convincing. This way, they were able to prevent the wife''s murder plan. This case is still being talked about by many people today. It is an example of police using a creative method to protect citizens. It was recorded as a special case of cooperation by law enforcement agencies (organizations that enforce the law). This kind of dramatic situation seems like something you would only see in a drama. However, it''s even more surprising because it actually happened. It''s a story of how police officers'' resourcefulness saved one person''s life.", "Korean teacher shortage crisis worsens, disrupting school classes", "What is an ''anxiety bag''? A popular trend", "The US and China resume talks over trade issues", "\"Talking pig\" becomes an SNS star", "''Nothing maxing'' trend spreads—doing absolutely nothing"], "sentences": [{"text": "2015년 미국 텍사스주에서 특별한 일이 일어났어요.", "translation": "In 2015, something special happened in Texas, USA.", "vocab": [{"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special"}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to happen"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense ending for informal polite speech. Marks completed action in past. 일어나다 → 일어났어요.", "example_in_sentence": "일어났어요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~에서 (location/setting)", "exp": "Marks the location where an action occurs. 텍사스주에서 = in Texas.", "example_in_sentence": "텍사스주에서"}]}, {"text": "한 남성의 아내가 킬러를 고용해 남편을 죽이려 했어요.", "translation": "A man''s wife hired a hitman to try to kill her husband.", "vocab": [{"ko": "고용하다", "en": "to hire; to employ"}, {"ko": "죽이다", "en": "to kill"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)려(고) 하다 (try to)", "exp": "intention or attempt. 죽이다 → 죽이려 했어요 = \"tried to kill\".", "example_in_sentence": "죽이려 했어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어 (sequential connection)", "exp": "Connects actions in sequence showing cause or means. 고용해 = hired (and then attempted to kill). 고용하다 → 고용해.", "example_in_sentence": "고용해 남편을 죽이려"}]}, {"text": "경찰이 이 사실을 알게 된 후 놀라운 결정을 했습니다.", "translation": "After the police came to know this fact, they made a surprising decision.", "vocab": [{"ko": "알다", "en": "to know; to find out"}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be surprising; astonishing"}, {"ko": "결정", "en": "decision"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 되다", "exp": "Marks a change of state or circumstance that comes about naturally/unintentionally. 알다 → 알게 → 알게 되다.", "example_in_sentence": "알게 된"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~ㄴ/은 후 (after)", "exp": "Indicates temporal sequence: after an event completes. 알게 된 후 = after coming to know.", "example_in_sentence": "알게 된 후"}]}, {"text": "경찰은 이 남성과 함께 가짜 죽음을 연출했어요.", "translation": "The police staged a fake death together with this man.", "vocab": [{"ko": "가짜", "en": "fake; false"}, {"ko": "연출하다", "en": "to stage; to produce"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense in informal polite register. 연출하다 → 연출했어요.", "example_in_sentence": "연출했어요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~과/와 함께 (together with)", "exp": "Indicates accompaniment or cooperation. 남성과 함께 = together with the man.", "example_in_sentence": "남성과 함께"}]}, {"text": "무덤 사진까지 찍어서 완벽하게 꾸몄습니다.", "translation": "They even took photos of a grave and staged it all perfectly.", "vocab": [{"ko": "무덤", "en": "grave; tomb"}, {"ko": "찍다", "en": "to take (a photo); to shoot"}, {"ko": "완벽하다", "en": "to be perfect; flawless"}, {"ko": "꾸미다", "en": "to set up; to fake; to decorate"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~까지", "exp": "Particle marking extent or inclusion; emphasizes that something goes as far as what follows. 사진까지 = even photos.", "example_in_sentence": "사진까지"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어서 (sequential)", "exp": "one action, then the next. 찍다 → 찍어서 = \"took (photos) and then\".", "example_in_sentence": "찍어서"}]}, {"text": "이렇게 해서 아내의 살인 계획을 막을 수 있었어요.", "translation": "In this way, they were able to stop the wife''s murder plan.", "vocab": [{"ko": "살인", "en": "murder; homicide"}, {"ko": "계획", "en": "plan"}, {"ko": "막다", "en": "to stop; to block; to prevent"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "Expresses ability or possibility. 막을 수 있다 = was able to prevent. Combines potential form with auxiliary.", "example_in_sentence": "막을 수 있었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense. 있다 → 있었어요, marking past ability/state.", "example_in_sentence": "있었어요"}]}, {"text": "이 사건은 현재까지도 많은 사람들에게 회자되고 있어요.", "translation": "This case is still being talked about by many people up to the present.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사건", "en": "incident; case"}, {"ko": "현재", "en": "present; now"}, {"ko": "회자되다", "en": "to be discussed; to be talked about"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect: ongoing state or action in present. 회자되다 → 회자되고 있다. Indicates continuous or repeated action.", "example_in_sentence": "회자되고 있어요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~까지 (up to; through)", "exp": "Marks extent to current time. 현재까지 = up to/through the present.", "example_in_sentence": "현재까지도"}]}, {"text": "경찰이 시민을 보호하기 위해 창의적인 방법을 사용한 사례예요.", "translation": "It is a case where police used a creative method to protect citizens.", "vocab": [{"ko": "시민", "en": "citizen"}, {"ko": "보호하다", "en": "to protect"}, {"ko": "창의적", "en": "creative"}, {"ko": "사례", "en": "case; example; instance"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~기 위해 (in order to; for the purpose of)", "exp": "Expresses purpose or goal. 보호하다 → 보호하기 → 보호하기 위해.", "example_in_sentence": "보호하기 위해"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "describes a noun with a past action. 사용하다 → 사용한 사례 = \"a case where (they) used\".", "example_in_sentence": "사용한 사례"}]}, {"text": "법 집행 기관(법을 지키게 하는 조직)의 특별한 협력 사례로 기록되었습니다.", "translation": "It was recorded as a special case of cooperation by law enforcement agencies (organizations that make people obey the law).", "vocab": [{"ko": "법 집행 기관", "en": "law enforcement agency"}, {"ko": "협력", "en": "cooperation"}, {"ko": "기록되다", "en": "to be recorded"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~되다 (passive)", "exp": "makes a 하다 verb passive. 기록하다 → 기록되다 → 기록되었습니다 = \"was recorded\".", "example_in_sentence": "기록되었습니다"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~로 (as; in the capacity of)", "exp": "Marks the role or designation. 사례로 = as a case; in the role of.", "example_in_sentence": "사례로"}]}, {"text": "이런 극적인 상황은 드라마에서나 볼 수 있을 것 같아요.", "translation": "Such a dramatic situation seems like it could only be seen in dramas.", "vocab": [{"ko": "극적", "en": "dramatic"}, {"ko": "상황", "en": "situation; circumstance"}, {"ko": "드라마", "en": "drama"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "Expresses possibility. 볼 수 있다 = can be seen. Potential form with auxiliary.", "example_in_sentence": "볼 수 있을"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 것 같다 (seems like it would)", "exp": "a guess or impression. 있다 → 있을 것 같아요 = \"it seems (one) could\".", "example_in_sentence": "있을 것 같아요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서나 (only in; nowhere but in)", "exp": "Restricts to a specific location/context. 드라마에서나 = only/nowhere but in dramas.", "example_in_sentence": "드라마에서나"}]}, {"text": "하지만 실제로 일어난 일이라서 더욱 놀랍습니다.", "translation": "However, because it actually happened, it is even more surprising.", "vocab": [{"ko": "실제로", "en": "actually; in reality"}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be surprising; astonishing"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "describes a noun with a past action. 일어나다 → 일어난 일 = \"something that happened\".", "example_in_sentence": "일어난"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~라서 (because; so)", "exp": "Causal connector in informal speech. 일이라서 = because it is an event. Combines ~라 + ~아/어서.", "example_in_sentence": "일이라서"}]}, {"text": "경찰의 기지로 한 사람의 생명을 구한 이야기예요.", "translation": "It is a story about how the police''s quick thinking saved a person''s life.", "vocab": [{"ko": "기지", "en": "wit; resourcefulness; quick thinking"}, {"ko": "생명", "en": "life"}, {"ko": "구하다", "en": "to save; to rescue"}, {"ko": "이야기", "en": "story; tale"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "describes a noun with a past action. 구하다 → 구한 이야기 = \"a story of (how they) saved\".", "example_in_sentence": "구한"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~로 (by means of; through)", "exp": "Marks means or instrument. 기지로 = by/through wit.", "example_in_sentence": "기지로"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to happen", "note": ""}, {"ko": "고용하다", "en": "to hire; to employ", "note": ""}, {"ko": "죽이다", "en": "to kill", "note": ""}, {"ko": "알다", "en": "to know; to find out", "note": ""}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be surprising; astonishing", "note": ""}, {"ko": "결정", "en": "decision", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가짜", "en": "fake; false", "note": ""}, {"ko": "연출하다", "en": "to stage; to produce", "note": ""}, {"ko": "무덤", "en": "grave; tomb", "note": ""}, {"ko": "찍다", "en": "to take (a photo); to shoot", "note": ""}, {"ko": "완벽하다", "en": "to be perfect; flawless", "note": ""}, {"ko": "꾸미다", "en": "to set up; to fake; to decorate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "살인", "en": "murder; homicide", "note": ""}, {"ko": "계획", "en": "plan", "note": ""}, {"ko": "막다", "en": "to stop; to block; to prevent", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사건", "en": "incident; case", "note": ""}, {"ko": "현재", "en": "present; now", "note": ""}, {"ko": "회자되다", "en": "to be discussed; to be talked about", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시민", "en": "citizen", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보호하다", "en": "to protect", "note": ""}, {"ko": "창의적", "en": "creative", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사례", "en": "case; example; instance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "법 집행 기관", "en": "law enforcement agency", "note": ""}, {"ko": "협력", "en": "cooperation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기록되다", "en": "to be recorded", "note": ""}, {"ko": "극적", "en": "dramatic", "note": ""}, {"ko": "상황", "en": "situation; circumstance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "드라마", "en": "drama", "note": ""}, {"ko": "실제로", "en": "actually; in reality", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기지", "en": "wit; resourcefulness; quick thinking", "note": ""}, {"ko": "생명", "en": "life", "note": ""}, {"ko": "구하다", "en": "to save; to rescue", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이야기", "en": "story; tale", "note": ""}, {"word": "킬러", "reading": "killeo", "meaning": "killer; assassin", "context": "아내가 킬러를 고용해 남편을 죽이려 했어요"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~았/었어요", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past tense ending for informal polite speech. Marks completed action in past. 일어나다 → 일어났어요.", "ex_ko": "2015년 미국 텍사스주에서 특별한 일이 일어났어요.", "ex_en": "In 2015, something special happened in Texas, USA."}, {"name": "~(으)려(고) 하다 (try to)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "intention or attempt. 죽이다 → 죽이려 했어요 = \"tried to kill\".", "ex_ko": "한 남성의 아내가 킬러를 고용해 남편을 죽이려 했어요.", "ex_en": "A man''s wife hired a hitman to try to kill her husband."}, {"name": "~아/어 (sequential connection)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Connects actions in sequence showing cause or means. 고용해 = hired (and then attempted to kill). 고용하다 → 고용해.", "ex_ko": "한 남성의 아내가 킬러를 고용해 남편을 죽이려 했어요.", "ex_en": "A man''s wife hired a hitman to try to kill her husband."}, {"name": "~게 되다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Marks a change of state or circumstance that comes about naturally/unintentionally. 알다 → 알게 → 알게 되다.", "ex_ko": "경찰이 이 사실을 알게 된 후 놀라운 결정을 했습니다.", "ex_en": "After the police came to know this fact, they made a surprising decision."}, {"name": "~까지", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Particle marking extent or inclusion; emphasizes that something goes as far as what follows. 사진까지 = even photos.", "ex_ko": "무덤 사진까지 찍어서 완벽하게 꾸몄습니다.", "ex_en": "They even took photos of a grave and staged it all perfectly."}, {"name": "~고 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Progressive aspect: ongoing state or action in present. 회자되다 → 회자되고 있다. Indicates continuous or repeated action.", "ex_ko": "이 사건은 현재까지도 많은 사람들에게 회자되고 있어요.", "ex_en": "This case is still being talked about by many people up to the present."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "describes a noun with a past action. 구하다 → 구한 이야기 = \"a story of (how they) saved\".", "ex_ko": "경찰이 시민을 보호하기 위해 창의적인 방법을 사용한 사례예요.", "ex_en": "It is a case where police used a creative method to protect citizens."}, {"name": "~되다 (passive)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "makes a 하다 verb passive. 기록하다 → 기록되다 → 기록되었습니다 = \"was recorded\".", "ex_ko": "법 집행 기관(법을 지키게 하는 조직)의 특별한 협력 사례로 기록되었습니다.", "ex_en": "It was recorded as a special case of cooperation by law enforcement agencies (organizations that make people obey the law)."}, {"name": "~ㄹ 수 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Expresses possibility. 볼 수 있다 = can be seen. Potential form with auxiliary.", "ex_ko": "이런 극적인 상황은 드라마에서나 볼 수 있을 것 같아요.", "ex_en": "Such a dramatic situation seems like it could only be seen in dramas."}, {"name": "~에서나 (only in; nowhere but in)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Restricts to a specific location/context. 드라마에서나 = only/nowhere but in dramas.", "ex_ko": "이런 극적인 상황은 드라마에서나 볼 수 있을 것 같아요.", "ex_en": "Such a dramatic situation seems like it could only be seen in dramas."}, {"name": "~라서 (because; so)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Causal connector in informal speech. 일이라서 = because it is an event. Combines ~라 + ~아/어서.", "ex_ko": "하지만 실제로 일어난 일이라서 더욱 놀랍습니다.", "ex_en": "However, because it actually happened, it is even more surprising."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mofb1hx2an4c' and md5(translation) = 'bce8b81bc41a8cdc3e240c8775601079';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Recently, an interesting video has been trending online. It shows a single duck swimming on the water with numerous fish following behind it.", "This phenomenon happens more often than you might think. When a duck swims through the water, small insects and food scraps fall down. Fish know this and search for food around the duck.", "Experts explain this as a ''symbiotic relationship.'' The duck provides food for the fish, and the fish keep the area around the duck clean. It''s an interesting cooperative relationship you can see in nature.", "You can often see this kind of scene in Korea''s ponds and lakes. Next time you visit a park, try to observe the area around the ducks carefully. You will definitely be able to discover an interesting sight."], "sentences": [{"text": "최근 온라인에서 신기한 영상이 화제가 되고 있어요.", "translation": "Recently, an interesting video has been becoming a topic of discussion online.", "vocab": [{"ko": "최근", "en": "recently"}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be amazing; fascinating"}, {"ko": "화제", "en": "topic/subject of discussion"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect marker: indicates an action in progress. 되다 (become) + ~고 있어요 (is becoming/has been becoming).", "example_in_sentence": "화제가 되고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "한 마리 오리가 물 위를 헤엄치는데, 수많은 물고기들이 그 뒤를 따라다니는 모습이 담겨 있습니다.", "translation": "It shows a duck swimming on the water, with countless fish following behind it.", "vocab": [{"ko": "마리", "en": "counter for animals"}, {"ko": "헤엄치다", "en": "to swim"}, {"ko": "수많다", "en": "to be numerous"}, {"ko": "따라다니다", "en": "to follow around"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는데 (background)", "exp": "sets up the background for what follows. 헤엄치다 → 헤엄치는데 = \"(a duck) swims, and ~\".", "example_in_sentence": "헤엄치는데"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~는 모습", "exp": "Pattern meaning ''the scene/sight of ~ing''; combines relative clause with 모습 (appearance/scene).", "example_in_sentence": "따라다니는 모습"}]}, {"text": "이런 현상은 생각보다 자주 일어나요.", "translation": "This kind of phenomenon occurs more frequently than one might think.", "vocab": [{"ko": "현상", "en": "phenomenon"}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to occur/happen"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "생각보다", "exp": "Comparative expression meaning ''more than expected/thought''; 생각 (thought) + 보다 (than).", "example_in_sentence": "생각보다"}]}, {"text": "오리가 물속을 헤엄칠 때 작은 벌레나 음식 조각들이 떨어지기 때문입니다.", "translation": "It is because small insects or food fragments fall when the duck swims through the water.", "vocab": [{"ko": "벌레", "en": "insect/bug"}, {"ko": "조각", "en": "piece/fragment"}, {"ko": "떨어지다", "en": "to fall/drop"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄹ 때", "exp": "Temporal connective meaning ''when/at the time of ~''; attaches to verb stem 헤엄치다 → 헤엄칠 때.", "example_in_sentence": "헤엄칠 때"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 때문이다", "exp": "Causal ending: ''(it is) because ~''; 떨어지다 + ~기 (nominalizer) + 때문 (reason).", "example_in_sentence": "떨어지기 때문입니다"}]}, {"text": "물고기들은 이를 알고 오리 주변에서 먹이를 찾아요.", "translation": "Fish know this and search for food around the duck.", "vocab": [{"ko": "먹이", "en": "food/bait"}, {"ko": "찾다", "en": "to search/look for"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "Connective ending linking two sequential or related actions; 알다 + ~고 shows ''know and (then) search''.", "example_in_sentence": "알고"}]}, {"text": "전문가들은 이것을 ''공생 관계''라고 설명해요.", "translation": "Experts explain this as a ''symbiotic relationship.''", "vocab": [{"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert"}, {"ko": "공생", "en": "symbiosis"}, {"ko": "관계", "en": "relationship"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~라고 설명하다", "exp": "Expression for explanation/description: ~라고 (quotes/names something as) + 설명하다 (explain). 공생 관계 + ~라고 설명해요.", "example_in_sentence": "''공생 관계''라고 설명해요"}]}, {"text": "오리는 물고기들에게 음식을 제공하고, 물고기들은 오리 주변을 깨끗하게 만들어 줍니다.", "translation": "The duck provides food to the fish, and the fish make the area around the duck clean.", "vocab": [{"ko": "제공하다", "en": "to provide"}, {"ko": "깨끗하다", "en": "to be clean"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "Connective listing two parallel or contrasting clauses; 제공하고 (provide and) introduces the second clause with 물고기들은.", "example_in_sentence": "제공하고"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~게 만들다", "exp": "Causative expression meaning ''make/cause to be ~''; 깨끗하다 + ~게 (adverbial) + 만들다 (make).", "example_in_sentence": "깨끗하게 만들어"}]}, {"text": "자연에서 볼 수 있는 흥미로운 협력 관계예요.", "translation": "It is an interesting cooperative relationship that can be seen in nature.", "vocab": [{"ko": "협력", "en": "cooperation"}, {"ko": "흥미롭다", "en": "to be interesting"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~ㄹ 수 있다", "exp": "Possibility marker: ''(is) able to/can ~''; 보다 (see) + ~ㄹ 수 있다 in relative clause modifying 관계.", "example_in_sentence": "볼 수 있는"}]}, {"text": "이런 모습은 우리나라 연못이나 호수에서도 종종 볼 수 있어요.", "translation": "This kind of sight can often be seen in ponds or lakes in our country too.", "vocab": [{"ko": "연못", "en": "pond"}, {"ko": "호수", "en": "lake"}, {"ko": "종종", "en": "often"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~나", "exp": "Alternative/listing particle meaning ''or''; 연못이나 호수 (pond or lake).", "example_in_sentence": "연못이나 호수"}]}, {"text": "다음에 공원에 가시면 오리 주변을 자세히 관찰해 보세요.", "translation": "Next time you go to a park, try closely observing the area around a duck.", "vocab": [{"ko": "자세히", "en": "carefully/in detail"}, {"ko": "관찰하다", "en": "to observe"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)시- (honorific)", "exp": "shows respect to the listener. 가다 → 가시다 → 가시면 = \"if you go\".", "example_in_sentence": "가시면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어 보다", "exp": "Attempt/try marker: ''try to/attempt to ~''; 관찰하다 + ~어 보세요 (please try observing).", "example_in_sentence": "관찰해 보세요"}]}, {"text": "분명 재미있는 광경을 발견할 수 있을 거예요.", "translation": "You will definitely be able to discover an interesting sight.", "vocab": [{"ko": "분명", "en": "definitely/surely"}, {"ko": "광경", "en": "sight/scene"}, {"ko": "발견하다", "en": "to discover"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄹ 것이다", "exp": "Future tense/prediction marker; 발견할 수 있다 + ~ㄹ 거예요 (will be able to discover).", "example_in_sentence": "발견할 수 있을 거예요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "최근", "en": "recently", "note": ""}, {"ko": "신기하다", "en": "to be amazing; fascinating", "note": ""}, {"ko": "화제", "en": "topic/subject of discussion", "note": ""}, {"ko": "마리", "en": "counter for animals", "note": ""}, {"ko": "헤엄치다", "en": "to swim", "note": ""}, {"ko": "수많다", "en": "to be numerous", "note": ""}, {"ko": "따라다니다", "en": "to follow around", "note": ""}, {"ko": "현상", "en": "phenomenon", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일어나다", "en": "to occur/happen", "note": ""}, {"ko": "벌레", "en": "insect/bug", "note": ""}, {"ko": "조각", "en": "piece/fragment", "note": ""}, {"ko": "떨어지다", "en": "to fall/drop", "note": ""}, {"ko": "먹이", "en": "food/bait", "note": ""}, {"ko": "찾다", "en": "to search/look for", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert", "note": ""}, {"ko": "공생", "en": "symbiosis", "note": ""}, {"ko": "관계", "en": "relationship", "note": ""}, {"ko": "제공하다", "en": "to provide", "note": ""}, {"ko": "깨끗하다", "en": "to be clean", "note": ""}, {"ko": "협력", "en": "cooperation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "흥미롭다", "en": "to be interesting", "note": ""}, {"ko": "연못", "en": "pond", "note": ""}, {"ko": "호수", "en": "lake", "note": ""}, {"ko": "종종", "en": "often", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자세히", "en": "carefully/in detail", "note": ""}, {"ko": "관찰하다", "en": "to observe", "note": ""}, {"ko": "분명", "en": "definitely/surely", "note": ""}, {"ko": "광경", "en": "sight/scene", "note": ""}, {"ko": "발견하다", "en": "to discover", "note": ""}, {"word": "공생 관계", "reading": "gongsaeng gwangye", "meaning": "symbiotic relationship", "context": "전문가들은 이것을 ''공생 관계''라고 설명해요"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~고 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp"