Attempt/try marker: ''try to/attempt to ~''; 관찰하다 + ~어 보세요 (please try observing).", "ex_ko": "다음에 공원에 가시면 오리 주변을 자세히 관찰해 보세요.", "ex_en": "Next time you go to a park, try closely observing the area around a duck."}, {"name": "~ㄹ 것이다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Future tense/prediction marker; 발견할 수 있다 + ~ㄹ 거예요 (will be able to discover).", "ex_ko": "분명 재미있는 광경을 발견할 수 있을 거예요.", "ex_en": "You will definitely be able to discover an interesting sight."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mofqmezs2q4x' and md5(translation) = 'fbcdd99d9673e77e423de0beeabde3b5';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["A photo of Hitler from Nazi Germany wearing a special outfit in 1936 has become a topic of discussion. He wore a custom-made kimono gifted by the Japanese ambassador.", "This kimono was made to commemorate the diplomatic cooperation between Nazi Germany and Japan. At that time, the two countries were becoming politically closer.", "The kimono is a traditional Japanese garment with special significance. It was very rare for a foreign political leader to wear a kimono.", "This photograph is a historical document showing the international political situation of the 1930s. It helps us understand the relationship between Germany and Japan at that time."], "sentences": [{"text": "1936년 독일의 히틀러가 특별한 옷을 입은 사진이 화제가 되고 있어요.", "translation": "A photograph of Adolf Hitler of Germany wearing special clothing in 1936 is becoming a hot topic.", "vocab": [{"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special"}, {"ko": "화제", "en": "topic; subject of discussion"}, {"ko": "되다", "en": "to become"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "describes a noun with a past action. 입다 → 입은 사진 = \"a photo of (him) wearing\".", "example_in_sentence": "입은 사진"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있어요 (progressive aspect)", "exp": "Indicates ongoing or habitual action in present. Shows continuous state of ''becoming a topic''.", "example_in_sentence": "화제가 되고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "그는 일본 대사가 선물한 맞춤 제작 기모노를 입었습니다.", "translation": "He wore a custom-made kimono gifted by the Japanese ambassador.", "vocab": [{"ko": "대사", "en": "ambassador"}, {"ko": "선물하다", "en": "to gift; to give as a present"}, {"ko": "맞춤 제작", "en": "custom-made"}, {"ko": "기모노", "en": "kimono"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "describes a noun with a past action. 선물하다 → 선물한 기모노 = \"a kimono (that he) gave as a gift\".", "example_in_sentence": "선물한 맞춤 제작 기모노"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었습니다 (past tense, formal)", "exp": "Past tense in formal/written register. 입다 → 입었습니다.", "example_in_sentence": "입었습니다"}]}, {"text": "이 기모노는 나치 독일과 일본의 외교적 협력을 기념하기 위해 만들어졌어요.", "translation": "This kimono was made to commemorate the diplomatic cooperation between Nazi Germany and Japan.", "vocab": [{"ko": "나치", "en": "Nazi"}, {"ko": "외교적", "en": "diplomatic"}, {"ko": "협력", "en": "cooperation"}, {"ko": "기념하다", "en": "to commemorate"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 위해 (purpose/reason connective)", "exp": "Expresses purpose or intention: ''in order to'' or ''for the purpose of''. 기념하다 → 기념하기.", "example_in_sentence": "기념하기 위해"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어졌어요 (passive voice, past)", "exp": "Passive past tense. 만들다 → 만들어지다 → 만들어졌어요. Shows the kimono was created by someone.", "example_in_sentence": "만들어졌어요"}]}, {"text": "당시 두 나라는 정치적으로 가까워지고 있었습니다.", "translation": "At that time, the two countries were becoming politically closer.", "vocab": [{"ko": "당시", "en": "at that time; then"}, {"ko": "정치적", "en": "political; politically"}, {"ko": "가까워지다", "en": "to become close; to draw near"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있었습니다 (progressive aspect, past)", "exp": "Past progressive: shows an action that was ongoing in the past. 가까워지다 → 가까워지고 있었습니다.", "example_in_sentence": "가까워지고 있었습니다"}]}, {"text": "기모노는 일본의 전통 의상으로 특별한 의미가 있어요.", "translation": "The kimono is Japan''s traditional garment and has special significance.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전통", "en": "tradition"}, {"ko": "의상", "en": "garment; clothing"}, {"ko": "의미", "en": "meaning; significance"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~으로 (as; in the capacity of)", "exp": "Marks a role or category. Here, 기모노 is identified as 전통 의상 (traditional garment).", "example_in_sentence": "전통 의상으로"}]}, {"text": "외국 정치 지도자가 기모노를 입는 것은 매우 드문 일이었습니다.", "translation": "It was very rare for a foreign political leader to wear a kimono.", "vocab": [{"ko": "외국", "en": "foreign country"}, {"ko": "정치", "en": "politics"}, {"ko": "지도자", "en": "leader"}, {"ko": "드물다", "en": "to be rare; to be uncommon"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것 (nominalization)", "exp": "Converts a clause into a noun phrase. 입다 → 입는 것. Here, the action ''wearing a kimono'' becomes the subject.", "example_in_sentence": "기모노를 입는 것"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (adjective modifier)", "exp": "adjective before a noun; a stem-final ㄹ drops. 드물다 → 드문 일 = \"a rare thing\".", "example_in_sentence": "드문 일"}]}, {"text": "이 사진은 1930년대 국제 정치 상황을 보여주는 역사적 자료예요.", "translation": "This photograph is historical material that shows the international political situation of the 1930s.", "vocab": [{"ko": "국제", "en": "international"}, {"ko": "상황", "en": "situation; circumstances"}, {"ko": "보여주다", "en": "to show; to display"}, {"ko": "자료", "en": "material; data; resource"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present participle modifier)", "exp": "Modifies the noun 자료. 보여주다 → 보여주는 (that shows). Describes what kind of material it is.", "example_in_sentence": "보여주는 역사적 자료"}]}, {"text": "당시 독일과 일본의 관계를 이해하는 데 도움이 됩니다.", "translation": "It helps in understanding the relationship between Germany and Japan at that time.", "vocab": [{"ko": "관계", "en": "relationship"}, {"ko": "이해하다", "en": "to understand"}, {"ko": "도움", "en": "help; assistance"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 데 (in V-ing)", "exp": "names what something helps with. 이해하다 → 이해하는 데 도움이 되다 = \"to help in understanding\".", "example_in_sentence": "이해하는 데"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "도움이 되다 (to be helpful; to assist)", "exp": "Collocation expressing usefulness or benefit. Often follows ~는 데 or ~에.", "example_in_sentence": "도움이 됩니다"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "화제", "en": "topic; subject of discussion", "note": ""}, {"ko": "되다", "en": "to become", "note": ""}, {"ko": "대사", "en": "ambassador", "note": ""}, {"ko": "선물하다", "en": "to gift; to give as a present", "note": ""}, {"ko": "맞춤 제작", "en": "custom-made", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기모노", "en": "kimono", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나치", "en": "Nazi", "note": ""}, {"ko": "외교적", "en": "diplomatic", "note": ""}, {"ko": "협력", "en": "cooperation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기념하다", "en": "to commemorate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "당시", "en": "at that time; then", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정치적", "en": "political; politically", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가까워지다", "en": "to become close; to draw near", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전통", "en": "tradition", "note": ""}, {"ko": "의상", "en": "garment; clothing", "note": ""}, {"ko": "의미", "en": "meaning; significance", "note": ""}, {"ko": "외국", "en": "foreign country", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정치", "en": "politics", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지도자", "en": "leader", "note": ""}, {"ko": "드물다", "en": "to be rare; to be uncommon", "note": ""}, {"ko": "국제", "en": "international", "note": ""}, {"ko": "상황", "en": "situation; circumstances", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보여주다", "en": "to show; to display", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자료", "en": "material; data; resource", "note": ""}, {"ko": "관계", "en": "relationship", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이해하다", "en": "to understand", "note": ""}, {"ko": "도움", "en": "help; assistance", "note": ""}, {"word": "전통 의상", "reading": "jeongtong uisang", "meaning": "traditional clothing; traditional garment", "context": "기모노는 일본의 전통 의상으로 특별한 의미가 있어요"}, {"word": "사진", "reading": "sajin", "meaning": "photograph; picture", "context": "히틀러가 특별한 옷을 입은 사진이 화제가 되고 있어요"}, {"word": "역사적", "reading": "yeoksajok", "meaning": "historical; pertaining to history", "context": "이 사진은 1930년대 국제 정치 상황을 보여주는 역사적 자료예요"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "describes a noun with a past action. 선물하다 → 선물한 기모노 = \"a kimono (that he) gave as a gift\".", "ex_ko": "1936년 독일의 히틀러가 특별한 옷을 입은 사진이 화제가 되고 있어요.", "ex_en": "A photograph of Adolf Hitler of Germany wearing special clothing in 1936 is becoming a hot topic."}, {"name": "~고 있어요 (progressive aspect)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Indicates ongoing or habitual action in present. Shows continuous state of ''becoming a topic''.", "ex_ko": "1936년 독일의 히틀러가 특별한 옷을 입은 사진이 화제가 되고 있어요.", "ex_en": "A photograph of Adolf Hitler of Germany wearing special clothing in 1936 is becoming a hot topic."}, {"name": "~았/었습니다 (past tense, formal)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past tense in formal/written register. 입다 → 입었습니다.", "ex_ko": "그는 일본 대사가 선물한 맞춤 제작 기모노를 입었습니다.", "ex_en": "He wore a custom-made kimono gifted by the Japanese ambassador."}, {"name": "~기 위해 (purpose/reason connective)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Expresses purpose or intention: ''in order to'' or ''for the purpose of''. 기념하다 → 기념하기.", "ex_ko": "이 기모노는 나치 독일과 일본의 외교적 협력을 기념하기 위해 만들어졌어요.", "ex_en": "This kimono was made to commemorate the diplomatic cooperation between Nazi Germany and Japan."}, {"name": "~아/어졌어요 (passive voice, past)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Passive past tense. 만들다 → 만들어지다 → 만들어졌어요. Shows the kimono was created by someone.", "ex_ko": "이 기모노는 나치 독일과 일본의 외교적 협력을 기념하기 위해 만들어졌어요.", "ex_en": "This kimono was made to commemorate the diplomatic cooperation between Nazi Germany and Japan."}, {"name": "~고 있었습니다 (progressive aspect, past)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past progressive: shows an action that was ongoing in the past. 가까워지다 → 가까워지고 있었습니다.", "ex_ko": "당시 두 나라는 정치적으로 가까워지고 있었습니다.", "ex_en": "At that time, the two countries were becoming politically closer."}, {"name": "~으로 (as; in the capacity of)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Marks a role or category. Here, 기모노 is identified as 전통 의상 (traditional garment).", "ex_ko": "기모노는 일본의 전통 의상으로 특별한 의미가 있어요.", "ex_en": "The kimono is Japan''s traditional garment and has special significance."}, {"name": "~는 것 (nominalization)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Converts a clause into a noun phrase. 입다 → 입는 것. Here, the action ''wearing a kimono'' becomes the subject.", "ex_ko": "외국 정치 지도자가 기모노를 입는 것은 매우 드문 일이었습니다.", "ex_en": "It was very rare for a foreign political leader to wear a kimono."}, {"name": "~는 (present participle modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Modifies the noun 자료. 보여주다 → 보여주는 (that shows). Describes what kind of material it is.", "ex_ko": "이 사진은 1930년대 국제 정치 상황을 보여주는 역사적 자료예요.", "ex_en": "This photograph is historical material that shows the international political situation of the 1930s."}, {"name": "~는 데 (in V-ing)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "names what something helps with. 이해하다 → 이해하는 데 도움이 되다 = \"to help in understanding\".", "ex_ko": "당시 독일과 일본의 관계를 이해하는 데 도움이 됩니다.", "ex_en": "It helps in understanding the relationship between Germany and Japan at that time."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mofqn23002xf' and md5(translation) = '6cc83136f0a2b9d1febcff49822aab02';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Quetzalcoatlus Northropi was the largest flying animal ever discovered. This giant pterosaur (flying dinosaur) lived approximately 70 million years ago.", "In recently released photos, you can get a real sense of this animal''s size. When compared to a woman who is 1.6 meters tall, you can understand how remarkable the Quetzalcoatlus''s size was. When it spread its wings, they were said to be over 10 meters long.", "This pterosaur was as tall as a modern-day giraffe. However, its weight was relatively light, which allowed it to fly in the sky. It mainly hunted and ate fish and small animals.", "Scientists continue to research how such a giant animal was able to fly. The Quetzalcoatlus can be said to have been the king of the sky during the age of dinosaurs."], "sentences": [{"text": "케찰코아틀루스 노르트로피(Quetzalcoatlus Northropi)는 지금까지 발견된 것 중 가장 큰 날아다니는 동물이었어요.", "translation": "Quetzalcoatlus Northropi was the largest flying animal ever discovered.", "vocab": [{"ko": "발견되다", "en": "to be discovered"}, {"ko": "날아다니다", "en": "to fly around"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 것 중 (among those that ~)", "exp": "picks one from a group. 발견되다 → 발견된 것 중 가장 큰 = \"the biggest of those discovered\".", "example_in_sentence": "발견된 것 중"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense informal polite)", "exp": "Marks past tense in casual polite register. 이다 (be) → 이었어요.", "example_in_sentence": "이었어요"}]}, {"text": "이 거대한 익룡(날아다니는 공룡)은 약 7천만 년 전에 살았습니다.", "translation": "This giant pterosaur (flying dinosaur) lived approximately 70 million years ago.", "vocab": [{"ko": "거대하다", "en": "to be huge/giant"}, {"ko": "익룡", "en": "pterosaur"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었습니다 (past formal)", "exp": "past formal-polite. 살다 → 살았습니다 = \"lived\".", "example_in_sentence": "살았습니다"}]}, {"text": "최근 공개된 사진에서는 이 동물의 크기를 실감할 수 있어요.", "translation": "In recently released photographs, you can actually grasp the size of this animal.", "vocab": [{"ko": "공개되다", "en": "to be released/disclosed"}, {"ko": "실감하다", "en": "to grasp/feel concretely"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다 (can)", "exp": "possibility. 실감하다 → 실감할 수 있어요 = \"can really feel\".", "example_in_sentence": "실감할 수 있어요"}]}, {"text": "키 1.6미터인 여성과 비교했을 때, 케찰코아틀루스의 크기가 얼마나 놀라운지 알 수 있습니다.", "translation": "When compared with a 1.6-meter-tall woman, you can understand how remarkable the size of Quetzalcoatlus was.", "vocab": [{"ko": "비교하다", "en": "to compare"}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be remarkable; astonishing"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~았/었을 때 (when ~ did)", "exp": "when, for a completed action. 비교하다 → 비교했을 때 = \"when compared\".", "example_in_sentence": "비교했을 때"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ지 (how / whether)", "exp": "indirect question. 놀랍다 → 놀라운지 (ㅂ-irregular); 얼마나 놀라운지 알다 = \"to see how amazing (it is)\".", "example_in_sentence": "놀라운지"}]}, {"text": "날개를 펼치면 무려 10미터가 넘었다고 해요.", "translation": "When the wings were spread, they apparently exceeded 10 meters.", "vocab": [{"ko": "날개", "en": "wing"}, {"ko": "펼치다", "en": "to spread/unfold"}, {"ko": "넘다", "en": "to exceed/go over"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면 (if/when)", "exp": "condition. 펼치다 → 펼치면 = \"when (it) spreads (its wings)\".", "example_in_sentence": "펼치면"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~았/었다고 하다 (they say ~ did)", "exp": "hearsay about the past. 넘다 → 넘었다고 해요 = \"reportedly exceeded\".", "example_in_sentence": "넘었다고 해요"}]}, {"text": "이 익룡은 현재의 기린만큼 키가 컸어요.", "translation": "This pterosaur was as tall as a modern giraffe.", "vocab": [{"ko": "기린", "en": "giraffe"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~만큼 (as much as; as...as)", "exp": "Marks comparison of degree or extent. Attaches to noun.", "example_in_sentence": "기린만큼"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense informal polite)", "exp": "Marks past tense. 크다 → 컸어요.", "example_in_sentence": "컸어요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 무게는 비교적 가벼워서 하늘을 날 수 있었습니다.", "translation": "However, its weight was relatively light, so it was able to fly in the sky.", "vocab": [{"ko": "무게", "en": "weight"}, {"ko": "비교적", "en": "relatively/comparatively"}, {"ko": "가볍다", "en": "to be light"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~어/아서 (causal/connective)", "exp": "Connects clauses with cause-and-effect relationship. 가볍다 → 가벼워서.", "example_in_sentence": "가벼워서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄹ 수 있다 (possibility/ability)", "exp": "Expresses ability. 날다 → 날 수 있었습니다.", "example_in_sentence": "날 수 있었습니다"}]}, {"text": "주로 물고기나 작은 동물을 잡아먹고 살았어요.", "translation": "It primarily lived by hunting and eating fish and small animals.", "vocab": [{"ko": "주로", "en": "mainly/primarily"}, {"ko": "잡아먹다", "en": "to catch and eat"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 (sequential connective)", "exp": "Connects sequential actions. 잡아먹다 → 잡아먹고.", "example_in_sentence": "잡아먹고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past tense informal polite)", "exp": "Marks past tense. 살다 → 살았어요.", "example_in_sentence": "살았어요"}]}, {"text": "과학자들은 이런 거대한 동물이 어떻게 날 수 있었는지 계속 연구하고 있어요.", "translation": "Scientists are continually researching how such a giant animal was able to fly.", "vocab": [{"ko": "과학자", "en": "scientist"}, {"ko": "연구하다", "en": "to research/study"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는지 (how / whether)", "exp": "indirect question. 날 수 있었다 → 날 수 있었는지 = \"how (it) was able to fly\".", "example_in_sentence": "날 수 있었는지"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다 (progressive aspect)", "exp": "Marks ongoing/continuous action. 연구하다 → 연구하고 있어요.", "example_in_sentence": "연구하고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "케찰코아틀루스는 공룡 시대 하늘의 왕이었다고 할 수 있습니다.", "translation": "Quetzalcoatlus can be said to have been the king of the sky in the age of dinosaurs.", "vocab": [], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~다고 할 수 있다 (can be said to; it can be said that)", "exp": "Expresses a conclusion or assertion with some qualification. 이다 → 이었다고 할 수 있다.", "example_in_sentence": "이었다고 할 수 있습니다"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "발견되다", "en": "to be discovered", "note": ""}, {"ko": "날아다니다", "en": "to fly around", "note": ""}, {"ko": "거대하다", "en": "to be huge/giant", "note": ""}, {"ko": "익룡", "en": "pterosaur", "note": ""}, {"ko": "공개되다", "en": "to be released/disclosed", "note": ""}, {"ko": "실감하다", "en": "to grasp/feel concretely", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비교하다", "en": "to compare", "note": ""}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be remarkable; astonishing", "note": ""}, {"ko": "날개", "en": "wing", "note": ""}, {"ko": "펼치다", "en": "to spread/unfold", "note": ""}, {"ko": "넘다", "en": "to exceed/go over", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기린", "en": "giraffe", "note": ""}, {"ko": "무게", "en": "weight", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비교적", "en": "relatively/comparatively", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가볍다", "en": "to be light", "note": ""}, {"ko": "주로", "en": "mainly/primarily", "note": ""}, {"ko": "잡아먹다", "en": "to catch and eat", "note": ""}, {"ko": "과학자", "en": "scientist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "연구하다", "en": "to research/study", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(으)ㄴ 것 중 (among those that ~)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "picks one from a group. 발견되다 → 발견된 것 중 가장 큰 = \"the biggest of those discovered\".", "ex_ko": "케찰코아틀루스 노르트로피(Quetzalcoatlus Northropi)는 지금까지 발견된 것 중 가장 큰 날아다니는 동물이었어요.", "ex_en": "Quetzalcoatlus Northropi was the largest flying animal ever discovered."}, {"name": "~았/었어요 (past tense informal polite)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Marks past tense in casual polite register. 이다 (be) → 이었어요.", "ex_ko": "케찰코아틀루스 노르트로피(Quetzalcoatlus Northropi)는 지금까지 발견된 것 중 가장 큰 날아다니는 동물이었어요.", "ex_en": "Quetzalcoatlus Northropi was the largest flying animal ever discovered."}, {"name": "~았/었습니다 (past formal)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "past formal-polite. 살다 → 살았습니다 = \"lived\".", "ex_ko": "이 거대한 익룡(날아다니는 공룡)은 약 7천만 년 전에 살았습니다.", "ex_en": "This giant pterosaur (flying dinosaur) lived approximately 70 million years ago."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다 (can)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "possibility. 실감하다 → 실감할 수 있어요 = \"can really feel\".", "ex_ko": "최근 공개된 사진에서는 이 동물의 크기를 실감할 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "In recently released photographs, you can actually grasp the size of this animal."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ지 (how / whether)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "indirect question. 놀랍다 → 놀라운지 (ㅂ-irregular); 얼마나 놀라운지 알다 = \"to see how amazing (it is)\".", "ex_ko": "키 1.6미터인 여성과 비교했을 때, 케찰코아틀루스의 크기가 얼마나 놀라운지 알 수 있습니다.", "ex_en": "When compared with a 1.6-meter-tall woman, you can understand how remarkable the size of Quetzalcoatlus was."}, {"name": "~(으)면 (if/when)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "condition. 펼치다 → 펼치면 = \"when (it) spreads (its wings)\".", "ex_ko": "날개를 펼치면 무려 10미터가 넘었다고 해요.", "ex_en": "When the wings were spread, they apparently exceeded 10 meters."}, {"name": "~어/아서 (causal/connective)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Connects clauses with cause-and-effect relationship. 가볍다 → 가벼워서.", "ex_ko": "하지만 무게는 비교적 가벼워서 하늘을 날 수 있었습니다.", "ex_en": "However, its weight was relatively light, so it was able to fly in the sky."}, {"name": "~ㄹ 수 있다 (possibility/ability)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Expresses ability. 날다 → 날 수 있었습니다.", "ex_ko": "하지만 무게는 비교적 가벼워서 하늘을 날 수 있었습니다.", "ex_en": "However, its weight was relatively light, so it was able to fly in the sky."}, {"name": "~고 (sequential connective)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Connects sequential actions. 잡아먹다 → 잡아먹고.", "ex_ko": "주로 물고기나 작은 동물을 잡아먹고 살았어요.", "ex_en": "It primarily lived by hunting and eating fish and small animals."}, {"name": "~는지 (how / whether)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "indirect question. 날 수 있었다 → 날 수 있었는지 = \"how (it) was able to fly\".", "ex_ko": "과학자들은 이런 거대한 동물이 어떻게 날 수 있었는지 계속 연구하고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Scientists are continually researching how such a giant animal was able to fly."}, {"name": "~고 있다 (progressive aspect)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Marks ongoing/continuous action. 연구하다 → 연구하고 있어요.", "ex_ko": "과학자들은 이런 거대한 동물이 어떻게 날 수 있었는지 계속 연구하고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Scientists are continually researching how such a giant animal was able to fly."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mofqnvumyj96' and md5(translation) = '7a4a81bc1f2cb90efb7573c241baad39';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Interesting leopard behavior was observed in African wildlife. A female leopard woke up a sleeping male leopard and initiated mating behavior.", "Wildlife experts explain that this behavior is natural. They say that when it''s mating season for leopards, the female sends a signal to the male first.", "This video received great attention online. Many people were amazed by the natural behavior of wildlife. Leopards usually live alone, but during mating season they spend time together.", "Experts say that such observations help in leopard ecology research. This is because it''s not easy to directly see leopard behavior in the wild."], "sentences": [{"text": "아프리카 야생에서 흥미로운 표범 행동이 관찰됐어요.", "translation": "Interesting leopard behavior has been observed in African wilderness.", "vocab": [{"ko": "야생", "en": "wilderness"}, {"ko": "흥미롭다", "en": "to be interesting"}, {"ko": "표범", "en": "leopard"}, {"ko": "관찰되다", "en": "to be observed"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense suffix indicating completed action in casual polite form. 관찰되다 (to be observed) → 관찰됐어요 (was observed).", "example_in_sentence": "관찰됐어요"}]}, {"text": "암컷 표범이 잠자고 있던 수컷 표범을 깨워서 짝짓기 의식을 시작했습니다.", "translation": "A female leopard woke a sleeping male leopard and started a mating ritual.", "vocab": [{"ko": "암컷", "en": "female"}, {"ko": "잠자다", "en": "to sleep"}, {"ko": "수컷", "en": "male"}, {"ko": "깨우다", "en": "to wake up"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~던", "exp": "Retrospective aspect marker describing an ongoing or habitual state in the past. 잠자다 → 잠자고 있던 (that was sleeping).", "example_in_sentence": "잠자고 있던"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어서", "exp": "Connective suffix expressing sequential action (and then). 깨우다 → 깨워서 (woke up and [then]).", "example_in_sentence": "깨워서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았습니다", "exp": "Past tense in formal polite style. 시작하다 → 시작했습니다 (initiated).", "example_in_sentence": "시작했습니다"}]}, {"text": "야생동물 전문가들은 이런 행동이 자연스럽다고 설명해요.", "translation": "Wildlife experts explain that such behavior is natural.", "vocab": [{"ko": "야생동물", "en": "wildlife"}, {"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert"}, {"ko": "자연스럽다", "en": "to be natural"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~다고 설명하다", "exp": "Quotative ~다고 with verb 설명하다 (to explain). Reports or explains that something is a certain way.", "example_in_sentence": "자연스럽다고 설명해요"}]}, {"text": "표범의 짝짓기 시기가 되면 암컷이 먼저 수컷에게 신호를 보낸다고 합니다.", "translation": "When mating season comes for leopards, it is said that the female sends a signal to the male first.", "vocab": [{"ko": "짝짓기", "en": "mating"}, {"ko": "시기", "en": "season; time"}, {"ko": "신호", "en": "signal"}, {"ko": "보내다", "en": "to send"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면 (when)", "exp": "condition or time. 되다 → 되면 = \"when (the season) comes\".", "example_in_sentence": "시기가 되면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ다고 하다", "exp": "Reported speech marker. 보내다 → 보낸다고 합니다 (it is said that [subject] sends).", "example_in_sentence": "보낸다고 합니다"}]}, {"text": "이 영상은 온라인에서 큰 관심을 받았어요.", "translation": "This video received great interest online.", "vocab": [{"ko": "영상", "en": "video"}, {"ko": "온라인", "en": "online"}, {"ko": "관심", "en": "interest"}, {"ko": "받다", "en": "to receive"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았어요", "exp": "Past tense in casual polite form. 받다 → 받았어요 (received).", "example_in_sentence": "받았어요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "관심을 받다", "exp": "Collocation meaning ''to receive/attract interest or attention.'' Object 관심 + particle 을 + verb 받다.", "example_in_sentence": "큰 관심을 받았어요"}]}, {"text": "많은 사람들이 야생동물의 자연스러운 행동에 놀라워했습니다.", "translation": "Many people were amazed at the natural behavior of wildlife.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사람", "en": "person"}, {"ko": "야생동물", "en": "wildlife"}, {"ko": "자연스럽다", "en": "natural"}, {"ko": "행동", "en": "behavior"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았습니다", "exp": "Past tense in formal polite style. 놀라워하다 → 놀라워했습니다 (were amazed).", "example_in_sentence": "놀라워했습니다"}]}, {"text": "표범은 보통 혼자 생활하지만 짝짓기 시기에는 함께 시간을 보내요.", "translation": "Leopards usually live alone, but during mating season they spend time together.", "vocab": [{"ko": "표범", "en": "leopard"}, {"ko": "보통", "en": "usually"}, {"ko": "혼자", "en": "alone"}, {"ko": "생활하다", "en": "to live"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지만", "exp": "Connective particle expressing contrast. 생활하다 → 생활하지만 (live, but [contrast]).", "example_in_sentence": "생활하지만"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~에는", "exp": "Particle indicating a specific time or context (at/during). 시기 + 에는 (during [that] time).", "example_in_sentence": "시기에는"}]}, {"text": "전문가들은 이런 관찰이 표범 생태 연구에 도움이 된다고 말해요.", "translation": "Experts say that such observation is helpful for leopard ecology research.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert"}, {"ko": "관찰", "en": "observation"}, {"ko": "표범", "en": "leopard"}, {"ko": "생태", "en": "ecology"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~다고 말하다", "exp": "Quotative ~다고 with verb 말하다 (to say). Reports or states what someone says.", "example_in_sentence": "된다고 말해요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "도움이 되다", "exp": "Collocation meaning ''to be helpful/beneficial.'' Noun 도움 + particle 이 + verb 되다.", "example_in_sentence": "도움이 된다고"}]}, {"text": "야생에서 표범의 행동을 직접 보기는 쉽지 않기 때문입니다.", "translation": "It is because it is not easy to directly observe leopard behavior in the wild.", "vocab": [{"ko": "야생", "en": "wild"}, {"ko": "표범", "en": "leopard"}, {"ko": "행동", "en": "behavior"}, {"ko": "직접", "en": "directly"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기(는) (V-ing as a noun)", "exp": "~기 turns a verb into a noun; 는 adds contrast. 보다 → 보기는 쉽지 않다 = \"seeing (it) is not easy\".", "example_in_sentence": "보기는 쉽지 않기"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않다 (not)", "exp": "negation. 쉽다 → 쉽지 않다 = \"is not easy\".", "example_in_sentence": "쉽지 않기"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~기 때문이다 (it is because)", "exp": "gives the reason for the previous sentence. 않다 → 않기 때문입니다 = \"it is because (it is) not ~\".", "example_in_sentence": "않기 때문입니다"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "야생", "en": "wilderness", "note": ""}, {"ko": "흥미롭다", "en": "to be interesting", "note": ""}, {"ko": "표범", "en": "leopard", "note": ""}, {"ko": "관찰되다", "en": "to be observed", "note": ""}, {"ko": "암컷", "en": "female", "note": ""}, {"ko": "잠자다", "en": "to sleep", "note": ""}, {"ko": "수컷", "en": "male", "note": ""}, {"ko": "깨우다", "en": "to wake up", "note": ""}, {"ko": "야생동물", "en": "wildlife", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert", "note": ""}, {"ko": "자연스럽다", "en": "to be natural", "note": ""}, {"ko": "짝짓기", "en": "mating", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시기", "en": "season; time", "note": ""}, {"ko": "신호", "en": "signal", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보내다", "en": "to send", "note": ""}, {"ko": "영상", "en": "video", "note": ""}, {"ko": "온라인", "en": "online", "note": ""}, {"ko": "관심", "en": "interest", "note": ""}, {"ko": "받다", "en": "to receive", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person", "note": ""}, {"ko": "행동", "en": "behavior", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보통", "en": "usually", "note": ""}, {"ko": "혼자", "en": "alone", "note": ""}, {"ko": "생활하다", "en": "to live", "note": ""}, {"ko": "관찰", "en": "observation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "생태", "en": "ecology", "note": ""}, {"ko": "직접", "en": "directly", "note": ""}, {"word": "의식", "reading": "uisik", "meaning": "ceremony, ritual, conscious act", "context": "짝짓기 의식을 시작했습니다"}, {"word": "관심을 받다", "reading": "gwansim-eul batda", "meaning": "to receive attention, to attract interest", "context": "이 영상은 온라인에서 큰 관심을 받았어요"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~았/었어요", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past tense suffix indicating completed action in casual polite form. 관찰되다 (to be observed) → 관찰됐어요 (was observed).", "ex_ko": "아프리카 야생에서 흥미로운 표범 행동이 관찰됐어요.", "ex_en": "Interesting leopard behavior has been observed in African wilderness."}, {"name": "~던", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Retrospective aspect marker describing an ongoing or habitual state in the past. 잠자다 → 잠자고 있던 (that was sleeping).", "ex_ko": "암컷 표범이 잠자고 있던 수컷 표범을 깨워서 짝짓기 의식을 시작했습니다.", "ex_en": "A female leopard woke a sleeping male leopard and started a mating ritual."}, {"name": "~아/어서", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Connective suffix expressing sequential action (and then). 깨우다 → 깨워서 (woke up and [then]).", "ex_ko": "암컷 표범이 잠자고 있던 수컷 표범을 깨워서 짝짓기 의식을 시작했습니다.", "ex_en": "A female leopard woke a sleeping male leopard and started a mating ritual."}, {"name": "~았습니다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past tense in formal polite style. 놀라워하다 → 놀라워했습니다 (were amazed).", "ex_ko": "암컷 표범이 잠자고 있던 수컷 표범을 깨워서 짝짓기 의식을 시작했습니다.", "ex_en": "A female leopard woke a sleeping male leopard and started a mating ritual."}, {"name": "~다고 설명하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Quotative ~다고 with verb 설명하다 (to explain). Reports or explains that something is a certain way.", "ex_ko": "야생동물 전문가들은 이런 행동이 자연스럽다고 설명해요.", "ex_en": "Wildlife experts explain that such behavior is natural."}, {"name": "~(으)면 (when)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "condition or time. 되다 → 되면 = \"when (the season) comes\".", "ex_ko": "표범의 짝짓기 시기가 되면 암컷이 먼저 수컷에게 신호를 보낸다고 합니다.", "ex_en": "When mating season comes for leopards, it is said that the female sends a signal to the male first."}, {"name": "~ㄴ다고 하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Reported speech marker. 보내다 → 보낸다고 합니다 (it is said that [subject] sends).", "ex_ko": "표범의 짝짓기 시기가 되면 암컷이 먼저 수컷에게 신호를 보낸다고 합니다.", "ex_en": "When mating season comes for leopards, it is said that the female sends a signal to the male first."}, {"name": "~았어요", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past tense in casual polite form. 받다 → 받았어요 (received).", "ex_ko": "이 영상은 온라인에서 큰 관심을 받았어요.", "ex_en": "This video received great interest online."}, {"name": "~지만", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Connective particle expressing contrast. 생활하다 → 생활하지만 (live, but [contrast]).", "ex_ko": "표범은 보통 혼자 생활하지만 짝짓기 시기에는 함께 시간을 보내요.", "ex_en": "Leopards usually live alone, but during mating season they spend time together."}, {"name": "~다고 말하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Quotative ~다고 with verb 말하다 (to say). Reports or states what someone says.", "ex_ko": "전문가들은 이런 관찰이 표범 생태 연구에 도움이 된다고 말해요.", "ex_en": "Experts say that such observation is helpful for leopard ecology research."}, {"name": "~기(는) (V-ing as a noun)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "~기 turns a verb into a noun; 는 adds contrast. 보다 → 보기는 쉽지 않다 = \"seeing (it) is not easy\".", "ex_ko": "야생에서 표범의 행동을 직접 보기는 쉽지 않기 때문입니다.", "ex_en": "It is because it is not easy to directly observe leopard behavior in the wild."}, {"name": "~지 않다 (not)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "negation. 쉽다 → 쉽지 않다 = \"is not easy\".", "ex_ko": "야생에서 표범의 행동을 직접 보기는 쉽지 않기 때문입니다.", "ex_en": "It is because it is not easy to directly observe leopard behavior in the wild."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mofqoromcunm' and md5(translation) = 'd438ff8e3213533c1180da20ae92ca8e';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["A funny video has recently become a hot topic online. It contains people''s reactions when a remote control falls off a sofa.", "Many people are relating to this situation. When a remote control falls under a sofa, it becomes really difficult to find. Especially if it gets stuck in a narrow gap, it''s even more frustrating.", "Netizens are leaving funny comments saying ''I do the same thing.'' Some people said they use a smartphone app instead of a remote control.", "This everyday experience is drawing the attention of many people. It''s a small inconvenience, but it''s a common experience that everyone goes through."], "sentences": [{"text": "최근 온라인에서 재미있는 영상이 화제가 되고 있어요.", "translation": "Recently, an entertaining video has become a hot topic online.", "vocab": [{"ko": "최근", "en": "recently"}, {"ko": "화제", "en": "hot topic; issue"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있어요", "exp": "Progressive aspect marker indicating an ongoing action or state. Verb stem + 고 있다 conjugated to present polite form.", "example_in_sentence": "화제가 되고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "소파에서 리모컨이 떨어졌을 때 사람들의 반응을 담은 내용입니다.", "translation": "It is content that captures people''s reactions when a remote control falls from a sofa.", "vocab": [{"ko": "리모컨", "en": "remote control"}, {"ko": "떨어지다", "en": "to fall; to drop"}, {"ko": "반응", "en": "reaction; response"}, {"ko": "담다", "en": "to contain; to capture"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었을 때 (when ~ happened)", "exp": "when, for a completed event. 떨어지다 → 떨어졌을 때 = \"when (it) fell\".", "example_in_sentence": "떨어졌을 때"}]}, {"text": "많은 사람들이 이 상황에 공감하고 있어요.", "translation": "Many people are empathizing with this situation.", "vocab": [{"ko": "공감하다", "en": "to relate to; to sympathize"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있어요", "exp": "Progressive aspect marking an ongoing action. Verb stem + 고 있다 in present polite form.", "example_in_sentence": "공감하고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "리모컨이 소파 아래로 떨어지면 찾기가 정말 어려워져요.", "translation": "When a remote control falls under a sofa, finding it becomes really difficult.", "vocab": [{"ko": "아래", "en": "under; below"}, {"ko": "어렵다", "en": "to be difficult"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면 (if/when)", "exp": "condition. 떨어지다 → 떨어지면 = \"if/when (it) falls\".", "example_in_sentence": "떨어지면"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~ 아래로 (down under)", "exp": "아래 (below) + 로 (direction). 소파 → 소파 아래로 = \"(down) under the sofa\".", "example_in_sentence": "소파 아래로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어지다 (become)", "exp": "change of state. 어렵다 → 어려워지다 (ㅂ-irregular) → 어려워져요 = \"becomes difficult\".", "example_in_sentence": "어려워져요"}]}, {"text": "특히 좁은 틈 사이에 끼면 더욱 답답합니다.", "translation": "It is especially frustrating when it gets stuck in a narrow gap.", "vocab": [{"ko": "특히", "en": "especially; particularly"}, {"ko": "틈", "en": "gap; crack; crevice"}, {"ko": "끼다", "en": "to be stuck; to wedge"}, {"ko": "답답하다", "en": "to be frustrating; to be stuffy"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~ 사이에", "exp": "Locational expression marking space between two things. 사이 (between) + 에 (locative particle).", "example_in_sentence": "틈 사이에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면 (if/when)", "exp": "condition. 끼다 → 끼면 = \"if/when (it) gets stuck\".", "example_in_sentence": "끼면"}]}, {"text": "네티즌들은 \"나도 똑같다\"며 재미있는 댓글을 남기고 있어요.", "translation": "Netizens are leaving funny comments, saying \"Same here.\"", "vocab": [{"ko": "네티즌", "en": "netizen; internet user"}, {"ko": "똑같다", "en": "to be identical; to be the same"}, {"ko": "댓글", "en": "comment"}, {"ko": "남기다", "en": "to leave; to post"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~다며 (saying that)", "exp": "quotes what people say while doing something else. 똑같다 → 똑같다며 = \"saying (it''s) the same\".", "example_in_sentence": "\"나도 똑같다\"며"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있어요", "exp": "Progressive aspect marking ongoing action. Verb stem + 고 있다 in present polite form.", "example_in_sentence": "남기고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "어떤 사람은 리모컨 대신 스마트폰 앱을 사용한다고 했습니다.", "translation": "One person said they use a smartphone app instead of a remote control.", "vocab": [{"ko": "대신", "en": "instead of; in place of"}, {"ko": "앱", "en": "app; application"}, {"ko": "사용하다", "en": "to use"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ다고 하다", "exp": "Reported speech pattern. Verb in present declarative ~ㄴ다 + 고 하다 (say that). Reports what someone says.", "example_in_sentence": "사용한다고 했습니다"}]}, {"text": "이런 일상적인 경험이 많은 사람들의 관심을 끌고 있어요.", "translation": "Such everyday experiences are drawing the attention of many people.", "vocab": [{"ko": "일상적", "en": "everyday; ordinary"}, {"ko": "경험", "en": "experience"}, {"ko": "관심", "en": "interest; attention"}, {"ko": "끌다", "en": "to draw; to attract"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "관심을 끌다", "exp": "Verb+object collocation meaning ''to attract attention/interest''. 끌다 (draw) takes 관심 (interest) as its direct object.", "example_in_sentence": "관심을 끌고 있어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있어요", "exp": "Progressive aspect marking an ongoing action. Verb stem + 고 있다 in present polite form.", "example_in_sentence": "끌고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "작은 불편함이지만 모든 사람이 겪는 공통된 경험이기 때문입니다.", "translation": "It''s because, although it''s a small inconvenience, it''s a common experience that everyone goes through.", "vocab": [{"ko": "불편함", "en": "inconvenience; discomfort"}, {"ko": "겪다", "en": "to experience; to go through"}, {"ko": "공통되다", "en": "to be common; to be shared"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지만", "exp": "Concessive conjunction connecting contrasting clauses. Stem + 지만 (but; although). Links ''small inconvenience'' with ''common experience''.", "example_in_sentence": "불편함이지만"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 때문이다", "exp": "Causal expression. Nominalizer 기 + 때문 (reason/cause) + 이다. Explains the reason: ''because [everyone experiences it]''.", "example_in_sentence": "겪는 공통된 경험이기 때문입니다"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "최근", "en": "recently", "note": ""}, {"ko": "화제", "en": "hot topic; issue", "note": ""}, {"ko": "리모컨", "en": "remote control", "note": ""}, {"ko": "떨어지다", "en": "to fall; to drop", "note": ""}, {"ko": "반응", "en": "reaction; response", "note": ""}, {"ko": "담다", "en": "to contain; to capture", "note": ""}, {"ko": "공감하다", "en": "to relate to; to sympathize", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아래", "en": "under; below", "note": ""}, {"ko": "어렵다", "en": "to be difficult", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특히", "en": "especially; particularly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "틈", "en": "gap; crack; crevice", "note": ""}, {"ko": "끼다", "en": "to be stuck; to wedge", "note": ""}, {"ko": "답답하다", "en": "to be frustrating; to be stuffy", "note": ""}, {"ko": "네티즌", "en": "netizen; internet user", "note": ""}, {"ko": "똑같다", "en": "to be identical; to be the same", "note": ""}, {"ko": "댓글", "en": "comment", "note": ""}, {"ko": "남기다", "en": "to leave; to post", "note": ""}, {"ko": "대신", "en": "instead of; in place of", "note": ""}, {"ko": "앱", "en": "app; application", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사용하다", "en": "to use", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일상적", "en": "everyday; ordinary", "note": ""}, {"ko": "경험", "en": "experience", "note": ""}, {"ko": "관심", "en": "interest; attention", "note": ""}, {"ko": "끌다", "en": "to draw; to attract", "note": ""}, {"ko": "불편함", "en": "inconvenience; discomfort", "note": ""}, {"ko": "겪다", "en": "to experience; to go through", "note": ""}, {"ko": "공통되다", "en": "to be common; to be shared", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~고 있어요", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Progressive aspect marker indicating an ongoing action or state. Verb stem + 고 있다 conjugated to present polite form.", "ex_ko": "최근 온라인에서 재미있는 영상이 화제가 되고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Recently, an entertaining video has become a hot topic online."}, {"name": "~았/었을 때 (when ~ happened)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "when, for a completed event. 떨어지다 → 떨어졌을 때 = \"when (it) fell\".", "ex_ko": "소파에서 리모컨이 떨어졌을 때 사람들의 반응을 담은 내용입니다.", "ex_en": "It is content that captures people''s reactions when a remote control falls from a sofa."}, {"name": "~(으)면 (if/when)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "condition. 끼다 → 끼면 = \"if/when (it) gets stuck\".", "ex_ko": "리모컨이 소파 아래로 떨어지면 찾기가 정말 어려워져요.", "ex_en": "When a remote control falls under a sofa, finding it becomes really difficult."}, {"name": "~아/어지다 (become)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "change of state. 어렵다 → 어려워지다 (ㅂ-irregular) → 어려워져요 = \"becomes difficult\".", "ex_ko": "리모컨이 소파 아래로 떨어지면 찾기가 정말 어려워져요.", "ex_en": "When a remote control falls under a sofa, finding it becomes really difficult."}, {"name": "~다며 (saying that)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "quotes what people say while doing something else. 똑같다 → 똑같다며 = \"saying (it''s) the same\".", "ex_ko": "네티즌들은 \"나도 똑같다\"며 재미있는 댓글을 남기고 있어요.", "ex_en": "Netizens are leaving funny comments, saying \"Same here.\""}, {"name": "~ㄴ다고 하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Reported speech pattern. Verb in present declarative ~ㄴ다 + 고 하다 (say that). Reports what someone says.", "ex_ko": "어떤 사람은 리모컨 대신 스마트폰 앱을 사용한다고 했습니다.", "ex_en": "One person said they use a smartphone app instead of a remote control."}, {"name": "~지만", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Concessive conjunction connecting contrasting clauses. Stem + 지만 (but; although). Links ''small inconvenience'' with ''common experience''.", "ex_ko": "작은 불편함이지만 모든 사람이 겪는 공통된 경험이기 때문입니다.", "ex_en": "It''s because, although it''s a small inconvenience, it''s a common experience that everyone goes through."}, {"name": "~기 때문이다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Causal expression. Nominalizer 기 + 때문 (reason/cause) + 이다. Explains the reason: ''because [everyone experiences it]''.", "ex_ko": "작은 불편함이지만 모든 사람이 겪는 공통된 경험이기 때문입니다.", "ex_en": "It''s because, although it''s a small inconvenience, it''s a common experience that everyone goes through."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mofqpcmxshdf' and md5(translation) = 'd309b5edf714a5d20b568f12aa74f6cd';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Several stores in China have started using robots instead of human cashiers. These robots handle all checkout tasks from scanning products to processing payments.", "Robot cashiers operate using artificial intelligence (AI) technology. When a customer places a product, it automatically recognizes it and calculates the price. They can process cash, card, and mobile payments as well.", "Store operators cite labor cost savings and the ability to operate 24 hours as advantages. However, some customers say they miss the communication with people.", "In Korea, unmanned checkout counters are also increasing, but fully autonomous robot cashiers have not yet been introduced. There is growing interest in whether this technology will spread to our country in the future."], "sentences": [{"text": "중국의 여러 매장에서 사람 계산원 대신 로봇을 사용하기 시작했어요.", "translation": "Several stores in China have started using robots instead of human cashiers.", "vocab": [{"ko": "매장", "en": "store; shop"}, {"ko": "계산원", "en": "cashier"}, {"ko": "대신", "en": "instead of; in place of"}, {"ko": "로봇", "en": "robot"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 시작하다 (start V-ing)", "exp": "the start of an action. 사용하다 → 사용하기 시작했어요 = \"started using\".", "example_in_sentence": "사용하기 시작했어요"}]}, {"text": "이 로봇들은 상품 스캔부터 결제 처리까지 모든 계산 업무를 담당해요.", "translation": "These robots handle all checkout tasks from product scanning to payment processing.", "vocab": [{"ko": "상품", "en": "product; item"}, {"ko": "스캔", "en": "scan"}, {"ko": "결제", "en": "payment"}, {"ko": "담당하다", "en": "to be in charge of; handle"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~부터 ~까지", "exp": "Marks range or scope ''from...to''; used with time, space, or sequence. Places two boundary points to frame inclusive span.", "example_in_sentence": "상품 스캔부터 결제 처리까지"}]}, {"text": "로봇 계산원은 인공지능(AI) 기술을 활용해서 작동해요.", "translation": "The robot cashier operates by utilizing artificial intelligence technology.", "vocab": [{"ko": "인공지능", "en": "artificial intelligence; AI"}, {"ko": "기술", "en": "technology; technique"}, {"ko": "활용하다", "en": "to use; make use of"}, {"ko": "작동하다", "en": "to operate; work"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어서 (by, by means of)", "exp": "means. 활용하다 → 활용해서 = \"by using\".", "example_in_sentence": "기술을 활용해서"}]}, {"text": "고객이 상품을 올려놓으면 자동으로 인식하고 가격을 계산해줘요.", "translation": "When a customer places a product, it automatically recognizes it and calculates the price.", "vocab": [{"ko": "고객", "en": "customer; client"}, {"ko": "올려놓다", "en": "to place; to put down"}, {"ko": "인식하다", "en": "to recognize"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면 (when/if)", "exp": "condition. 올려놓다 → 올려놓으면 = \"when (a customer) puts (it) down\".", "example_in_sentence": "올려놓으면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "Coordinate connective linking sequential or related actions. Form: verb root + 고. Here joins two parallel actions: recognizes AND calculates.", "example_in_sentence": "인식하고 가격을 계산해줘요"}]}, {"text": "현금이나 카드, 모바일 결제도 모두 처리할 수 있어요.", "translation": "It can handle cash, card, and mobile payments.", "vocab": [{"ko": "현금", "en": "cash"}, {"ko": "카드", "en": "card"}, {"ko": "모바일 결제", "en": "mobile payment"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다 (can)", "exp": "ability. 처리하다 → 처리할 수 있어요 = \"can handle\".", "example_in_sentence": "처리할 수 있어요"}]}, {"text": "매장 운영자들은 인건비 절약과 24시간 운영이 가능하다는 점을 장점으로 꼽아요.", "translation": "Store operators cite savings on labor costs and the ability to operate 24 hours a day as advantages.", "vocab": [{"ko": "운영자", "en": "operator; manager"}, {"ko": "인건비", "en": "labor cost"}, {"ko": "절약", "en": "savings; economy"}, {"ko": "장점", "en": "advantage; strength"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~다는 점 (the fact that)", "exp": "turns a statement into a noun phrase. 가능하다 → 가능하다는 점 = \"the fact that (it) is possible\".", "example_in_sentence": "가능하다는 점을"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)로 (as)", "exp": "marks a role or status. 장점 → 장점으로 꼽다 = \"to name as an advantage\".", "example_in_sentence": "장점으로"}]}, {"text": "하지만 일부 고객들은 사람과의 소통이 없어서 아쉽다고 말해요.", "translation": "However, some customers say they find it regrettable that there is no interaction with people.", "vocab": [{"ko": "일부", "en": "some; a part"}, {"ko": "소통", "en": "communication; interaction"}, {"ko": "아쉽다", "en": "to be a pity; regrettable"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어서 (because)", "exp": "reason. 없다 → 없어서 = \"because there is no\".", "example_in_sentence": "없어서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다고 말해요", "exp": "Reported speech. Form: clause + ~다고 + 말하다. Marks indirect quotation of what someone says or claims.", "example_in_sentence": "아쉽다고 말해요"}]}, {"text": "한국에서도 무인 계산대가 늘어나고 있지만, 완전한 로봇 계산원은 아직 도입되지 않았어요.", "translation": "Self-checkout counters are increasing in Korea too, but fully robotic cashiers have not been introduced yet.", "vocab": [{"ko": "무인", "en": "unmanned; unattended"}, {"ko": "계산대", "en": "checkout counter"}, {"ko": "늘어나다", "en": "to increase; to grow"}, {"ko": "완전하다", "en": "to be complete; full"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있지만", "exp": "Progressive aspect (~고 있다) + contrastive connective (~지만). Marks ongoing action contrasted with following clause. Form: verb + 고 있지만.", "example_in_sentence": "늘어나고 있지만"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않았다 (did not)", "exp": "past negation. 도입되다 → 도입되지 않았어요 = \"has not been introduced\".", "example_in_sentence": "도입되지 않았어요"}]}, {"text": "앞으로 이런 기술이 우리나라에도 확산될지 관심이 모아져요.", "translation": "Interest is gathering on whether such technology will spread to our country in the future.", "vocab": [{"ko": "앞으로", "en": "from now on; in the future"}, {"ko": "기술", "en": "technology; technique"}, {"ko": "확산되다", "en": "to spread"}, {"ko": "모아지다", "en": "to gather; to be collected"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ지 (whether ~ will)", "exp": "an uncertain future, as an indirect question. 확산되다 → 확산될지 = \"whether (it) will spread\".", "example_in_sentence": "확산될지"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "관심이 모아지다", "exp": "Idiomatic collocation: ''attention/interest gathers/concentrates.'' Marks that focus or concern is directed toward a topic.", "example_in_sentence": "관심이 모아져요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "매장", "en": "store; shop", "note": ""}, {"ko": "계산원", "en": "cashier", "note": ""}, {"ko": "대신", "en": "instead of; in place of", "note": ""}, {"ko": "로봇", "en": "robot", "note": ""}, {"ko": "상품", "en": "product; item", "note": ""}, {"ko": "스캔", "en": "scan", "note": ""}, {"ko": "결제", "en": "payment", "note": ""}, {"ko": "담당하다", "en": "to be in charge of; handle", "note": ""}, {"ko": "인공지능", "en": "artificial intelligence; AI", "note": ""}, {"ko": "기술", "en": "technology; technique", "note": ""}, {"ko": "활용하다", "en": "to use; make use of", "note": ""}, {"ko": "작동하다", "en": "to operate; work", "note": ""}, {"ko": "고객", "en": "customer; client", "note": ""}, {"ko": "올려놓다", "en": "to place; to put down", "note": ""}, {"ko": "인식하다", "en": "to recognize", "note": ""}, {"ko": "현금", "en": "cash", "note": ""}, {"ko": "카드", "en": "card", "note": ""}, {"ko": "모바일 결제", "en": "mobile payment", "note": ""}, {"ko": "운영자", "en": "operator; manager", "note": ""}, {"ko": "인건비", "en": "labor cost", "note": ""}, {"ko": "절약", "en": "savings; economy", "note": ""}, {"ko": "장점", "en": "advantage; strength", "note": ""}, {"ko": "일부", "en": "some; a part", "note": ""}, {"ko": "소통", "en": "communication; interaction", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아쉽다", "en": "to be a pity; regrettable", "note": ""}, {"ko": "무인", "en": "unmanned; unattended", "note": ""}, {"ko": "계산대", "en": "checkout counter", "note": ""}, {"ko": "늘어나다", "en": "to increase; to grow", "note": ""}, {"ko": "완전하다", "en": "to be complete; full", "note": ""}, {"ko": "앞으로", "en": "from now on; in the future", "note": ""}, {"ko": "확산되다", "en": "to spread", "note": ""}, {"ko": "모아지다", "en": "to gather; to be collected", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~기 시작하다 (start V-ing)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "the start of an action. 사용하다 → 사용하기 시작했어요 = \"started using\".", "ex_ko": "중국의 여러 매장에서 사람 계산원 대신 로봇을 사용하기 시작했어요.", "ex_en": "Several stores in China have started using robots instead of human cashiers."}, {"name": "~아/어서 (by, by means of)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "reason. 없다 → 없어서 = \"because there is no\".", "ex_ko": "로봇 계산원은 인공지능(AI) 기술을 활용해서 작동해요.", "ex_en": "The robot cashier operates by utilizing artificial intelligence technology."}, {"name": "~(으)면 (when/if)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "condition. 올려놓다 → 올려놓으면 = \"when (a customer) puts (it) down\".", "ex_ko": "고객이 상품을 올려놓으면 자동으로 인식하고 가격을 계산해줘요.", "ex_en": "When a customer places a product, it automatically recognizes it and calculates the price."}, {"name": "~고", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Coordinate connective linking sequential or related actions. Form: verb root + 고. Here joins two parallel actions: recognizes AND calculates.", "ex_ko": "고객이 상품을 올려놓으면 자동으로 인식하고 가격을 계산해줘요.", "ex_en": "When a customer places a product, it automatically recognizes it and calculates the price."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다 (can)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "ability. 처리하다 → 처리할 수 있어요 = \"can handle\".", "ex_ko": "현금이나 카드, 모바일 결제도 모두 처리할 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "It can handle cash, card, and mobile payments."}, {"name": "~다는 점 (the fact that)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "turns a statement into a noun phrase. 가능하다 → 가능하다는 점 = \"the fact that (it) is possible\".", "ex_ko": "매장 운영자들은 인건비 절약과 24시간 운영이 가능하다는 점을 장점으로 꼽아요.", "ex_en": "Store operators cite savings on labor costs and the ability to operate 24 hours a day as advantages."}, {"name": "~(으)로 (as)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "marks a role or status. 장점 → 장점으로 꼽다 = \"to name as an advantage\".", "ex_ko": "매장 운영자들은 인건비 절약과 24시간 운영이 가능하다는 점을 장점으로 꼽아요.", "ex_en": "Store operators cite savings on labor costs and the ability to operate 24 hours a day as advantages."}, {"name": "~다고 말해요", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Reported speech. Form: clause + ~다고 + 말하다. Marks indirect quotation of what someone says or claims.", "ex_ko": "하지만 일부 고객들은 사람과의 소통이 없어서 아쉽다고 말해요.", "ex_en": "However, some customers say they find it regrettable that there is no interaction with people."}, {"name": "~고 있지만", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Progressive aspect (~고 있다) + contrastive connective (~지만). Marks ongoing action contrasted with following clause. Form: verb + 고 있지만.", "ex_ko": "한국에서도 무인 계산대가 늘어나고 있지만, 완전한 로봇 계산원은 아직 도입되지 않았어요.", "ex_en": "Self-checkout counters are increasing in Korea too, but fully robotic cashiers have not been introduced yet."}, {"name": "~지 않았다 (did not)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "past negation. 도입되다 → 도입되지 않았어요 = \"has not been introduced\".", "ex_ko": "한국에서도 무인 계산대가 늘어나고 있지만, 완전한 로봇 계산원은 아직 도입되지 않았어요.", "ex_en": "Self-checkout counters are increasing in Korea too, but fully robotic cashiers have not been introduced yet."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ지 (whether ~ will)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "an uncertain future, as an indirect question. 확산되다 → 확산될지 = \"whether (it) will spread\".", "ex_ko": "앞으로 이런 기술이 우리나라에도 확산될지 관심이 모아져요.", "ex_en": "Interest is gathering on whether such technology will spread to our country in the future."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mofqq2fftt3n' and md5(translation) = '860f70abe17dbf38bf039167cc8b4587';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["In the 1940s and 1950s, there were surprising advertisements in the United States. A famous cigarette brand called Marlboro used babies in their advertisements. This was a time when the health risks of cigarettes (the degree of harm to health) were not well known. Advertising companies tried to make cigarettes look like safe and healthy products. Babies symbolize purity and a healthy image. Marlboro tried to use this image to give the impression that their cigarettes were harmless. However, starting in the 1960s, the dangers of cigarettes began to be revealed. Currently, most countries ban this type of cigarette advertising. In Korea as well, cigarette advertising is strictly regulated.", "Korean Teacher Shortage Becomes Serious, School Classes Disrupted", "What is an \"anxiety bag\"? A Popular Trend", "The United States and China Resume Talks Over Trade Issues", "\"Talking Pig\" Becomes SNS Star", "Apple Greatly Improves iPhone Speed with New AI Chip"], "sentences": [{"text": "1940년대와 1950년대에 미국에서는 놀라운 광고가 있었어요.", "translation": "In the 1940s and 1950s, there were surprising advertisements in the United States.", "vocab": [{"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be surprising; astonishing"}, {"ko": "광고", "en": "advertisement"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense ending for statements. 있다 (to exist) → 있었어요 (there was/were).", "example_in_sentence": "있었어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서는", "exp": "Location particle 에서 + topic particle 는. Marks the place where action occurs, with topic emphasis.", "example_in_sentence": "미국에서는"}]}, {"text": "유명한 담배 브랜드인 말보로(Marlboro)가 아기들을 광고에 사용했습니다.", "translation": "The famous cigarette brand Marlboro used babies in advertisements.", "vocab": [{"ko": "유명하다", "en": "to be famous; well-known"}, {"ko": "담배", "en": "cigarette, tobacco"}, {"ko": "브랜드", "en": "brand"}, {"ko": "아기", "en": "baby"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~인 (that is N)", "exp": "noun-modifying form of 이다. 담배 브랜드인 말보로 = \"Marlboro, which is a cigarette brand\".", "example_in_sentence": "브랜드인 말보로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었습니다", "exp": "Past tense formal statement ending. 사용하다 (to use) → 사용했습니다.", "example_in_sentence": "사용했습니다"}]}, {"text": "이 시기는 담배의 건강 위험성(건강에 해로운 정도)이 잘 알려지지 않았던 때였어요.", "translation": "This period was a time when the health risks of cigarettes (the extent of harm to health) were not well known.", "vocab": [{"ko": "시기", "en": "period, time"}, {"ko": "위험성", "en": "risk, danger, hazard"}, {"ko": "해롭다", "en": "to be harmful"}, {"ko": "알려지다", "en": "to be known, to become known"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않다", "exp": "Negation with auxiliary verb. 알려지다 (to be known) → 알려지지 않다 (not to be known).", "example_in_sentence": "알려지지 않았던"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었던", "exp": "Past retrospective modifier. Marks 때 as a point in past time.", "example_in_sentence": "알려지지 않았던 때"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이었/였어요", "exp": "Past copula for descriptive statements. 때 (time) + 이다 → 때였어요 (was a time).", "example_in_sentence": "때였어요"}]}, {"text": "광고회사들은 담배를 안전하고 건강한 제품처럼 보이게 하려고 했습니다.", "translation": "Advertising companies tried to make cigarettes appear as safe and healthy products.", "vocab": [{"ko": "광고회사", "en": "advertising company, ad agency"}, {"ko": "안전하다", "en": "to be safe, safe"}, {"ko": "건강하다", "en": "to be healthy, healthy"}, {"ko": "제품", "en": "product"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 하다", "exp": "Causative auxiliary. 보이다 (to appear) + 게 하다 (make/cause to) = to make appear.", "example_in_sentence": "보이게 하려고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~려고 하다", "exp": "Intentional/prospective ending. Expresses intention or attempt to do something. 하다 → 하려고 했습니다.", "example_in_sentence": "하려고 했습니다"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~처럼", "exp": "Resemblance particle. Marks comparison: ''like'' or ''as if''.", "example_in_sentence": "제품처럼"}]}, {"text": "아기는 순수하고 건강한 이미지를 상징해요.", "translation": "Babies symbolize a pure and healthy image.", "vocab": [{"ko": "순수하다", "en": "to be pure, pure"}, {"ko": "이미지", "en": "image"}, {"ko": "상징하다", "en": "to symbolize, to represent"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고", "exp": "Coordinate conjunction. Connects two adjectives of equal weight: 순수하고 건강한.", "example_in_sentence": "순수하고 건강한"}]}, {"text": "말보로는 이런 이미지를 이용해서 자신들의 담배가 무해하다는 인상을 주려고 했습니다.", "translation": "Marlboro tried to give the impression that their cigarettes were harmless by using this kind of image.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이용하다", "en": "to use, to utilize"}, {"ko": "무해하다", "en": "to be harmless, harmless"}, {"ko": "인상", "en": "impression"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어서 (by means of)", "exp": "means. 이용하다 → 이용해서 = \"by using\".", "example_in_sentence": "이용해서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~다는", "exp": "Nominal subordinator. Nominalizes the clause: 무해하다 → 무해하다는 (the fact/idea that [it] is harmless).", "example_in_sentence": "무해하다는 인상"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~려고 하다", "exp": "Intentional prospective. 주다 → 주려고 했습니다 (tried to give).", "example_in_sentence": "주려고 했습니다"}]}, {"text": "하지만 1960년대부터 담배의 위험성이 밝혀지기 시작했어요.", "translation": "However, starting from the 1960s, the risks of cigarettes began to be revealed.", "vocab": [{"ko": "밝혀지다", "en": "to be revealed, to come to light, to be discovered"}, {"ko": "시작하다", "en": "to begin, to start"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~부터", "exp": "Starting-point particle. Marks the beginning of a time span: 1960년대 → 1960년대부터 (from the 1960s).", "example_in_sentence": "1960년대부터"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 시작하다", "exp": "Inchoative auxiliary. Marks the beginning of an action. 밝혀지다 → 밝혀지기 시작했어요 (began to be revealed).", "example_in_sentence": "밝혀지기 시작했어요"}]}, {"text": "현재는 대부분의 나라에서 이런 방식의 담배 광고를 금지하고 있습니다.", "translation": "Currently, most countries prohibit this type of cigarette advertisement.", "vocab": [{"ko": "현재", "en": "present, currently"}, {"ko": "대부분", "en": "majority, most"}, {"ko": "나라", "en": "country, nation"}, {"ko": "방식", "en": "method, way, manner"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive/continuous aspect. 금지하다 → 금지하고 있습니다 (are prohibiting, currently maintain prohibition).", "example_in_sentence": "금지하고 있습니다"}]}, {"text": "한국에서도 담배 광고는 엄격하게 규제되고 있어요.", "translation": "Cigarette advertisements are also strictly regulated in Korea.", "vocab": [{"ko": "엄격하다", "en": "to be strict, strict, rigorous"}, {"ko": "규제되다", "en": "to be regulated"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive/continuous passive. 규제되다 → 규제되고 있어요 (are being regulated).", "example_in_sentence": "규제되고 있어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~도", "exp": "Additive particle. Extends the scope: 한국에서도 (also in Korea).", "example_in_sentence": "한국에서도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 (adverb form)", "exp": "turns an adjective into an adverb. 엄격하다 → 엄격하게 = \"strictly\".", "example_in_sentence": "엄격하게"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be surprising; astonishing", "note": ""}, {"ko": "광고", "en": "advertisement", "note": ""}, {"ko": "유명하다", "en": "to be famous; well-known", "note": ""}, {"ko": "담배", "en": "cigarette, tobacco", "note": ""}, {"ko": "브랜드", "en": "brand", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아기", "en": "baby", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시기", "en": "period, time", "note": ""}, {"ko": "위험성", "en": "risk, danger, hazard", "note": ""}, {"ko": "해롭다", "en": "to be harmful", "note": ""}, {"ko": "알려지다", "en": "to be known, to become known", "note": ""}, {"ko": "광고회사", "en": "advertising company, ad agency", "note": ""}, {"ko": "안전하다", "en": "to be safe, safe", "note": ""}, {"ko": "건강하다", "en": "to be healthy, healthy", "note": ""}, {"ko": "제품", "en": "product", "note": ""}, {"ko": "순수하다", "en": "to be pure, pure", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이미지", "en": "image", "note": ""}, {"ko": "상징하다", "en": "to symbolize, to represent", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이용하다", "en": "to use, to utilize", "note": ""}, {"ko": "무해하다", "en": "to be harmless, harmless", "note": ""}, {"ko": "인상", "en": "impression", "note": ""}, {"ko": "밝혀지다", "en": "to be revealed, to come to light, to be discovered", "note": ""}, {"ko": "시작하다", "en": "to begin, to start", "note": ""}, {"ko": "현재", "en": "present, currently", "note": ""}, {"ko": "대부분", "en": "majority, most", "note": ""}, {"ko": "나라", "en": "country, nation", "note": ""}, {"ko": "방식", "en": "method, way, manner", "note": ""}, {"ko": "엄격하다", "en": "to be strict, strict, rigorous", "note": ""}, {"ko": "규제되다", "en": "to be regulated", "note": ""}, {"word": "금지하다", "reading": "geumjihada", "meaning": "to ban; to prohibit; to forbid", "context": "이런 방식의 담배 광고를 금지하고"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~았/었어요", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past tense ending for statements. 있다 (to exist) → 있었어요 (there was/were).", "ex_ko": "1940년대와 1950년대에 미국에서는 놀라운 광고가 있었어요.", "ex_en": "In the 1940s and 1950s, there were surprising advertisements in the United States."}, {"name": "~에서는", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Location particle 에서 + topic particle 는. Marks the place where action occurs, with topic emphasis.", "ex_ko": "1940년대와 1950년대에 미국에서는 놀라운 광고가 있었어요.", "ex_en": "In the 1940s and 1950s, there were surprising advertisements in the United States."}, {"name": "~인 (that is N)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "noun-modifying form of 이다. 담배 브랜드인 말보로 = \"Marlboro, which is a cigarette brand\".", "ex_ko": "유명한 담배 브랜드인 말보로(Marlboro)가 아기들을 광고에 사용했습니다.", "ex_en": "The famous cigarette brand Marlboro used babies in advertisements."}, {"name": "~았/었습니다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past tense formal statement ending. 사용하다 (to use) → 사용했습니다.", "ex_ko": "유명한 담배 브랜드인 말보로(Marlboro)가 아기들을 광고에 사용했습니다.", "ex_en": "The famous cigarette brand Marlboro used babies in advertisements."}, {"name": "~지 않다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Negation with auxiliary verb. 알려지다 (to be known) → 알려지지 않다 (not to be known).", "ex_ko": "이 시기는 담배의 건강 위험성(건강에 해로운 정도)이 잘 알려지지 않았던 때였어요.", "ex_en": "This period was a time when the health risks of cigarettes (the extent of harm to health) were not well known."}, {"name": "~았/었던", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past retrospective modifier. Marks 때 as a point in past time.", "ex_ko": "이 시기는 담배의 건강 위험성(건강에 해로운 정도)이 잘 알려지지 않았던 때였어요.", "ex_en": "This period was a time when the health risks of cigarettes (the extent of harm to health) were not well known."}, {"name": "~이었/였어요", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past copula for descriptive statements. 때 (time) + 이다 → 때였어요 (was a time).", "ex_ko": "이 시기는 담배의 건강 위험성(건강에 해로운 정도)이 잘 알려지지 않았던 때였어요.", "ex_en": "This period was a time when the health risks of cigarettes (the extent of harm to health) were not well known."}, {"name": "~게 하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Causative auxiliary. 보이다 (to appear) + 게 하다 (make/cause to) = to make appear.", "ex_ko": "광고회사들은 담배를 안전하고 건강한 제품처럼 보이게 하려고 했습니다.", "ex_en": "Advertising companies tried to make cigarettes appear as safe and healthy products."}, {"name": "~려고 하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Intentional/prospective ending. Expresses intention or attempt to do something. 하다 → 하려고 했습니다.", "ex_ko": "광고회사들은 담배를 안전하고 건강한 제품처럼 보이게 하려고 했습니다.", "ex_en": "Advertising companies tried to make cigarettes appear as safe and healthy products."}, {"name": "~고", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Coordinate conjunction. Connects two adjectives of equal weight: 순수하고 건강한.", "ex_ko": "아기는 순수하고 건강한 이미지를 상징해요.", "ex_en": "Babies symbolize a pure and healthy image."}, {"name": "~아/어서 (by means of)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "means. 이용하다 → 이용해서 = \"by using\".", "ex_ko": "말보로는 이런 이미지를 이용해서 자신들의 담배가 무해하다는 인상을 주려고 했습니다.", "ex_en": "Marlboro tried to give the impression that their cigarettes were harmless by using this kind of image."}, {"name": "~다는", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Nominal subordinator. Nominalizes the clause: 무해하다 → 무해하다는 (the fact/idea that [it] is harmless).", "ex_ko": "말보로는 이런 이미지를 이용해서 자신들의 담배가 무해하다는 인상을 주려고 했습니다.", "ex_en": "Marlboro tried to give the impression that their cigarettes were harmless by using this kind of image."}, {"name": "~부터", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Starting-point particle. Marks the beginning of a time span: 1960년대 → 1960년대부터 (from the 1960s).", "ex_ko": "하지만 1960년대부터 담배의 위험성이 밝혀지기 시작했어요.", "ex_en": "However, starting from the 1960s, the risks of cigarettes began to be revealed."}, {"name": "~기 시작하다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Inchoative auxiliary. Marks the beginning of an action. 밝혀지다 → 밝혀지기 시작했어요 (began to be revealed).", "ex_ko": "하지만 1960년대부터 담배의 위험성이 밝혀지기 시작했어요.", "ex_en": "However, starting from the 1960s, the risks of cigarettes began to be revealed."}, {"name": "~고 있다", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Progressive/continuous aspect. 금지하다 → 금지하고 있습니다 (are prohibiting, currently maintain prohibition).", "ex_ko": "현재는 대부분의 나라에서 이런 방식의 담배 광고를 금지하고 있습니다.", "ex_en": "Currently, most countries prohibit this type of cigarette advertisement."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mofqqs0exakz' and md5(translation) = '740e3ec1900a9ad24f087e8a0bac01e8';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["A medical student has become a hot topic by drawing a perfect heart diagram in just 20 seconds. This student accurately expressed the complex structure of the heart with just one pen.", "Looking at the video released online, you can confirm the remarkable skill. Many people marveled, saying ''That''s truly amazing.''", "Students studying medicine draw a lot of pictures to memorize the structure of the human body. It seems they developed this amazing skill through repeated practice.", "Korean medical students also do similar practice for anatomy (the study of human body structure) studies. Accurate drawing skills are one of the important abilities in becoming a doctor."], "sentences": [{"text": "한 의대생이 20초 만에 완벽한 심장 그림을 그려서 화제가 되고 있어요.", "translation": "A medical student has become a hot topic by drawing a perfect heart diagram in just 20 seconds.", "vocab": [{"ko": "의대생", "en": "medical student"}, {"ko": "완벽하다", "en": "to be perfect; flawless"}, {"ko": "화제", "en": "hot topic; subject of discussion"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~ 만에 (in, within)", "exp": "how long something took. 20초 → 20초 만에 = \"in just 20 seconds\".", "example_in_sentence": "20초 만에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어서 (and so)", "exp": "cause or sequence. 그리다 → 그려서 = \"drew (it) and so\".", "example_in_sentence": "그려서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있어요", "exp": "Progressive/continuous aspect. Auxiliary 있다 in present tense form, indicating ongoing state or action.", "example_in_sentence": "되고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "이 학생은 펜 하나로 심장의 복잡한 구조를 정확하게 표현했습니다.", "translation": "This student expressed the heart''s complex structure accurately with just one pen.", "vocab": [{"ko": "복잡하다", "en": "to be complex; complicated"}, {"ko": "구조", "en": "structure"}, {"ko": "정확하다", "en": "to be accurate; precise"}, {"ko": "표현하다", "en": "to express; depict"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~로", "exp": "Instrumental particle indicating the means or tool used for an action.", "example_in_sentence": "펜 하나로"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었습니다 (past formal)", "exp": "past formal-polite. 표현하다 → 표현했습니다 = \"expressed\".", "example_in_sentence": "표현했습니다"}]}, {"text": "온라인에서 공개된 영상을 보면 놀라운 실력을 확인할 수 있어요.", "translation": "If you watch the video posted online, you can see the amazing skill for yourself.", "vocab": [{"ko": "온라인", "en": "online"}, {"ko": "공개되다", "en": "to be released; made public"}, {"ko": "영상", "en": "video; footage"}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be amazing; surprising"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "describes a noun with a past action. 공개되다 → 공개된 영상 = \"a video that was released\".", "example_in_sentence": "공개된 영상"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면 (if/when)", "exp": "condition. 보다 → 보면 = \"if you watch\".", "example_in_sentence": "보면"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다 (can)", "exp": "possibility. 확인하다 → 확인할 수 있어요 = \"can see\".", "example_in_sentence": "확인할 수 있어요"}]}, {"text": "많은 사람들이 \"정말 대단하다\"며 감탄했습니다.", "translation": "Many people admired it, saying \"It''s truly remarkable.\"", "vocab": [{"ko": "대단하다", "en": "remarkable; impressive"}, {"ko": "감탄하다", "en": "to admire; marvel"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~다며 (saying that)", "exp": "quotes what people say while doing something else. 대단하다 → 대단하다며 = \"saying (it''s) amazing\".", "example_in_sentence": "\"정말 대단하다\"며"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었습니다 (past formal)", "exp": "past formal-polite. 감탄하다 → 감탄했습니다 = \"marveled\".", "example_in_sentence": "감탄했습니다"}]}, {"text": "의학을 공부하는 학생들은 인체 구조를 외우기 위해 그림을 많이 그려요.", "translation": "Students studying medicine draw pictures a lot in order to memorize the human body structure.", "vocab": [{"ko": "의학", "en": "medicine; medical science"}, {"ko": "인체", "en": "human body"}, {"ko": "외우다", "en": "memorize; learn by heart"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present participle)", "exp": "Attributive participle modifying nouns, expressing present/habitual action. Base form 공부하다 + participle marker 는.", "example_in_sentence": "공부하는 학생들"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~기 위해", "exp": "Purpose/goal marker. Nominalized form + purpose particle 위해, expressing ''in order to/for the purpose of''.", "example_in_sentence": "외우기 위해"}]}, {"text": "반복 연습을 통해 이런 놀라운 실력을 갖게 된 것 같습니다.", "translation": "It seems they have come to possess such amazing skill through repeated practice.", "vocab": [{"ko": "반복", "en": "repetition; repeat"}, {"ko": "연습", "en": "practice"}, {"ko": "실력", "en": "skill; ability"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~을 통해", "exp": "Through/by means of. Object particle 을 + postposition 통해, indicating method or medium.", "example_in_sentence": "반복 연습을 통해"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 되다 (come to)", "exp": "a change that came about over time. 갖다 → 갖게 되다 = \"to come to have\".", "example_in_sentence": "갖게 된"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~(으)ㄴ 것 같다 (it seems ~ did)", "exp": "a guess about something that happened. 되다 → 된 것 같습니다 = \"it seems (they) came to\".", "example_in_sentence": "된 것 같습니다"}]}, {"text": "한국의 의대생들도 해부학(인체의 구조를 연구하는 학문) 공부를 위해 비슷한 연습을 해요.", "translation": "Korean medical students also do similar practice to study anatomy (the field that studies the structure of the human body).", "vocab": [{"ko": "해부학", "en": "anatomy"}, {"ko": "연구", "en": "research; study"}, {"ko": "학문", "en": "discipline; field of study"}, {"ko": "비슷하다", "en": "to be similar"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (present participle)", "exp": "Attributive participle in appositive clause defining 해부학. Base form 연구하다 + 는.", "example_in_sentence": "연구하는 학문"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~을/를 위해 (for)", "exp": "purpose with a noun. 공부 → 공부를 위해 = \"for studying\".", "example_in_sentence": "공부를 위해"}]}, {"text": "정확한 그림 실력은 의사가 되는 데 중요한 능력 중 하나입니다.", "translation": "Accurate drawing skill is one of the important abilities for becoming a doctor.", "vocab": [{"ko": "정확하다", "en": "to be accurate; precise"}, {"ko": "능력", "en": "ability; capability"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 데 (in V-ing)", "exp": "for or in doing something. 되다 → 의사가 되는 데 = \"in becoming a doctor\".", "example_in_sentence": "되는 데"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~ 중 하나 (one of)", "exp": "one item from a group. 중요한 능력 중 하나 = \"one of the important abilities\".", "example_in_sentence": "중요한 능력 중 하나"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "의대생", "en": "medical student", "note": ""}, {"ko": "완벽하다", "en": "to be perfect; flawless", "note": ""}, {"ko": "화제", "en": "hot topic; subject of discussion", "note": ""}, {"ko": "복잡하다", "en": "to be complex; complicated", "note": ""}, {"ko": "구조", "en": "structure", "note": ""}, {"ko": "정확하다", "en": "to be accurate; precise", "note": ""}, {"ko": "표현하다", "en": "to express; depict", "note": ""}, {"ko": "온라인", "en": "online", "note": ""}, {"ko": "공개되다", "en": "to be released; made public", "note": ""}, {"ko": "영상", "en": "video; footage", "note": ""}, {"ko": "놀랍다", "en": "to be amazing; surprising", "note": ""}, {"ko": "대단하다", "en": "remarkable; impressive", "note": ""}, {"ko": "감탄하다", "en": "to admire; marvel", "note": ""}, {"ko": "의학", "en": "medicine; medical science", "note": ""}, {"ko": "인체", "en": "human body", "note": ""}, {"ko": "외우다", "en": "memorize; learn by heart", "note": ""}, {"ko": "반복", "en": "repetition; repeat", "note": ""}, {"ko": "연습", "en": "practice", "note": ""}, {"ko": "실력", "en": "skill; ability", "note": ""}, {"ko": "해부학", "en": "anatomy", "note": ""}, {"ko": "연구", "en": "research; study", "note": ""}, {"ko": "학문", "en": "discipline; field of study", "note": ""}, {"ko": "비슷하다", "en": "to be similar", "note": ""}, {"ko": "능력", "en": "ability; capability", "note": ""}, {"word": "화제가 되다", "reading": "hwajetae ga doeda", "meaning": "to become a topic of interest; to become a hot issue", "context": "20초 만에 완벽한 심장 그림을 그려서 화제가 되고 있어요"}, {"word": "반복 연습", "reading": "banbok yeonseup", "meaning": "repeated practice; practice repetition", "context": "반복 연습을 통해 이런 놀라운 실력을 갖게 된 것 같습니다"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~ 만에 (in, within)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "how long something took. 20초 → 20초 만에 = \"in just 20 seconds\".", "ex_ko": "한 의대생이 20초 만에 완벽한 심장 그림을 그려서 화제가 되고 있어요.", "ex_en": "A medical student has become a hot topic by drawing a perfect heart diagram in just 20 seconds."}, {"name": "~아/어서 (and so)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "cause or sequence. 그리다 → 그려서 = \"drew (it) and so\".", "ex_ko": "한 의대생이 20초 만에 완벽한 심장 그림을 그려서 화제가 되고 있어요.", "ex_en": "A medical student has become a hot topic by drawing a perfect heart diagram in just 20 seconds."}, {"name": "~고 있어요", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Progressive/continuous aspect. Auxiliary 있다 in present tense form, indicating ongoing state or action.", "ex_ko": "한 의대생이 20초 만에 완벽한 심장 그림을 그려서 화제가 되고 있어요.", "ex_en": "A medical student has become a hot topic by drawing a perfect heart diagram in just 20 seconds."}, {"name": "~로", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Instrumental particle indicating the means or tool used for an action.", "ex_ko": "이 학생은 펜 하나로 심장의 복잡한 구조를 정확하게 표현했습니다.", "ex_en": "This student expressed the heart''s complex structure accurately with just one pen."}, {"name": "~았/었습니다 (past formal)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "past formal-polite. 표현하다 → 표현했습니다 = \"expressed\".", "ex_ko": "이 학생은 펜 하나로 심장의 복잡한 구조를 정확하게 표현했습니다.", "ex_en": "This student expressed the heart''s complex structure accurately with just one pen."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "describes a noun with a past action. 공개되다 → 공개된 영상 = \"a video that was released\".", "ex_ko": "온라인에서 공개된 영상을 보면 놀라운 실력을 확인할 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "If you watch the video posted online, you can see the amazing skill for yourself."}, {"name": "~(으)면 (if/when)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "condition. 보다 → 보면 = \"if you watch\".", "ex_ko": "온라인에서 공개된 영상을 보면 놀라운 실력을 확인할 수 있어요.", "ex_en": "If you watch the video posted online, you can see the amazing skill for yourself."}, {"name": "~다며 (saying that)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "quotes what people say while doing something else. 대단하다 → 대단하다며 = \"saying (it''s) amazing\".", "ex_ko": "많은 사람들이 \"정말 대단하다\"며 감탄했습니다.", "ex_en": "Many people admired it, saying \"It''s truly remarkable.\""}, {"name": "~는 (present participle)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Attributive participle modifying nouns, expressing present/habitual action. Base form 공부하다 + participle marker 는.", "ex_ko": "의학을 공부하는 학생들은 인체 구조를 외우기 위해 그림을 많이 그려요.", "ex_en": "Students studying medicine draw pictures a lot in order to memorize the human body structure."}, {"name": "~게 되다 (come to)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "a change that came about over time. 갖다 → 갖게 되다 = \"to come to have\".", "ex_ko": "반복 연습을 통해 이런 놀라운 실력을 갖게 된 것 같습니다.", "ex_en": "It seems they have come to possess such amazing skill through repeated practice."}, {"name": "~는 데 (in V-ing)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "for or in doing something. 되다 → 의사가 되는 데 = \"in becoming a doctor\".", "ex_ko": "정확한 그림 실력은 의사가 되는 데 중요한 능력 중 하나입니다.", "ex_en": "Accurate drawing skill is one of the important abilities for becoming a doctor."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mogeixknc64m' and md5(translation) = 'ccfa16e1783f9d8216734701cbaa8843';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["In Namibia, Africa, a desert-adapted elephant was captured sliding down a sand dune. This special scene has become a big topic of discussion on the internet.", "Desert elephants in Namibia, unlike regular elephants, have adapted to dry environments. They travel long distances to find water and can move skillfully even on sand.", "The behavior of an elephant sliding down a sand dune is a very rare sight. Experts analyze that this is likely a play behavior. It''s an interesting case that shows animals, like humans, engage in activities for fun.", "This scene makes us feel the mystery of nature once again. We can see that even in harsh desert environments, animals enjoy life in their own way."], "sentences": [{"text": "아프리카 나미비아에서 사막에 적응한 코끼리가 모래언덕을 미끄러져 내려가는 모습이 포착되었어요.", "translation": "In Namibia, Africa, a desert-adapted elephant was spotted sliding down a sand dune.", "vocab": [{"ko": "적응하다", "en": "adapt; adjust"}, {"ko": "모래언덕", "en": "sand dune"}, {"ko": "미끄러지다", "en": "slide; slip"}, {"ko": "포착되다", "en": "be spotted; be caught"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "exp": "describes a noun with a past action. 적응하다 → 적응한 코끼리 = \"an elephant that has adapted\".", "example_in_sentence": "사막에 적응한 코끼리"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (modification: present participle)", "exp": "Marks a present participle modifying a noun. ''미끄러져 내려가는'' = ongoing action describing the manner of the sight being captured.", "example_in_sentence": "미끄러져 내려가는 모습"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense ending with polite/casual tone. ''포착되었어요'' = ''포착되다'' + -었어요, indicating a completed action.", "example_in_sentence": "포착되었어요"}]}, {"text": "이 특별한 장면은 인터넷에서 큰 화제가 되고 있습니다.", "translation": "This remarkable scene is becoming a major topic on the internet.", "vocab": [{"ko": "특별하다", "en": "special; remarkable"}, {"ko": "화제", "en": "topic; subject"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다 (progressive aspect)", "exp": "Indicates ongoing/progressive action. ''되고 있습니다'' = ''되다'' + -고 있다, showing continuous becoming a topic.", "example_in_sentence": "화제가 되고 있습니다"}]}, {"text": "나미비아의 사막 코끼리는 일반 코끼리와 달리 건조한 환경에 적응했어요.", "translation": "Unlike ordinary elephants, Namibia''s desert elephants have adapted to dry environments.", "vocab": [{"ko": "건조하다", "en": "dry; arid"}, {"ko": "적응하다", "en": "adapt; adjust"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~와/과 달리 (unlike)", "exp": "shows a contrast. 일반 코끼리 → 일반 코끼리와 달리 = \"unlike ordinary elephants\".", "example_in_sentence": "일반 코끼리와 달리"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense with polite tone. ''적응했어요'' = ''적응하다'' + -았어요, indicating completed adaptation.", "example_in_sentence": "적응했어요"}]}, {"text": "이들은 물을 찾아 먼 거리를 이동하며, 모래 위에서도 능숙하게 움직일 수 있습니다.", "translation": "They move long distances searching for water, and can skillfully move on sand as well.", "vocab": [{"ko": "이동하다", "en": "move; relocate"}, {"ko": "능숙하다", "en": "skillful; adept"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)며 (and, while)", "exp": "links two actions, mostly in writing. 이동하다 → 이동하며 = \"move (long distances), and\".", "example_in_sentence": "이동하며"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다 (can)", "exp": "ability. 움직이다 → 움직일 수 있습니다 = \"can move\".", "example_in_sentence": "움직일 수 있습니다"}]}, {"text": "코끼리가 모래언덕을 미끄러져 내려가는 행동은 매우 드문 광경이에요.", "translation": "The behavior of an elephant sliding down a sand dune is a very rare sight.", "vocab": [{"ko": "미끄러지다", "en": "slide; slip"}, {"ko": "행동", "en": "behavior; action"}, {"ko": "드물다", "en": "rare; uncommon"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (modification: present participle)", "exp": "Marks present participle modifying a noun. ''미끄러져 내려가는'' describes the ongoing behavior being characterized.", "example_in_sentence": "미끄러져 내려가는 행동"}]}, {"text": "전문가들은 이것이 놀이 행동일 가능성이 높다고 분석하고 있습니다.", "translation": "Experts believe this is most likely play behavior.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert; specialist"}, {"ko": "놀이", "en": "play; game"}, {"ko": "가능성", "en": "possibility; likelihood"}, {"ko": "분석하다", "en": "analyze"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 가능성이 높다 (likely)", "exp": "probability. 놀이 행동이다 → 놀이 행동일 가능성이 높다 = \"is likely to be play behavior\".", "example_in_sentence": "놀이 행동일 가능성이 높다"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다 (progressive aspect)", "exp": "Ongoing action. ''분석하고 있습니다'' = ''분석하다'' + -고 있다, indicating experts are currently analyzing.", "example_in_sentence": "분석하고 있습니다"}]}, {"text": "동물들도 사람처럼 재미를 위한 활동을 한다는 것을 보여주는 흥미로운 사례예요.", "translation": "It is an interesting case showing that animals, like humans, engage in activities for fun.", "vocab": [{"ko": "재미", "en": "fun; enjoyment"}, {"ko": "활동", "en": "activity"}, {"ko": "사례", "en": "case; example"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~처럼 (like; as; similar to)", "exp": "Comparison/similarity marker. ''사람처럼'' = comparing animals to humans.", "example_in_sentence": "사람처럼"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~ㄴ/는다는 것 (the fact that)", "exp": "turns a statement into a noun. 활동을 한다 → 한다는 것 = \"the fact that (they) do (activities)\".", "example_in_sentence": "한다는 것"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (modification: present participle)", "exp": "Present participle modifying noun. ''보여주는'' = ''보여주다'' + -는, describing the case/example.", "example_in_sentence": "보여주는 흥미로운 사례"}]}, {"text": "이런 모습은 자연의 신비로움을 다시 한번 느끼게 해줘요.", "translation": "Such sights make us feel the mystery of nature once again.", "vocab": [{"ko": "신비로움", "en": "mystery; wonder"}, {"ko": "느끼다", "en": "feel; sense"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~게 하다 (causative)", "exp": "Causative auxiliary meaning ''make/let/cause.'' ''느끼게 해줘요'' = ''느끼다'' + -게 하다, causing someone to feel.", "example_in_sentence": "느끼게 해줘요"}]}, {"text": "혹독한 사막 환경에서도 동물들은 자신만의 방식으로 삶을 즐기고 있다는 것을 알 수 있습니다.", "translation": "We can understand that even in harsh desert environments, animals enjoy life in their own way.", "vocab": [{"ko": "혹독하다", "en": "harsh; severe"}, {"ko": "환경", "en": "environment"}, {"ko": "방식", "en": "way; method"}, {"ko": "즐기다", "en": "enjoy"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~다는 것 (the fact that)", "exp": "turns a statement into a noun. 즐기고 있다 → 즐기고 있다는 것 = \"the fact that (they) are enjoying\".", "example_in_sentence": "즐기고 있다는 것"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다 (can)", "exp": "possibility. 알다 → 알 수 있습니다 (ㄹ-stem: no extra ㄹ) = \"can see, can tell\".", "example_in_sentence": "알 수 있습니다"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "적응하다", "en": "adapt; adjust", "note": ""}, {"ko": "모래언덕", "en": "sand dune", "note": ""}, {"ko": "미끄러지다", "en": "slide; slip", "note": ""}, {"ko": "포착되다", "en": "be spotted; be caught", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "special; remarkable", "note": ""}, {"ko": "화제", "en": "topic; subject", "note": ""}, {"ko": "건조하다", "en": "dry; arid", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이동하다", "en": "move; relocate", "note": ""}, {"ko": "능숙하다", "en": "skillful; adept", "note": ""}, {"ko": "행동", "en": "behavior; action", "note": ""}, {"ko": "드물다", "en": "rare; uncommon", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전문가", "en": "expert; specialist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "놀이", "en": "play; game", "note": ""}, {"ko": "가능성", "en": "possibility; likelihood", "note": ""}, {"ko": "분석하다", "en": "analyze", "note": ""}, {"ko": "재미", "en": "fun; enjoyment", "note": ""}, {"ko": "활동", "en": "activity", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사례", "en": "case; example", "note": ""}, {"ko": "신비로움", "en": "mystery; wonder", "note": ""}, {"ko": "느끼다", "en": "feel; sense", "note": ""}, {"ko": "혹독하다", "en": "harsh; severe", "note": ""}, {"ko": "환경", "en": "environment", "note": ""}, {"ko": "방식", "en": "way; method", "note": ""}, {"ko": "즐기다", "en": "enjoy", "note": ""}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(으)ㄴ (past verb modifier)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "describes a noun with a past action. 적응하다 → 적응한 코끼리 = \"an elephant that has adapted\".", "ex_ko": "아프리카 나미비아에서 사막에 적응한 코끼리가 모래언덕을 미끄러져 내려가는 모습이 포착되었어요.", "ex_en": "In Namibia, Africa, a desert-adapted elephant was spotted sliding down a sand dune."}, {"name": "~는 (modification: present participle)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Marks a present participle modifying a noun. ''미끄러져 내려가는'' = ongoing action describing the manner of the sight being captured.", "ex_ko": "아프리카 나미비아에서 사막에 적응한 코끼리가 모래언덕을 미끄러져 내려가는 모습이 포착되었어요.", "ex_en": "In Namibia, Africa, a desert-adapted elephant was spotted sliding down a sand dune."}, {"name": "~았/었어요", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Past tense ending with polite/casual tone. ''포착되었어요'' = ''포착되다'' + -었어요, indicating a completed action.", "ex_ko": "아프리카 나미비아에서 사막에 적응한 코끼리가 모래언덕을 미끄러져 내려가는 모습이 포착되었어요.", "ex_en": "In Namibia, Africa, a desert-adapted elephant was spotted sliding down a sand dune."}, {"name": "~고 있다 (progressive aspect)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Indicates ongoing/progressive action. ''되고 있습니다'' = ''되다'' + -고 있다, showing continuous becoming a topic.", "ex_ko": "이 특별한 장면은 인터넷에서 큰 화제가 되고 있습니다.", "ex_en": "This remarkable scene is becoming a major topic on the internet."}, {"name": "~(으)며 (and, while)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "links two actions, mostly in writing. 이동하다 → 이동하며 = \"move (long distances), and\".", "ex_ko": "이들은 물을 찾아 먼 거리를 이동하며, 모래 위에서도 능숙하게 움직일 수 있습니다.", "ex_en": "They move long distances searching for water, and can skillfully move on sand as well."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수 있다 (can)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "possibility. 알다 → 알 수 있습니다 (ㄹ-stem: no extra ㄹ) = \"can see, can tell\".", "ex_ko": "이들은 물을 찾아 먼 거리를 이동하며, 모래 위에서도 능숙하게 움직일 수 있습니다.", "ex_en": "They move long distances searching for water, and can skillfully move on sand as well."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 가능성이 높다 (likely)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "probability. 놀이 행동이다 → 놀이 행동일 가능성이 높다 = \"is likely to be play behavior\".", "ex_ko": "전문가들은 이것이 놀이 행동일 가능성이 높다고 분석하고 있습니다.", "ex_en": "Experts believe this is most likely play behavior."}, {"name": "~ㄴ/는다는 것 (the fact that)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "turns a statement into a noun. 활동을 한다 → 한다는 것 = \"the fact that (they) do (activities)\".", "ex_ko": "동물들도 사람처럼 재미를 위한 활동을 한다는 것을 보여주는 흥미로운 사례예요.", "ex_en": "It is an interesting case showing that animals, like humans, engage in activities for fun."}, {"name": "~게 하다 (causative)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "Causative auxiliary meaning ''make/let/cause.'' ''느끼게 해줘요'' = ''느끼다'' + -게 하다, causing someone to feel.", "ex_ko": "이런 모습은 자연의 신비로움을 다시 한번 느끼게 해줘요.", "ex_en": "Such sights make us feel the mystery of nature once again."}, {"name": "~다는 것 (the fact that)", "level": "Intermediate", "exp": "turns a statement into a noun. 즐기고 있다 → 즐기고 있다는 것 = \"the fact that (they) are enjoying\".", "ex_ko": "혹독한 사막 환경에서도 동물들은 자신만의 방식으로 삶을 즐기고 있다는 것을 알 수 있습니다.", "ex_en": "We can understand that even in harsh desert environments, animals enjoy life in their own way."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mogejm0r2t3z' and md5(translation) = '4c986b9371ca54fd6ab4c30a61cd436d';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["You shouldn''t make eye contact with a gorilla. Gorillas perceive eye contact as a threat. Especially large male gorillas get even angrier. They can even attack people. At zoos, they make special glasses. When you wear these glasses, your eyes don''t meet the gorilla''s eyes. This way, the gorilla doesn''t experience stress. Both the gorilla and people become safe.", "Korean Teacher Shortage Becomes Serious, School Classes Disrupted", "What is an \"anxiety bag\"? A Popular Trend", "The United States and China Resume Talks Over Trade Issues", "\"Talking Pig\" Becomes SNS Star", "Apple Greatly Improves iPhone Speed with New AI Chip"], "sentences": [{"text": "고릴라와 눈을 마주치면 안 돼요.", "translation": "You must not make eye contact with a gorilla.", "vocab": [{"ko": "고릴라", "en": "gorilla"}, {"ko": "눈", "en": "eye"}, {"ko": "마주치다", "en": "to meet; to make eye contact"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면 안 되다 (must not)", "exp": "prohibition. 마주치다 → 마주치면 안 돼요 = \"must not meet (its eyes)\".", "example_in_sentence": "마주치면 안 돼요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~와/과 (particle)", "exp": "Particle indicating ''with'' or ''and'' in the sense of accompaniment/association. Attached to noun 고릴라.", "example_in_sentence": "고릴라와"}]}, {"text": "고릴라는 눈을 마주치는 것을 위협으로 느껴요.", "translation": "Gorillas perceive eye contact as a threat.", "vocab": [{"ko": "위협", "en": "threat"}, {"ko": "느끼다", "en": "to feel; to perceive"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 것 (V-ing)", "exp": "turns a verb into a noun. 마주치다 → 마주치는 것 = \"making (eye contact)\"; 을 marks it as the object.", "example_in_sentence": "눈을 마주치는 것을"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~을/를 위협으로 느끼다", "exp": "Verb expression meaning ''to perceive/feel ~ as a threat.'' Combines object particle 을 + 위협(threat) + 으로(as) + 느끼다(to feel).", "example_in_sentence": "눈을 마주치는 것을 위협으로 느껴요"}]}, {"text": "특히 큰 수컷 고릴라는 더 화를 내요.", "translation": "Large male gorillas in particular get angrier.", "vocab": [{"ko": "특히", "en": "especially; particularly"}, {"ko": "수컷", "en": "male"}, {"ko": "화", "en": "anger"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "화를 내다", "exp": "Verb expression meaning ''to get angry; to become upset.'' Combines noun 화(anger) + object particle 를 + 내다(to express/show). An idiom rather than literal composition.", "example_in_sentence": "더 화를 내요"}]}, {"text": "사람을 공격할 수도 있어요.", "translation": "They may even attack people.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사람", "en": "person"}, {"ko": "공격하다", "en": "to attack"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)ㄹ 수도 있다 (may, might)", "exp": "possibility; 도 adds \"even\". 공격하다 → 공격할 수도 있어요 = \"may (even) attack\".", "example_in_sentence": "공격할 수도 있어요"}]}, {"text": "동물원에서는 특별한 안경을 만들어요.", "translation": "In zoos, they make special glasses.", "vocab": [{"ko": "동물원", "en": "zoo"}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special"}, {"ko": "안경", "en": "glasses; spectacles"}, {"ko": "만들다", "en": "to make; to create"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에서는", "exp": "Locative particle ~에서 (in/at) + topic particle ~는. Indicates location with topical emphasis. Here: ''in zoos [particularly]''.", "example_in_sentence": "동물원에서는"}]}, {"text": "이 안경을 쓰면 고릴라와 눈이 마주치지 않아요.", "translation": "If you wear these glasses, you don''t make eye contact with the gorillas.", "vocab": [{"ko": "쓰다", "en": "to wear (on head)"}, {"ko": "마주치다", "en": "to meet; to make contact"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~(으)면 (if/when)", "exp": "condition. 쓰다 → 쓰면 = \"if (you) wear\".", "example_in_sentence": "쓰면"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않다 (not)", "exp": "negation. 마주치다 → 마주치지 않아요 = \"(eyes) don''t meet\".", "example_in_sentence": "마주치지 않아요"}]}, {"text": "이렇게 하면 고릴라가 스트레스를 받지 않아요.", "translation": "If you do this, the gorillas don''t get stressed.", "vocab": [{"ko": "스트레스", "en": "stress"}, {"ko": "받다", "en": "to receive; to experience"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "스트레스를 받다", "exp": "Verb expression meaning ''to experience/receive stress.'' Combines noun 스트레스 + object particle 를 + 받다(to receive).", "example_in_sentence": "스트레스를 받지 않아요"}]}, {"text": "고릴라도 사람도 안전해져요.", "translation": "Both gorillas and people become safe.", "vocab": [{"ko": "안전하다", "en": "to be safe; to be secure"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "도 (particle, repeated)", "exp": "Particle meaning ''also; too'' or when repeated (X도 Y도), ''both X and Y.'' Here: ''both gorillas and people''.", "example_in_sentence": "고릴라도 사람도"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~어/아지다", "exp": "Auxiliary verb indicating state change or becoming. 안전하다 (adjective) + 어지다 → 안전해지다 → 안전해져요. Expresses transition to a state: ''become safe''.", "example_in_sentence": "안전해져요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "고릴라", "en": "gorilla", "note": ""}, {"ko": "눈", "en": "eye", "note": ""}, {"ko": "마주치다", "en": "to meet; to make eye contact", "note": ""}, {"ko": "위협", "en": "threat", "note": ""}, {"ko": "느끼다", "en": "to feel; to perceive", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특히", "en": "especially; particularly", "note": ""}, {"ko": "수컷", "en": "male", "note": ""}, {"ko": "화", "en": "anger", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person", "note": ""}, {"ko": "공격하다", "en": "to attack", "note": ""}, {"ko": "동물원", "en": "zoo", "note": ""}, {"ko": "특별하다", "en": "to be special", "note": ""}, {"ko": "안경", "en": "glasses; spectacles", "note": ""}, {"ko": "만들다", "en": "to make; to create", "note": ""}, {"ko": "쓰다", "en": "to wear (on head)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "스트레스", "en": "stress", "note": ""}, {"ko": "받다", "en": "to receive; to experience", "note": ""}, {"ko": "안전하다", "en": "to be safe; to be secure", "note": ""}, {"word": "눈을 마주치다", "reading": "nun-eul majuchida", "meaning": "to make eye contact / to look directly at someone''s eyes", "context": "고릴라와 눈을 마주치면 안 돼요"}, {"word": "화를 내다", "reading": "hwaleul naeda", "meaning": "to get angry / to lose one''s temper", "context": "큰 수컷 고릴라는 더 화를 내요"}]', grammar = '{"patterns": [{"name": "~(으)면 안 되다 (must not)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "prohibition. 마주치다 → 마주치면 안 돼요 = \"must not meet (its eyes)\".", "ex_ko": "고릴라와 눈을 마주치면 안 돼요.", "ex_en": "You must not make eye contact with a gorilla."}, {"name": "~와/과 (particle)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Particle indicating ''with'' or ''and'' in the sense of accompaniment/association. Attached to noun 고릴라.", "ex_ko": "고릴라와 눈을 마주치면 안 돼요.", "ex_en": "You must not make eye contact with a gorilla."}, {"name": "~는 것 (V-ing)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "turns a verb into a noun. 마주치다 → 마주치는 것 = \"making (eye contact)\"; 을 marks it as the object.", "ex_ko": "고릴라는 눈을 마주치는 것을 위협으로 느껴요.", "ex_en": "Gorillas perceive eye contact as a threat."}, {"name": "~(으)ㄹ 수도 있다 (may, might)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "possibility; 도 adds \"even\". 공격하다 → 공격할 수도 있어요 = \"may (even) attack\".", "ex_ko": "사람을 공격할 수도 있어요.", "ex_en": "They may even attack people."}, {"name": "~에서는", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Locative particle ~에서 (in/at) + topic particle ~는. Indicates location with topical emphasis. Here: ''in zoos [particularly]''.", "ex_ko": "동물원에서는 특별한 안경을 만들어요.", "ex_en": "In zoos, they make special glasses."}, {"name": "~(으)면 (if/when)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "condition. 쓰다 → 쓰면 = \"if (you) wear\".", "ex_ko": "이 안경을 쓰면 고릴라와 눈이 마주치지 않아요.", "ex_en": "If you wear these glasses, you don''t make eye contact with the gorillas."}, {"name": "~지 않다 (not)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "negation. 마주치다 → 마주치지 않아요 = \"(eyes) don''t meet\".", "ex_ko": "이 안경을 쓰면 고릴라와 눈이 마주치지 않아요.", "ex_en": "If you wear these glasses, you don''t make eye contact with the gorillas."}, {"name": "도 (particle, repeated)", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Particle meaning ''also; too'' or when repeated (X도 Y도), ''both X and Y.'' Here: ''both gorillas and people''.", "ex_ko": "고릴라도 사람도 안전해져요.", "ex_en": "Both gorillas and people become safe."}, {"name": "~어/아지다", "level": "Starter", "exp": "Auxiliary verb indicating state change or becoming. 안전하다 (adjective) + 어지다 → 안전해지다 → 안전해져요. Expresses transition to a state: ''become safe''.", "ex_ko": "고릴라도 사람도 안전해져요.", "ex_en": "Both gorillas and people become safe."}]}', updated_at = now() where article_id = 'mogek69w51r7' and md5(translation) = 'ca903edb808e56103664e8c5924ec7ce';
update public.article_cache set translation = '{"texts": ["Korea''s DMZ (Demilitarized Zone) was created in 1953. It is a 250km long area between North Korea and South Korea.", "Originally, the DMZ was a place to prevent war. However, now it has become a treasure trove of nature where many animals and plants live.", "Because people do not live there, nature has been well protected. Animals in danger of extinction also live in this place.", "People around the world are showing interest in the DMZ''s ecosystem. Although it is a place of pain from division, it has become a safe home for nature."], "sentences": [{"text": "한국의 DMZ(비무장지대)는 1953년에 만들어졌어요.", "translation": "Korea''s DMZ (demilitarized zone) was created in 1953.", "vocab": [{"ko": "비무장지대", "en": "demilitarized zone"}, {"ko": "만들어지다", "en": "to be made; created"}, {"ko": "년", "en": "year"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요 (past)", "exp": "past polite. 만들어지다 → 만들어졌어요 = \"was made\".", "example_in_sentence": "만들어졌어요"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에", "exp": "Locative particle marking time point. Indicates when an action occurred.", "example_in_sentence": "1953년에"}]}, {"text": "북한과 남한 사이에 있는 250km 길이의 지역이에요.", "translation": "It is a 250 km-long area between North Korea and South Korea.", "vocab": [{"ko": "북한", "en": "North Korea"}, {"ko": "남한", "en": "South Korea"}, {"ko": "사이", "en": "between"}, {"ko": "길이", "en": "length"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는 (modifier)", "exp": "present modifier before a noun. 있다 → 사이에 있는 지역 = \"an area that is between\".", "example_in_sentence": "있는"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "~ 사이에", "exp": "Postpositional phrase meaning ''between''. Marks the location where something exists in the middle of two entities.", "example_in_sentence": "사이에"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~의", "exp": "Possessive/attributive particle marking relationship between nouns. Indicates that the following noun modifies or belongs to the preceding noun.", "example_in_sentence": "길이의"}]}, {"text": "원래 DMZ는 전쟁을 막기 위한 곳이었어요.", "translation": "Originally, the DMZ was a place to prevent war.", "vocab": [{"ko": "원래", "en": "originally; originally intended"}, {"ko": "전쟁", "en": "war"}, {"ko": "막다", "en": "to block; to prevent"}, {"ko": "곳", "en": "place"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~기 위한", "exp": "Purposive construction. The nominalizer ~기 with postposition 위한 (intended for) forms an attributive phrase meaning ''for the purpose of.'' 막다 → 막기.", "example_in_sentence": "막기 위한"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense in polite speech. Indicates a state or identity in the past. 이다 → 이었어요.", "example_in_sentence": "이었어요"}]}, {"text": "하지만 지금은 많은 동물과 식물이 사는 자연의 보고가 되었어요.", "translation": "However, now it has become a treasure trove of nature where many animals and plants live.", "vocab": [{"ko": "하지만", "en": "however; but"}, {"ko": "지금", "en": "now"}, {"ko": "동물", "en": "animal"}, {"ko": "식물", "en": "plant"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~는", "exp": "Attributive ending on action verb. Modifies the following noun to indicate an ongoing or habitual state. 사는 = those where (animals and plants) live.", "example_in_sentence": "사는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 되다 (become)", "exp": "change of state. N이/가 되다 = \"to become N\"; 자연의 보고가 되었어요 = \"became a treasure trove of nature\".", "example_in_sentence": "보고가 되었어요"}, {"type": "expression", "label": "자연의 보고", "exp": "Noun phrase meaning ''treasure trove of nature.'' A figurative expression indicating a place rich in natural resources and life.", "example_in_sentence": "자연의 보고"}]}, {"text": "사람들이 살지 않아서 자연이 잘 보호되었어요.", "translation": "Because people do not live there, nature has been well protected.", "vocab": [{"ko": "사람", "en": "person"}, {"ko": "살다", "en": "to live"}, {"ko": "보호되다", "en": "to be protected"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~지 않다", "exp": "Negation suffix attached to verb stem. Expresses negative state or non-action. 살다 → 살지 않다.", "example_in_sentence": "살지 않아서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~아/어서 (because)", "exp": "reason. 않다 → 않아서 = \"because (people) don''t\".", "example_in_sentence": "않아서"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~았/었어요", "exp": "Past tense in polite speech. Indicates completed action or result state. 보호되다 → 보호되었어요.", "example_in_sentence": "보호되었어요"}]}, {"text": "멸종 위기에 처한 동물들도 이곳에서 살고 있어요.", "translation": "Animals in danger of extinction also live in this place.", "vocab": [{"ko": "멸종", "en": "extinction"}, {"ko": "위기", "en": "crisis; danger"}, {"ko": "처하다", "en": "to be in (a situation)"}, {"ko": "이곳", "en": "this place"}], "analysis": [{"type": "grammar", "label": "~에 처하다", "exp": "Postpositional phrase meaning ''to be in (a state/condition).'' Marks the condition or situation. 처한 = in the state of.", "example_in_sentence": "위기에 처한"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect marker. Indicates an ongoing or continuous action. 살다 → 살고 있다.", "example_in_sentence": "살고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "전 세계 사람들이 DMZ의 생태계에 관심을 보이고 있어요.", "translation": "People around the world are showing interest in the DMZ''s ecosystem.", "vocab": [{"ko": "전 세계", "en": "the whole world"}, {"ko": "생태계", "en": "ecosystem"}, {"ko": "관심", "en": "interest"}, {"ko": "보이다", "en": "to show"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "관심을 보이다", "exp": "Verb phrase meaning ''to show interest.'' Common collocation expressing the act of demonstrating or displaying interest.", "example_in_sentence": "관심을 보이고"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~고 있다", "exp": "Progressive aspect. Indicates ongoing or continuous action. 보이다 → 보이고 있다.", "example_in_sentence": "보이고 있어요"}]}, {"text": "분단의 아픔이 있는 곳이지만 자연에게는 안전한 집이 되었어요.", "translation": "Although it is a place with the pain of division, it has become a safe home for nature.", "vocab": [{"ko": "분단", "en": "division"}, {"ko": "아픔", "en": "pain; sorrow"}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist"}, {"ko": "안전하다", "en": "to be safe"}], "analysis": [{"type": "expression", "label": "~(이)지만 (although it is)", "exp": "contrast after a noun. 곳이다 → 곳이지만 = \"it is a place (of pain), but\".", "example_in_sentence": "곳이지만"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~에게는", "exp": "Recipient/beneficiary marker with topical emphasis. ~에게 marks the recipient; ~는 adds topical emphasis. Shows who/what benefits from the statement.", "example_in_sentence": "자연에게는"}, {"type": "grammar", "label": "~이/가 되다 (become)", "exp": "change of state. 안전한 집이 되었어요 = \"became a safe home\".", "example_in_sentence": "집이 되었어요"}]}], "version": "s6"}', vocab = '[{"ko": "비무장지대", "en": "demilitarized zone", "note": ""}, {"ko": "만들어지다", "en": "to be made; created", "note": ""}, {"ko": "년", "en": "year", "note": ""}, {"ko": "북한", "en": "North Korea", "note": ""}, {"ko": "남한", "en": "South Korea", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사이", "en": "between", "note": ""}, {"ko": "길이", "en": "length", "note": ""}, {"ko": "원래", "en": "originally; originally intended", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전쟁", "en": "war", "note": ""}, {"ko": "막다", "en": "to block; to prevent", "note": ""}, {"ko": "곳", "en": "place", "note": ""}, {"ko": "하지만", "en": "however; but", "note": ""}, {"ko": "지금", "en": "now", "note": ""}, {"ko": "동물", "en": "animal", "note": ""}, {"ko": "식물", "en": "plant", "note": ""}, {"ko": "사람", "en": "person", "note": ""}, {"ko": "살다", "en": "to live", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보호되다", "en": "to be protected", "note": ""}, {"ko": "멸종", "en": "extinction", "note": ""}, {"ko": "위기", "en": "crisis; danger", "note": ""}, {"ko": "처하다", "en": "to be in (a situation)", "note": ""}, {"ko": "이곳", "en": "this place", "note": ""}, {"ko": "전 세계", "en": "the whole world", "note": ""}, {"ko": "생태계", "en": "ecosystem", "note": ""}, {"ko": "관심", "en": "interest", "note": ""}, {"ko": "보이다", "en": "to show", "note": ""}, {"ko": "분단", "en": "division", "note": ""}, {"ko": "아픔", "en": "pain; sorrow", "note": ""}, {"ko": "있다", "en": "to exist", "note": ""}, {"ko": "안전하다", "en": "to be safe", "note": ""}